.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/daily-logger/commit/5302378aaa9952c3a63978166adcaed83bf188cc","node_id":"C_kwDORYWfptoAKDUzMDIzNzhhYWE5OTUyYzNhNjM5NzgxNjZhZGNhZWQ4M2JmMTg4Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/daily-logger/commit/1d52eb7fa8dad3c376b2488c10c081974d620de1","sha":"1d52eb7fa8dad3c376b2488c10c081974d620de1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/daily-logger/commits/1d52eb7fa8dad3c376b2488c10c081974d620de1"}],"sha":"5302378aaa9952c3a63978166adcaed83bf188cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/daily-logger/commits/5302378aaa9952c3a63978166adcaed83bf188cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/daily-logger/commits/1d52eb7fa8dad3c376b2488c10c081974d620de1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T21:45:03Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T02:48:36Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix(opm): correct SD1.1 zoom per first /opm lint pass — Council phase restored\n\nThe t0 lint (PR #243 comment) CONTRADICTED the decomposition sentence:\n\n- F1a: the Council phase (per-persona reviewDraft + synthesizeWithCouncil,\n  src/index.ts) was missing from the zoom — the repo''s signature mechanism.\n  Added Council Reviewing (yields Council Critiques) + Synthesizing\n  (consumes critiques, affects Article) in execution order.\n- F1b: Telemetry Collecting is not a sibling step — collectTelemetry runs\n  inside collect-context.ts:521. Re-expressed as Context Collecting\n  invokes Telemetry Collecting.\n- W2: Frontend Rendering yields Rendered Site (was enabling-links-only).\n- W3: Drafting requires (not consumes) Commit Context + Telemetry Digest —\n  code reads them (buildUserPrompt reused at verification); a consumed\n  object cannot be required later.\n- Probe extras: Claim Verifying affects Article (verification-flagged tag\n  + audit comment, src/index.ts); sharper anchor for the draft->accepted\n  change (stampDraft.ts step 3).\n- W1 (SD1.1 intermediates'' ancestor declaration) left as-is: profile\n  ambiguity flagged to the grammar owners, not resolved unilaterally.\n\nTwin re-rendered. 12/13 probes were CONFIRMED; this fix clears the one\nCONTRADICTED so the pilot clock (rm-l2-ojfbot#S31) starts from a model\nthat matches reality.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"789c11145e1eb31bf196b8bc34380d5084b52282","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/daily-logger/git/trees/789c11145e1eb31bf196b8bc34380