= False if ctx.value is None\nelse ctx.value`, collapsing the None straight back before any decision. With\nonly the derivations fixed, the trial SURVIVED the prefilter while the matcher\nstill answered `not_matched` — a trial sitting in the results labelled \"not\neligible\". Fixing one without the other is not a smaller fix, it is an\nincoherent one.\n\nThree gates keep the change to the case it is about. Each is load-bearing and\neach was added after measurement showed the seam firing too wide:\n\n* By NAME (`EXPLICIT_UNKNOWN_FIELDS`). `_provided_fields` holds every key the\n  caller named, and the matcher''s two `bool_restriction` handlers see all 36\n  attributes of that type. `PatientInfoSerializer` emits `vars(instance)`, so a\n  client that reads a record and posts it back names them all — measured without\n  this gate, that round trip moved 11 attributes from `matched` to `unknown`,\n  `meets_crab` among them, turning a trial the patient was excluded from into a\n  candidate. Widening to those is the open half of #502; the gate is what keeps\n  it genuinely deferred rather than shipped by accident.\n* By the TRIAL. Where the trial imposes no requirement the legacy path lands on\n  `matched` and the attribute is irrelevant to it. Without this gate a patient\n  who said \"renal unknown\" dropped from `100/eligible` to `98/potential` on\n  every trial that never asked about renal function.\n* By PROVENANCE, not the value. Twelve other `bool_restriction` attributes\n  already sit at None for any patient who never supplied their inputs, so a bare\n  None cannot mean \"unknown\" here.\n\n#488''s first lesson is carried over: a null yields unknown only where the\nderivation has nothing to go on. One stated positive receptor settles\n`tnbc_status` on its own even with the other two missing — ER+ rules out triple\nnegative whatever they say. \"Unknown\" is spelled two ways in these vocabularies,\n`None` and `''''` (`value_options` renders `''''` as the literal label \"Unknown\"),\nand both count as a missing input.\n\n`metastatic_status` outside breast cancer stays False deliberately: the\nattribute is disease-scoped there, so False is a determination rather than a gap.\n\n`_provided_fields` is captured in `_build_in_memory`, which is NOT\ninline-payload-only — the CTOMOP/PROMOP adapter and four management commands\nreach it too, and there a null is EXACT''s own stored derivation. What keeps them\napart today is `ctomop_adapter` stripping None from the row before calling in;\nnothing in `resolve` enforces it, and the comment there now says so.\n\nMutation-checked, each kill verified: emptying `_provided_fields` fails all five\nnull tests and the matcher test; restoring the terminal False in any derivation\nfails that field''s test; removing the matcher seam fails the end-to-end\ncandidate test; dropping the name gate fails twelve scoping tests; dropping the\ntrial-side gate fails the no-requirement test; dropping the\nstated-positive-receptor branch fails four tests; narrowing either blank check\nback to `is None` fails its blank case.\n\nNot asserted here, because it is identical on the base branch: naming one of the\n`no_*_status` attributes as null already moves it from `matched` to\n`not_matched`, since those default to True. Measured on both branches, twelve\nsuch attributes, same result.\n\nRefs #502, #510\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg65RgOXaobIWmShxVbQxxdrUES+\nprdck9i5CvM2zvHV4AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOZJb6IOkiQtFRp4/0wIneH6tp1RpZw+Udj/DpkOHpwVZOnI/qCogJJUX4OPSspGos\nLdncHyqedzBHZP67BJoQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T08:38:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/c4f4dda409c40795c310273ceff0387ec29978d2","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKGM0ZjRkZGE0MDljNDA3OTVjMzEwMjczY2VmZjAzODdlYzI5OTc4ZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2","sha":"0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2"}],"sha":"c4f4dda409c40795c310273ceff0387ec29978d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/c4f4dda409c40795c310273ceff0387ec29978d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/2d21b046fe118c291274588311c0e1f1055e0f2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T22:38:31Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T22:38:31Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"fix(federation): say what the trials screen is waiting for\n\nThe bridge resolves the patient from PRomop before EXACT can match\nanything, and the loading text described that rather than what the\nvisitor asked for: a page headed Clinical Trials that says \"Loading your\nhealth profile…\" reads as the wrong screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww","tree":{"sha":"2d7f60768f32b25cd15044f06c905a180a0d3c39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/2d7f60768f32b25cd15044f06c905a180a0d3c39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/2d21b046fe118c291274588311c0e1f1055e0f2e","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d7f60768f32b25cd15044f06c905a180a0d3c39\nparent c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c\nauthor vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1789511911 -0700\ncommitter vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1789511911 -0700\n\nfix(federation): say what the trials screen is waiting for\n\nThe bridge resolves the patient from PRomop before EXACT can match\nanything, and the loading text described that rather than what the\nvisitor asked for: a page headed Clinical Trials that says \"Loading your\nhealth profile…\" reads as the wrong screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgWuNq98bBFRbSZySPDwmm79gA+X\nk8rPpPXqcPr67fa6AAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHfIT7Ky9A35pG0U0jnQKB8GTQkDyjszJ05SKhMExSPNfjelOoLP9TcKfWJS6vRZdb\npBHLjWbBeThWd6AlGclgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T22:38:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/2d21b046fe118c291274588311c0e1f1055e0f2e","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDJkMjFiMDQ2ZmUxMThjMjkxMjc0NTg4MzExYzBlMWYxMDU1ZTBmMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c","sha":"c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c"}],"sha":"2d21b046fe118c291274588311c0e1f1055e0f2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/2d21b046fe118c291274588311c0e1f1055e0f2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T17:40:13Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:16:05Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"fix(federation): keep injected CSS out of the host''s utilities layer\n\nOur stylesheet is appended to the host document''s head, so anything it\ncarries competes with the host''s own rules at equal specificity and wins\nby source order — that is how a remote''s bare `.hidden` erased HealthTree\nONE''s header logo. This sheet is scoped under `.exact-root` and ships no\nTailwind layers, so it was not the offender, but the contract is the same\nfor every remote.\n\n`layerRemoteCss` wraps everything we inject in the host''s `mf-remote`\nlayer, which hosts declare between `components` and `utilities`: above\ntheir preflight so our screens still style themselves, below their\nutilities so we cannot restyle their chrome. `@property`, `@keyframes`\nand `@font-face` are hoisted back out — layers do not change how those\nregister, and `@property` inside a layer is not honoured everywhere.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww\n(cherry picked from commit 32ece56ce650040034ffa42c68e575948cc9ae8a)","tree":{"sha":"ad053230b01b2641eb72b20b7773bce79e2cad57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/ad053230b01b2641eb72b20b7773bce79e2cad57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c","verification":{"payload":"tree ad053230b01b2641eb72b20b7773bce79e2cad57\nparent 907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25\nauthor vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1788802813 -0700\ncommitter vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1789506965 -0700\n\nfix(federation): keep injected CSS out of the host''s utilities layer\n\nOur stylesheet is appended to the host document''s head, so anything it\ncarries competes with the host''s own rules at equal specificity and wins\nby source order — that is how a remote''s bare `.hidden` erased HealthTree\nONE''s header logo. This sheet is scoped under `.exact-root` and ships no\nTailwind layers, so it was not the offender, but the contract is the same\nfor every remote.\n\n`layerRemoteCss` wraps everything we inject in the host''s `mf-remote`\nlayer, which hosts declare between `components` and `utilities`: above\ntheir preflight so our screens still style themselves, below their\nutilities so we cannot restyle their chrome. `@property`, `@keyframes`\nand `@font-face` are hoisted back out — layers do not change how those\nregister, and `@property` inside a layer is not honoured everywhere.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww\n(cherry picked from commit 32ece56ce650040034ffa42c68e575948cc9ae8a)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgWuNq98bBFRbSZySPDwmm79gA+X\nk8rPpPXqcPr67fa6AAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPLR5lM5n+Y2Jw6Ohonex2u4cAxb6fRaNXDa5Omwcmvg6R5IVRQb8CC9b0fiz0qfW0\nmTOWFioZUMnXhUHHQ83gc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T21:16:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKGM5ZWU0NWFkZmIxZTc3ZDdhMjdhNzllODhkYThkNzZmMjJlZmYwOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25","sha":"907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25"}],"sha":"c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/c9ee45adfb1e77d7a27a79e88da8d76f22eff08c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:31:41Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:16:05Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"feat(federation): resolve the signed-in patient inside the TrialMatches bridge\n\nTrialMatches needs a patient to match against, and renders \"Pass a patientInfo\npayload or personId\" without one. ht-phr resolves that itself: PRomop''s\n/patient-info/me/, then EXACT''s /normalize-ctomop-row/, then the inline\npatientInfo prop. Every other host would have to reimplement the same two\ncalls, so the bridge now does it, given `ctomopBaseUrl`.\n\nIt has to be the caller''s own token: the server-side person_id resolver is\ndisabled by default (EXACT_ALLOW_PERSON_ID_LOOKUP) because its CTOMOP service\ntoken is not bound to the caller, so honouring an arbitrary person_id would\nleak another patient''s PHI. Fetching \"me\" makes PRomop enforce access.\n\nNormalisation is not optional — the inline path''s in-memory builder does none,\nso receptor statuses and TNM strings would reach the matcher unmapped.\n\nAn explicit patientInfo or personId prop still wins, and hosts that pass no\nctomopBaseUrl keep the previous behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww\n(cherry picked from commit e85e4ad25bcf9153e5de9f0f677e12087f9b389a)","tree":{"sha":"925a8c2c88f56e8aaa2ff16146da8e6b6a3d1298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/925a8c2c88f56e8aaa2ff16146da8e6b6a3d1298"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25","verification":{"payload":"tree 925a8c2c88f56e8aaa2ff16146da8e6b6a3d1298\nparent 109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5\nauthor vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1788751901 -0700\ncommitter vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1789506965 -0700\n\nfeat(federation): resolve the signed-in patient inside the TrialMatches bridge\n\nTrialMatches needs a patient to match against, and renders \"Pass a patientInfo\npayload or personId\" without one. ht-phr resolves that itself: PRomop''s\n/patient-info/me/, then EXACT''s /normalize-ctomop-row/, then the inline\npatientInfo prop. Every other host would have to reimplement the same two\ncalls, so the bridge now does it, given `ctomopBaseUrl`.\n\nIt has to be the caller''s own token: the server-side person_id resolver is\ndisabled by default (EXACT_ALLOW_PERSON_ID_LOOKUP) because its CTOMOP service\ntoken is not bound to the caller, so honouring an arbitrary person_id would\nleak another patient''s PHI. Fetching \"me\" makes PRomop enforce access.\n\nNormalisation is not optional — the inline path''s in-memory builder does none,\nso receptor statuses and TNM strings would reach the matcher unmapped.\n\nAn explicit patientInfo or personId prop still wins, and hosts that pass no\nctomopBaseUrl keep the previous behaviour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww\n(cherry picked from commit e85e4ad25bcf9153e5de9f0f677e12087f9b389a)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgWuNq98bBFRbSZySPDwmm79gA+X\nk8rPpPXqcPr67fa6AAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMYdU7QAjN8IN2W634pYaNFDzTSnx3JpJSqRQhTs+HTCYSmUsOLo6HBfrXcqUBCZnX\nN+9s9r6HX34FVbRFxpfQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T21:16:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDkwN2M0ZmFlYzFiMWE1OWE4YjA3YzQwNDBjZWQxNzIxNDY4NDBiMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5","sha":"109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5"}],"sha":"907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/907c4faec1b1a59a8b07c4040ced172146840b25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T03:21:42Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:16:05Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"feat(federation): expose TrialMatches through a framework-agnostic bridge\n\nAdds ./TrialMatchesBridge alongside the existing ./TrialMatches export, so a\nhost that is not React — HealthTree ONE is SvelteKit — can mount it by handing\nover a DOM node:\n\n    provider().render({ dom, baseUrl, getToken, ... })\n    provider().destroy({ moduleName, dom })\n\nProps are data-only: the host passes baseUrl + getToken rather than a live\nAxiosInstance, so it needs neither axios nor react-query, and EXACT keeps\nownership of how it calls its own API. ./TrialMatches is untouched.\n\nAlso pins react/react-dom to exactly 19.2.6, matching the other remotes. The\nlockfile had drifted to 19.2.7, and Module Federation shares React as a\nsingleton across remotes in one page: whichever loaded first won, and the\nother died with React error #527.\n\nSee ht-phr/docs/mf-bridge-proposal.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww\n(cherry picked from commit 9e02a8ee6cde80890ec770c971dd2468644c2a6e)","tree":{"sha":"8d1c6164621b03ccfaa9f6b1e528de336a1b52f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/8d1c6164621b03ccfaa9f6b1e528de336a1b52f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d1c6164621b03ccfaa9f6b1e528de336a1b52f2\nparent bc92fd51a305336d85a61434b83f1a11cd377e46\nauthor vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1788751302 -0700\ncommitter vtrv101 <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1789506965 -0700\n\nfeat(federation): expose TrialMatches through a framework-agnostic bridge\n\nAdds ./TrialMatchesBridge alongside the existing ./TrialMatches export, so a\nhost that is not React — HealthTree ONE is SvelteKit — can mount it by handing\nover a DOM node:\n\n    provider().render({ dom, baseUrl, getToken, ... })\n    provider().destroy({ moduleName, dom })\n\nProps are data-only: the host passes baseUrl + getToken rather than a live\nAxiosInstance, so it needs neither axios nor react-query, and EXACT keeps\nownership of how it calls its own API. ./TrialMatches is untouched.\n\nAlso pins react/react-dom to exactly 19.2.6, matching the other remotes. The\nlockfile had drifted to 19.2.7, and Module Federation shares React as a\nsingleton across remotes in one page: whichever loaded first won, and the\nother died with React error #527.\n\nSee ht-phr/docs/mf-bridge-proposal.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015dVAjtcAhgRnzmzFpYgWww\n(cherry picked from commit 9e02a8ee6cde80890ec770c971dd2468644c2a6e)\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgWuNq98bBFRbSZySPDwmm79gA+X\nk8rPpPXqcPr67fa6AAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNKh1k0LIXGv8gc3DzNRHS66RDXB0C6T2H8LwczWaavIzqzyqmbx4aZyFqFIIrMo3f\ni+q6YhkTylZXx/+N1FEwg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T21:16:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDEwOWM0ODkxNjZjY2NkM2I5NGUzMTQ0ZGViNjI2YzU2MjBlZGQ5ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/bc92fd51a305336d85a61434b83f1a11cd377e46","sha":"bc92fd51a305336d85a61434b83f1a11cd377e46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/bc92fd51a305336d85a61434b83f1a11cd377e46"}],"sha":"109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/109c489166cccd3b94e3144deb626c5620edd9e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:12:56Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:12:56Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"message":"fix(patient): renal adequacy was decided before the eGFR it reads (#510)\n\n`normalize()` copies `renal_adequacy_status` off the attributes object and\nderives `estimated_glomerular_filtration_rate` one line BELOW that. The status\nwas decided against a field that was still empty, so for every patient whose\neGFR is calculated rather than stated the derivation took its \"inputs missing\"\nbranch and answered False.\n\nThat is not one unmet criterion among many: `match_score_and_status()`\nshort-circuits the trial to `not_eligible` and the SQL prefilter drops it.\nMeasured against `dev`: a patient with a derived eGFR of 129.93 and a\ncreatinine clearance of 110 — both far above the threshold — was published\n`False` and removed from trials, indistinguishably from one at half the\nthreshold.\n\n`renal_adequacy_status` now computes the value it needs (`_screening_egfr`)\ninstead of reading whatever `normalize` has filled in so far. Reordering the two\nlines was the first attempt and it introduced three defects of its own, because\nmoving the read past the derivation changes which value every OTHER case screens\non. Deciding at the point of use cannot come apart that way.\n\nWhere the record states an eGFR and the labs imply a different one, the screen\ntakes the worse of the two. Disagreement means one of them is stale, and on a\nprefilter the optimistic reading is the one that offers a trial the protocol\nexcludes. It also settles a contradiction `dev` ships: a caller echoing an old\nderived eGFR back alongside fresh creatinine was published with the\nRECALCULATED 21.94 in the field and `renal_adequacy_status: True` beside it.\n\nFour more defects, all measured on `dev`, all reachable from this screen:\n\n* Truthiness. `if egfr and egfr < 60` skipped the check for ZERO — the worst\n  value either measure can carry — and with the other measure adequate fell\n  through to True. Both halves were already live.\n* `_coerce_numerics` short-circuited on `''''`, leaving a `str` in a numeric\n  column. `creatinine_clearance_rate: \"\"` and `hemoglobin_level: \"\"` each raise\n  TypeError from inside request resolution on `dev` — the search fails and every\n  trial is hidden.\n* `int(\"40.5\")` raises and the reading was discarded as None, so a stated\n  measurement was thrown away and the derived value screened in its place.\n* `float(\"inf\")` parses where `int(\"inf\")` refused, so the new fallback let\n  infinity into a clinical column, where it clears every ceiling criterion\n  outright and reads as adequate renal function. Rejected as non-finite in the\n  same place, along with NaN.\n* A list, dict or bool in a numeric column reaches the comparisons untouched —\n  `_coerce_numerics` only inspects strings. The truthiness checks absorbed the\n  falsy ones by accident, so replacing them with `is not None` would have turned\n  that into a raise. `_as_reading` closes it, along with NaN, which survives as\n  a valid `Decimal` and compares False against everything.\n\nThe coercion fallback stores `float`, NOT `int(float(...))`. Truncating would\nmake the quoted and unquoted forms of the same number mean different things\nacross all 31 IntegerField columns, several of which are physiologically\nfractional: `\"990.9\"`/`\"9.95\"` for the free light chain pair floors to 990/9, a\nratio of 110 against a true 99.59, which trips `meets_slim` and republishes a\nSMOLDERING patient as active myeloma. Floor is also biased on every ceiling\ncriterion — `\"2.9\"` against `ecog_performance_status_max=2` becomes a match.\nNothing enforces the column type here: `PatientInfo` is a plain object and\n`normalize` already writes a float 129.93 into that same \"IntegerField\".\n\nWhat this does to the PUBLISHED field, stated precisely because an earlier\nrevision of this message got it wrong: the min() rule leaves it alone, but the\ncoercion half moves it wherever a reading that used to be discarded now reaches\nthe derivation — `patient_age: \"64.9\"` published no eGFR on `dev` and publishes\n98.83 here. That is the intended consequence of not throwing away a stated\nvalue, and `..._min/max` criteria compare against it.\n\nMutation-checked, every kill verified individually: dropping the derivation\nfails the derived-eGFR test and the queryset trace snapshot; `min` -> `max`\nfails three tests; restoring either truthiness check fails the two zero tests;\nrestoring the `''''` short-circuit fails the empty-reading tests; restoring\ntruncation fails both decimal tests; removing either `_as_reading` guard or the\nNaN exclusion fails their own tests.\n\nThree tests deliberately do not bite and say so in their docstrings.\n\nFixes #510\nRefs #502, #509","tree":{"sha":"1d545c3b92493c4b3241b5d149b23ded18f1668b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/1d545c3b92493c4b3241b5d149b23ded18f1668b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d545c3b92493c4b3241b5d149b23ded18f1668b\nparent 6e93128c220780578ddf85a691612be4c980d89b\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1789506776 +0300\ncommitter LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1789506776 +0300\n\nfix(patient): renal adequacy was decided before the eGFR it reads (#510)\n\n`normalize()` copies `renal_adequacy_status` off the attributes object and\nderives `estimated_glomerular_filtration_rate` one line BELOW that. The status\nwas decided against a field that was still empty, so for every patient whose\neGFR is calculated rather than stated the derivation took its \"inputs missing\"\nbranch and answered False.\n\nThat is not one unmet criterion among many: `match_score_and_status()`\nshort-circuits the trial to `not_eligible` and the SQL prefilter drops it.\nMeasured against `dev`: a patient with a derived eGFR of 129.93 and a\ncreatinine clearance of 110 — both far above the threshold — was published\n`False` and removed from trials, indistinguishably from one at half the\nthreshold.\n\n`renal_adequacy_status` now computes the value it needs (`_screening_egfr`)\ninstead of reading whatever `normalize` has filled in so far. Reordering the two\nlines was the first attempt and it introduced three defects of its own, because\nmoving the read past the derivation changes which value every OTHER case screens\non. Deciding at the point of use cannot come apart that way.\n\nWhere the record states an eGFR and the labs imply a different one, the screen\ntakes the worse of the two. Disagreement means one of them is stale, and on a\nprefilter the optimistic reading is the one that offers a trial the protocol\nexcludes. It also settles a contradiction `dev` ships: a caller echoing an old\nderived eGFR back alongside fresh creatinine was published with the\nRECALCULATED 21.94 in the field and `renal_adequacy_status: True` beside it.\n\nFour more defects, all measured on `dev`, all reachable from this screen:\n\n* Truthiness. `if egfr and egfr < 60` skipped the check for ZERO — the worst\n  value either measure can carry — and with the other measure adequate fell\n  through to True. Both halves were already live.\n* `_coerce_numerics` short-circuited on `''''`, leaving a `str` in a numeric\n  column. `creatinine_clearance_rate: \"\"` and `hemoglobin_level: \"\"` each raise\n  TypeError from inside request resolution on `dev` — the search fails and every\n  trial is hidden.\n* `int(\"40.5\")` raises and the reading was discarded as None, so a stated\n  measurement was thrown away and the derived value screened in its place.\n* `float(\"inf\")` parses where `int(\"inf\")` refused, so the new fallback let\n  infinity into a clinical column, where it clears every ceiling criterion\n  outright and reads as adequate renal function. Rejected as non-finite in the\n  same place, along with NaN.\n* A list, dict or bool in a numeric column reaches the comparisons untouched —\n  `_coerce_numerics` only inspects strings. The truthiness checks absorbed the\n  falsy ones by accident, so replacing them with `is not None` would have turned\n  that into a raise. `_as_reading` closes it, along with NaN, which survives as\n  a valid `Decimal` and compares False against everything.\n\nThe coercion fallback stores `float`, NOT `int(float(...))`. Truncating would\nmake the quoted and unquoted forms of the same number mean different things\nacross all 31 IntegerField columns, several of which are physiologically\nfractional: `\"990.9\"`/`\"9.95\"` for the free light chain pair floors to 990/9, a\nratio of 110 against a true 99.59, which trips `meets_slim` and republishes a\nSMOLDERING patient as active myeloma. Floor is also biased on every ceiling\ncriterion — `\"2.9\"` against `ecog_performance_status_max=2` becomes a match.\nNothing enforces the column type here: `PatientInfo` is a plain object and\n`normalize` already writes a float 129.93 into that same \"IntegerField\".\n\nWhat this does to the PUBLISHED field, stated precisely because an earlier\nrevision of this message got it wrong: the min() rule leaves it alone, but the\ncoercion half moves it wherever a reading that used to be discarded now reaches\nthe derivation — `patient_age: \"64.9\"` published no eGFR on `dev` and publishes\n98.83 here. That is the intended consequence of not throwing away a stated\nvalue, and `..._min/max` criteria compare against it.\n\nMutation-checked, every kill verified individually: dropping the derivation\nfails the derived-eGFR test and the queryset trace snapshot; `min` -> `max`\nfails three tests; restoring either truthiness check fails the two zero tests;\nrestoring the `''''` short-circuit fails the empty-reading tests; restoring\ntruncation fails both decimal tests; removing either `_as_reading` guard or the\nNaN exclusion fails their own tests.\n\nThree tests deliberately do not bite and say so in their docstrings.\n\nFixes #510\nRefs #502, #509\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg65RgOXaobIWmShxVbQxxdrUES+\nprdck9i5CvM2zvHV4AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIiGGUQvfObsrCPIQw8OOjkfkY3PCu0D20Y73eLgM/qltwHFDqtQYsPiFlADctgS35\ny+RM7KRPfAXa/IpifY0g0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T21:15:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDA5NzBiMjU3Yjc3OTZlOGQwNWRhY2VhYzQ3NmM4NGZmODM4NjljYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/6e93128c220780578ddf85a691612be4c980d89b","sha":"6e93128c220780578ddf85a691612be4c980d89b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/6e93128c220780578ddf85a691612be4c980d89b"}],"sha":"0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/0970b257b7796e8d05daceac476c84ff83869cb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://