act/commit/6e93128c220780578ddf85a691612be4c980d89b","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDZlOTMxMjhjMjIwNzgwNTc4ZGRmODVhNjkxNjEyYmU0Yzk4MGQ4OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/e568ccbf46e1f57f86566efddb5abc807ae568b4","sha":"e568ccbf46e1f57f86566efddb5abc807ae568b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/e568ccbf46e1f57f86566efddb5abc807ae568b4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4","sha":"335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4"}],"sha":"6e93128c220780578ddf85a691612be4c980d89b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/6e93128c220780578ddf85a691612be4c980d89b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:26:43Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T18:51:32Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"message":"perf(search): count a distinct trial scope over keys, not rows (#492)\n\nEvery country-filtered search pays for deduplicating whole trial rows, and the\nfrontend sends `country` on every request.\n\n`by_location` joins LocationTrial and restores one row per trial with\n`.distinct()`, so Django renders `.count()` as\n\n    SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT DISTINCT <~150 wide columns>\n                          FROM trials_trial JOIN trials_locationtrial …) sub\n\nThe paginator does that for EVERY paginated response, and `/trials/count/` —\nthe endpoint whose whole job is the count — does it again.\n\nMeasured twice, independently, on a 3,114-trial corpus with 43,021\nlocationtrial rows. Same answer, 2,037 trials, every time:\n\n    through Django''s paginator, country scope     5.1s / 7.7s\n    worst real view shape (sort=distance + geo)      22.9s\n    /trials/count/                                    7.1s\n    counted over primary keys                    0.012s-0.035s\n\nThe ids are already distinct, so counting them needs none of that width.\n`_base_manager` because this counts ids the scope has already decided —\nverified to carry no default filter here — and `using(scope.db)` so a\nsplit-database deployment stays on the alias the scope was built for.\n\nNo degradation at scale: 3,114 keys 0.002s, 18,462 keys 0.005s.\n\nHonest limit: this removes ~5s of an ~8s request. The page query itself is\nstill slow (2.6s for the first page, 5.6s at offset 2000), so the endpoint is\nnot fast afterwards — it is merely no longer counting the corpus twice.\n\n## What it refuses to touch\n\n* A non-distinct scope — already one aggregate; re-deriving it would add a\n  subquery for nothing. Verified byte-identical SQL to Django''s across five\n  shapes.\n* A `.values()` / `.values_list()` scope — its page yields distinct VALUE\n  TUPLES while this counts distinct PKs, and they differ: measured 1 against 2\n  on `.values(''register'').distinct()`. Unreachable today, but this paginator\n  serves three viewsets and nothing else says \"model querysets only\".\n* Anything without a `.distinct()`, via `getattr` — a `RawQuery` has no such\n  attribute and would raise rather than fall through.\n\n## The tests assert SHAPE and WIRING, not time\n\nTiming assertions are flaky, and correctness alone cannot separate the two\nforms: both return 2,037. The discriminator is the SQL — Django''s count names\n`\"trials_trial\".\"brief_title\"`, ours does not. Named one wide column rather\nthan counting columns, so a Django version change or a new model field does\nnot move it.\n\nThe fixture puts one trial at two sites, so a scope that lost its `.distinct()`\nwould double-count and be caught as well.\n\nThe first version of this commit tested the CLASS and not the one line that\ninstalls it: deleting `django_paginator_class = CountDistinctByKey` left all\n1206 tests green while the fix did nothing in production. Raised by review;\nthat mutation is now guarded, and so is the `count` action, which no paginator\ntest can reach because it does not paginate.\n\nMutation-checked, each independently:\n\n    remove `django_paginator_class`   -> 1 failure, the wiring test\n    disable the technique             -> 2, the shape and count-endpoint tests\n    remove the `values()` guard       -> 1, the values test\n\n## Also from that review\n\nThe earlier draft cited 48.911s for the annotated count. An independent\nreviewer''s worst on that shape was 22.9s, so the figure is dropped rather than\nquoted — it sat in a source docstring, where a commit-message caveat about\ncache state would not have travelled with it.\n\n1209 passed, 8 skipped (1203 before these six tests).","tree":{"sha":"ea3a569d3b72dd6ac7fd7688e159df013d0eed8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/ea3a569d3b72dd6ac7fd7688e159df013d0eed8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4","verification":{"payload":"tree ea3a569d3b72dd6ac7fd7688e159df013d0eed8c\nparent e568ccbf46e1f57f86566efddb5abc807ae568b4\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1789496803 +0300\ncommitter LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1789498292 +0300\n\nperf(search): count a distinct trial scope over keys, not rows (#492)\n\nEvery country-filtered search pays for deduplicating whole trial rows, and the\nfrontend sends `country` on every request.\n\n`by_location` joins LocationTrial and restores one row per trial with\n`.distinct()`, so Django renders `.count()` as\n\n    SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT DISTINCT <~150 wide columns>\n                          FROM trials_trial JOIN trials_locationtrial …) sub\n\nThe paginator does that for EVERY paginated response, and `/trials/count/` —\nthe endpoint whose whole job is the count — does it again.\n\nMeasured twice, independently, on a 3,114-trial corpus with 43,021\nlocationtrial rows. Same answer, 2,037 trials, every time:\n\n    through Django''s paginator, country scope     5.1s / 7.7s\n    worst real view shape (sort=distance + geo)      22.9s\n    /trials/count/                                    7.1s\n    counted over primary keys                    0.012s-0.035s\n\nThe ids are already distinct, so counting them needs none of that width.\n`_base_manager` because this counts ids the scope has already decided —\nverified to carry no default filter here — and `using(scope.db)` so a\nsplit-database deployment stays on the alias the scope was built for.\n\nNo degradation at scale: 3,114 keys 0.002s, 18,462 keys 0.005s.\n\nHonest limit: this removes ~5s of an ~8s request. The page query itself is\nstill slow (2.6s for the first page, 5.6s at offset 2000), so the endpoint is\nnot fast afterwards — it is merely no longer counting the corpus twice.\n\n## What it refuses to touch\n\n* A non-distinct scope — already one aggregate; re-deriving it would add a\n  subquery for nothing. Verified byte-identical SQL to Django''s across five\n  shapes.\n* A `.values()` / `.values_list()` scope — its page yields distinct VALUE\n  TUPLES while this counts distinct PKs, and they differ: measured 1 against 2\n  on `.values(''register'').distinct()`. Unreachable today, but this paginator\n  serves three viewsets and nothing else says \"model querysets only\".\n* Anything without a `.distinct()`, via `getattr` — a `RawQuery` has no such\n  attribute and would raise rather than fall through.\n\n## The tests assert SHAPE and WIRING, not time\n\nTiming assertions are flaky, and correctness alone cannot separate the two\nforms: both return 2,037. The discriminator is the SQL — Django''s count names\n`\"trials_trial\".\"brief_title\"`, ours does not. Named one wide column rather\nthan counting columns, so a Django version change or a new model field does\nnot move it.\n\nThe fixture puts one trial at two sites, so a scope that lost its `.distinct()`\nwould double-count and be caught as well.\n\nThe first version of this commit tested the CLASS and not the one line that\ninstalls it: deleting `django_paginator_class = CountDistinctByKey` left all\n1206 tests green while the fix did nothing in production. Raised by review;\nthat mutation is now guarded, and so is the `count` action, which no paginator\ntest can reach because it does not paginate.\n\nMutation-checked, each independently:\n\n    remove `django_paginator_class`   -> 1 failure, the wiring test\n    disable the technique             -> 2, the shape and count-endpoint tests\n    remove the `values()` guard       -> 1, the values test\n\n## Also from that review\n\nThe earlier draft cited 48.911s for the annotated count. An independent\nreviewer''s worst on that shape was 22.9s, so the figure is dropped rather than\nquoted — it sat in a source docstring, where a commit-message caveat about\ncache state would not have travelled with it.\n\n1209 passed, 8 skipped (1203 before these six tests).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg65RgOXaobIWmShxVbQxxdrUES+\nprdck9i5CvM2zvHV4AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHJGBvdzy7NUb7zl7ByTvzNUaDaqkOIfkBnSxE1I1IH9W2uxtn8JZqjMqA5W3MFhJ+\nWRzA5NtP2g4plL+Pcv/gU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T18:54:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDMzNWRiYWJmZjJjZTBkODhkYzc5MjJiOTc0YTg1YjM1YzQ1Mzg1ZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/e568ccbf46e1f57f86566efddb5abc807ae568b4","sha":"e568ccbf46e1f57f86566efddb5abc807ae568b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/e568ccbf46e1f57f86566efddb5abc807ae568b4"}],"sha":"335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/335dbabff2ce0d88dc7922b974a85b35c45385f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/bbd1df6732e81fbb358273ffb12b1e1a7fb7dd02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:27:19Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:27:19Z","email":"69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LeoMo42"},"message":"fix(security): an empty password is a value, and it was losing to the environment\n\nA DSN can say \"this connection has no password\" by carrying an empty one\n-- `postgresql://u:@h/db`, `password=''''`. Both halves dropped it as falsy\nand set nothing, and both hand psql an environment built on the inherited\none. So an ambient PGPASSWORD -- another database''s, exported by whoever\nran the command, or left over in a shell -- took its place, and libpq sent\na credential the DSN had explicitly declined to give it.\n\nThe distinction is between a password field that is absent and one that is\nempty: absent means the environment and .pgpass apply, which is libpq''s\nown precedence and must keep working; empty means empty. Python now tests\n`is not None` rather than truthiness, and bash exports inside the branch it\nalready knows the userinfo carried a `:`.\n\nMeasured with PGPASSWORD=ANOTHER-DATABASES-SECRET in the environment:\nbefore, `postgresql://u:@h/db` connected with that secret; after, with the\nempty password the DSN asked for. A DSN that names no password still\ninherits it, which is the case that must not change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkXu9aFDRDrMdbT3XJUdnc","tree":{"sha":"0f109fa54381079424e41c84d58bfa9f5436aa70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/0f109fa54381079424e41c84d58bfa9f5436aa70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/bbd1df6732e81fbb358273ffb12b1e1a7fb7dd02","verification":{"payload":"tree 0f109fa54381079424e41c84d58bfa9f5436aa70\nparent a8f8525f1bc5cc4fb74b516b08922e668152d1c0\nauthor LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1789489639 +0300\ncommitter LeoMo42 <69346755+LeoMo42@users.noreply.github.com> 1789489639 +0300\n\nfix(security): an empty password is a value, and it was losing to the environment\n\nA DSN can say \"this connection has no password\" by carrying an empty one\n-- `postgresql://u:@h/db`, `password=''''`. Both halves dropped it as falsy\nand set nothing, and both hand psql an environment built on the inherited\none. So an ambient PGPASSWORD -- another database''s, exported by whoever\nran the command, or left over in a shell -- took its place, and libpq sent\na credential the DSN had explicitly declined to give it.\n\nThe distinction is between a password field that is absent and one that is\nempty: absent means the environment and .pgpass apply, which is libpq''s\nown precedence and must keep working; empty means empty. Python now tests\n`is not None` rather than truthiness, and bash exports inside the branch it\nalready knows the userinfo carried a `:`.\n\nMeasured with PGPASSWORD=ANOTHER-DATABASES-SECRET in the environment:\nbefore, `postgresql://u:@h/db` connected with that secret; after, with the\nempty password the DSN asked for. A DSN that names no password still\ninherits it, which is the case that must not change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkXu9aFDRDrMdbT3XJUdnc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg65RgOXaobIWmShxVbQxxdrUES+\nprdck9i5CvM2zvHV4AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBtO4j+1CnYcRvp0Vq2unHtM/4Vxb00SialRHixHGN1wXLE+6l8l1RglU858VVf1kE\nzF2LrE0wWKn/jLyhIERwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T19:09:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69346755?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeoMo42","id":69346755,"login":"LeoMo42","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzQ2NzU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeoMo42","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/bbd1df6732e81fbb358273ffb12b1e1a7fb7dd02","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKGJiZDFkZjY3MzJlODFmYmIzNTgyNzNmZmIxMmIxZTFhN2ZiN2RkMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/co