com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/0647513f7809eaa2f3ce9ad6538f910cf3e2ed19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/a2b88f6404541530a67474062de9d6094a6dc115/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:17:40Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:33:19Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"fix(search): counts over a joined scope 500 the search endpoint (#490)\n\n`GET /trials/search/` returns 500 when a patient payload meets a filter that\nnarrows through a join. Pre-emptive on this branch — see \"How reachable\" — and\na live defect the moment #489 lands.\n\n`BlankAttributeRecordsCount` builds its aggregations from CASE-WHEN strings\nthat name columns UNQUALIFIED (`age_low_limit`, not\n`trials_trial.age_low_limit`). That resolves while the aggregate runs against\nthe table. It stops resolving the moment the scope carries a `.distinct()`:\nDjango computes `aggregate()` over a DERIVED TABLE whose select list does not\ncarry those columns, and Postgres answers\n\n    column \"age_low_limit\" does not exist\n\n`_trials_counts` runs under the `search` action, and two paths reach it with\nsuch a scope:\n\n* `by_location` — joins LocationTrial, ends in `.distinct()`\n* `with_distance_optimized` — same, and needs NO country, only a patient with\n  a `geo_point`\n\n## How reachable, precisely\n\nThe first version of this message said \"live in production\" and \"`dev` as it\nstands\". That was wrong, and the review that caught it measured why: on this\nbranch NO shipped caller reaches the failing combination. It needs all three of\n`action == ''search''`, a non-None `patient_info`, and a distinct scope, and:\n\n* `search` is GET-only here; `POST /trials/search/` is 405. The `match` and\n  `match_detail` aliases bind to `list`/`retrieve`, and `list` never calls\n  `_trials_counts`.\n* the shipped frontend uses `POST /trials/match/`, which is one of those.\n* the only ways to attach a patient are an inline body (needing GET-with-body,\n  which this repo''s own docstring says fetch/axios cannot send) or\n  `?person_id=`, which is 403-gated outside local/DEBUG.\n\nWhat IS exposed: a server-to-server integrator following `API_SURFACE.md:223`,\nwhich tells them to put `patientInfo` in the body of `GET /trials/search/`.\nAnd #489 adds `POST /trials/search/match/`, at which point the ordinary\nbrowser path reaches it on every search with a country.\n\nVerified over real HTTP against a live server, not just the test client:\n`GET /trials/search/` + JSON body → 200; the same with `?country=<title>` or\n`?distance=100` → 500; without the body → 200; `POST /trials/search/` → 405.\n\n## The fix\n\n`pk__in` re-derives the same trials as a plain, un-joined queryset, so the\naggregate runs against the table again. It covers the CLASS — any distinct,\njoined or sliced scope — rather than the one filter that exposed it.\n\nQualifying the columns does NOT work: the outer query''s FROM holds only the\nderived table, so `trials_trial.age_low_limit` fails with\n`missing FROM-clause entry`. Verified, not assumed.\n\n## Cost\n\nNot free, and the first version of this message claimed it was. Measured over\n15 warm iterations against the seeded corpora:\n\n    18,462 trials   26.2ms -> 50.3ms   (+24ms, +92%)\n     3,114 trials   10.7ms -> 13.5ms   (+2.8ms, +26%)\n\nSo the common case — every search WITHOUT a country or distance — pays roughly\ndouble for a fix it does not need, at ~50ms absolute. `EXPLAIN` confirms a\nsemi-join (Hash Join, HashAggregate on the id), not a correlated re-execution.\nAcceptable; worth knowing.\n\n## Why 1092 green tests never saw it\n\nNothing went through HTTP with a narrowing filter. The queryset tests all stop\nshort of the endpoint, and no view test combined a patient payload with a\nfilter that joins.\n\nBoth new tests were checked by mutation against `origin/dev`, not against a\nlocal checkout — a plain `git checkout <path>` after the fix is committed\nrestores the FIXED file and the measurement silently proves nothing:\n\n* the service test fails with the ProgrammingError\n* all three endpoint tests fail, including the two that need no country\n\n## Not fixed here\n\n`by_location`''s DISTINCT over ~150 wide columns makes the paginator''s\n`.count()` take ~10s for a country-filtered search, and THAT one the shipped\nfrontend does reach. Filed separately. It is the same trick one layer up:\n`Trial.objects.filter(pk__in=scope.values(''pk'')).count()` answers in 8ms.\n\n1092 passed, 6 skipped.","tree":{"sha":"381be2bed6bc8189f08bd80189ceae25582b8afe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/381be2bed6bc8189f08bd80189ceae25582b8afe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/a2b88f6404541530a67474062de9d6094a6dc115","verification":{"payload":"tree 381be2bed6bc8189f08bd80189ceae25582b8afe\nparent 41d27e83e23cf0bc18b01b904