PI_SURFACE.md:223`,\nwhich tells them to put `patientInfo` in the body of `GET /trials/search/`.\nAnd #489 adds `POST /trials/search/match/`, at which point the ordinary\nbrowser path reaches it on every search with a country.\n\nVerified over real HTTP against a live server, not just the test client:\n`GET /trials/search/` + JSON body → 200; the same with `?country=<title>` or\n`?distance=100` → 500; without the body → 200; `POST /trials/search/` → 405.\n\n## The fix\n\n`pk__in` re-derives the same trials as a plain, un-joined queryset, so the\naggregate runs against the table again. It covers the CLASS — any distinct,\njoined or sliced scope — rather than the one filter that exposed it.\n\nQualifying the columns does NOT work: the outer query''s FROM holds only the\nderived table, so `trials_trial.age_low_limit` fails with\n`missing FROM-clause entry`. Verified, not assumed.\n\n## Cost\n\nNot free, and the first version of this message claimed it was. Measured over\n15 warm iterations against the seeded corpora:\n\n    18,462 trials   26.2ms -> 50.3ms   (+24ms, +92%)\n     3,114 trials   10.7ms -> 13.5ms   (+2.8ms, +26%)\n\nSo the common case — every search WITHOUT a country or distance — pays roughly\ndouble for a fix it does not need, at ~50ms absolute. `EXPLAIN` confirms a\nsemi-join (Hash Join, HashAggregate on the id), not a correlated re-execution.\nAcceptable; worth knowing.\n\n## Why 1092 green tests never saw it\n\nNothing went through HTTP with a narrowing filter. The queryset tests all stop\nshort of the endpoint, and no view test combined a patient payload with a\nfilter that joins.\n\nBoth new tests were checked by mutation against `origin/dev`, not against a\nlocal checkout — a plain `git checkout <path>` after the fix is committed\nrestores the FIXED file and the measurement silently proves nothing:\n\n* the service test fails with the ProgrammingError\n* all three endpoint tests fail, including the two that need no country\n\n## Not fixed here\n\n`by_location`''s DISTINCT over ~150 wide columns makes the paginator''s\n`.count()` take ~10s for a country-filtered search, and THAT one the shipped\nfrontend does reach. Filed separately. It is the same trick one layer up:\n`Trial.objects.filter(pk__in=scope.values(''pk'')).count()` answers in 8ms.\n\n1092 passed, 6 skipped.\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg65RgOXaobIWmShxVbQxxdrUES+\nprdck9i5CvM2zvHV4AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQM8Zw3BuZM+UhhvAQQzaTXWqt+M0R6bW25Vz2uonRk0TEqdlOsqZwOHETLI4dcCQ2v\nIuUMS1GHcg9XsHIN18hQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/a2b88f6404541530a67474062de9d6094a6dc115","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKGEyYjg4ZjY0MDQ1NDE1MzBhNjc0NzQwNjJkZTlkNjA5NGE2ZGMxMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/41d27e83e23cf0bc18b01b90487f231f2a50a39e"