m/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b","sha":"005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b"}],"sha":"0d837a36b99a517ddcd6c5c473d5aa109a4e5317","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/0d837a36b99a517ddcd6c5c473d5aa109a4e5317"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/25fbe0441efde4fbf172ab0aa9c2e84502a26cb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:14:41Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:23:20Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"ci: stop caching an installed site-packages across runner images\n\nForward-port of the fix on `cb-like-trials` (PR #452). Preventive here, and\nthe reason differs from the feature branches — worth stating, because the\nweaker reason is the one that looks obvious.\n\n`main` is not broken today. The failure there needed two things: caching\nthe interpreter''s whole `site-packages`, and downgrading pip INSIDE that\ncached directory. This branch does the first but not the second, so the\nentry has matched the image so far.\n\nThe hazard that already came close on `main` is the other one: `test` has\nNO install step. It restores `build`''s installed tree and runs on it, so\nanything that keeps the entry from being there leaves the job with no\ndependencies at all. Run 32647557900 (2026-08-23) logged, in `build`:\n\n    Failed to save: Unable to reserve cache with key\n    Linux-/opt/hostedtoolcache/Python/3.12.14/x64-...-v1,\n    another job may be creating this cache.\n\nIts three `test` jobs got a hit anyway — but only because a push 38 seconds\nearlier (run 32647521764) had written that key. Alone, they would have died\nat `makemigrations` with a bare ModuleNotFoundError, on `main`.\n\nThe second hazard is the one that broke the feature branches:\n`actions/cache` untars OVER an existing tree rather than replacing it, so a\nrestored entry and the image are unioned, not swapped. There the union put\n26.2.1''s `build_env/` package beside 24.0''s `build_env.py`; the package won\nthe import and asked the overwritten `cli/spinners.py` for a symbol 24.0\nnever had, and every `python -m pip` died. Here it needs pip to change\nunder an unchanged 3.12.x — the key embeds the interpreter''s patch path, so\na new image usually misses rather than unions — which a toolcache rebuild\ncan do.\n\nBoth end the same way: don''t ship one job''s installed tree to another. So\nthe site-packages cache goes, `test` installs its own dependencies, and the\nonly cache left is `~/.cache/pip` — downloads rather than an installed\ntree, validated by pip when it uses them, never untarred over a live\ninterpreter.\n\nUnlike `dev`, there is no pip pin here to remove. `requirements.txt` is the\nsame git blob on this branch, `dev` and `cb-like-trials`, so #452''s green\nCI is direct evidence for this port.\n\nThis branch also still lacks the `sudo rm -f .../azure-cli.list` guard the\nothers carry (0cd7400). That is a separate port and is left alone\ndeliberately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd33125e6a3f8597cfe4f3755b8b49cf2779432a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/bd33125e6a3f8597cfe4f3755b8b49cf2779432a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/25fbe0441efde4fbf172ab0aa9c2e84502a26cb2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/25fbe0441efde4fbf172ab0aa9c2e84502a26cb2","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDI1ZmJlMDQ0MWVmZGU0ZmJmMTcyYWIwYWE5YzJlODQ1MDJhMjZjYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/d3d3cb39bea0fbae2598275e7ab9ceb78fd0a613","sha":"d3d3cb39bea0fbae2598275e7ab9ceb78fd0a613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/d3d3cb39bea0fbae2598275e7ab9ceb78fd0a613"}],"sha":"25fbe0441efde4fbf172ab0aa9c2e84502a26cb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/25fbe0441efde4fbf172ab0aa9c2e84502a26cb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:14:41Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:23:16Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"ci: stop caching a downgraded pip on top of the image''s own\n\nForward-port of the fix on `cb-like-trials` (PR #452). `dev` carries both\nhalves of the bug, so this branch is affected exactly as the feature\nbranches were.\n\n`build` dies inside pip before installing anything:\n\n    ImportError: cannot import name ''open_rich_spinner'' from\n    ''pip._internal.cli.spinners''. Did you mean: ''open_spinner''?\n\nTwo of our own decisions, harmless apart and fatal together: the workflow\ncached the interpreter''s whole `site-packages`, and the install step\ndowngraded pip to 24.0 INSIDE that directory. The saved entry could\ntherefore never agree with the image it was restored onto (26.2.1), and\n`actions/cache` untars OVER a tree rather than replacing it. The union is\nneither version: 24.0''s `cli/spinners.py` lands on top while 26.2.1''s\n`build_env/` package survives beside 24.0''s `build_env.py` and wins the\nimport, then asks the overwritten `spinners.py` for a symbol 24.0 never had.\n\nNo runner-image change is involved. Entries are scoped per\n`refs/pull/N/merge`, so each PR poisons only itself: first run misses,\npasses, saves; the second — a re-run or another push — hits what it just\nwrote and dies. PR #432 is the clean pair, eleven minutes apart on one\nimage:\n\n    06:30  run 34570074256   Cache not found   passed, then saved\n    06:39  run 34570854589   Cache hit         ImportError\n\nBoth halves go. The cache goes because re-keying cannot help — the next\nentry is poisoned like the last — and because keying the runner image in\nwould have been worse than useless: `test` had NO install step, it ran on\n`build`''s site-packages, so a `test` job landing on a different image would\nhave run with nothing installed. Both jobs now install their own\ndependencies; the only cache left is `~/.cache/pip`, which is downloads\nrather than an installed tree.\n\nThe pin goes because its stated reason was never true. `get_runnable_pip`\nwas not removed in 24.1 — it is in `build_env.py` in both 24.0 and 24.1,\nand moved to `utils/misc.py` by 26.2.1 — so the ImportError this branch''s\n`ensurepip` repair was built around (a13f4c7) was this same mixed tree read\nfrom the other side. `requirements.txt` here is byte-identical to the one\non `cb-like-trials`, where CI is green with no pin under the image''s own\n26.2.1, psycopg2''s sdist build isolation included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97252b6e403b9d1b75bc18581a61e8dbcee729b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/97252b6e403b9d1b75bc18581a61e8dbcee729b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDAwNWM3NzQwZTUwZmZkZjljMTI0MzU1YzJiNWM4NGMxYjhjNjdkNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/06758f6ee8b70fd5fa4b83bf3f4dae9a3c76568f","sha":"06758f6ee8b70fd5fa4b83bf3f4dae9a3c76568f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/06758f6ee8b70fd5fa4b83bf3f4dae9a3c76568f"}],"sha":"005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/005c7740e50ffdf9c124355c2b5c84c1b8c67d5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/31a230c80f6cd673c5807b06123f998bf8ac726c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:17:12Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:37:38Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"Merge origin/feat/phr-federation into fix/phr-federation-hardening\n\nThe base moved when #364 landed, and #364 did overlapping work, so this branch\nwent CONFLICTING. Resolved by taking the base wherever both solved the same\nproblem, and re-applying by hand the one thing only this branch has.\n\nTaken from the base:\n\n- alg routing. The base dispatches on a named `_INTROSPECTABLE_ALGS` set with\n  an `isinstance(alg, str)` guard; this branch had a bare `elif alg ==\n  \"HS256\"`. On type safety the two are equivalent — `==` never raises, so a\n  list-valued `alg` was never a problem here; the guard exists because the\n  base''s `in` form needs it. The base wins on being the base, on the named\n  constant, and on admitting HS384/HS512, which are as symmetric as HS256 and\n  equally gated. All three were untested in either direction, so widening or\n  narrowing the set was free; `test_every_allowlisted_alg_routes_to_introspection`\n  now covers them (narrowing the set back to HS256 fails two of its cases).\n- introspection opt-in. This branch stopped auto-deriving the URL; the base\n  added `PHR_ALLOW_INTROSPECTION`, which fails closed on an unset ENVIRONMENT,\n  plus pre-network access/expiry checks and a call budget. Both halves are kept\n  — the URL still does not derive — but the gate is the load-bearing one.\n- the deploy-render comment, which says the same thing and names the test that\n  guards the workflow-name pairing.\n\nKept from this branch — RFC 7662 §2.1. The base posts `json={\"token\": …}`. A\nspec-compliant portal parses the body as a form, finds no `token` parameter,\nand answers \"not active\" for a token that is perfectly good: a rejection that\nlooks like a verdict. Now form-encoded with `token_type_hint`, plus optional\nHTTP Basic from `PHR_INTROSPECT_AUTH`. `partition` keeps a secret containing a\ncolon intact, and a value missing *either* half — `\"id\"`, `\"id:\"`, `\":secret\"`\n— is refused with a warning rather than sent as a half-blank credential, which\nwould read as authenticated in the portal''s log and is not. (Testing only for\na missing colon would have let `\"id:\"` through the guard written to stop it.)\n\nAlso an explicit empty-URL check, placed with the other no-network checks and\nahead of the call budget: it costs nothing, and behind the budget an\nunconfigured deployment would spend its whole allowance on calls that were\nnever going to happen, so the first properly configured call would be refused.\nMoving it back behind the budget fails its test.\n\n`tests/test_phr_provider.py` is dropped rather than repaired. All eleven of its\ntests are covered by `tests/test_phr_auth.py`, which the base added and which\nis far more thorough on the same ground, and three of them failed after the\nmerge because they predate the `exp` requirement and the gate. Two test files\nfor one provider, with different fixtures and one written against superseded\nbehaviour, is a trap rather than coverage. Its only uncovered assertions — the\nwire format — move to `TestIntrospectionRequestShape` beside the introspection\nfixtures. That fixture recorded `kwargs[''json'']`, which after this change would\nrecord `None` for every call and silently stop asserting anything; it now\nrecords the whole call.\n\nDocs the merge would otherwise have left describing removed behaviour:\n`docs/setup.md` still said `PHR_BASE_URL` derives `PHR_INTROSPECT_URL` and\nlisted the latter as `_(derived)_`, which would send an operator to configure\n`PHR_ALLOW_INTROSPECTION` and watch HS256 sign-in 401 with only a debug line to\nshow for it. `.env.example` mentioned neither variable. Three comments still gave\n\"both URLs derive\" as the *reason* the gate exists — including the docstring of\nthe test class whose whole job is to defend the gate''s default — which is how\nsomeone later talks themselves into removing it. And the `PHR_BASE_URL` row''s\n\"unset means portal tokens never verify\" is now true only of the RS256 path.\n\nVerified by mutation, not just by passing: reverting the request block to\n`json=` fails the wire-format tests, restoring \"a colon anywhere\" fails three\ncredential cases, moving the URL check behind the budget fails its test, and\nnarrowing the alg set fails two. Suite 880 passed / 6 skipped against 868 on\nthe base alone — the +12 is exactly the tests added here; `makemigrations\n--check` clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RCfnBjgPjApVRZFHYzCFnV","tree":{"sha":"8d9726d3d3dd9276259a11e45aeac95bace364f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/8d9726d3d3dd9276259a11e45aeac95bace364f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/31a230c80f6cd673c5807b06123f998bf8ac726c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/31a230c80f6cd673c5807b06123f998bf8ac726c","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDMxYTIzMGM4MGY2Y2Q2NzNjNTgwN2IwNjEyM2Y5OThiZjhhYzcyNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1","sha":"8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/2b9f633ae80a296e1022b4ea5630ef3bba262279","sha":"2b9f633ae80a296e1022b4ea5630ef3bba262279","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/2b9f633ae80a296e1022b4ea5630ef3bba262279"}],"sha":"31a230c80f6cd673c5807b06123f998bf8ac726c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/31a230c80f6cd673c5807b06123f998bf8ac726c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/6d9b0135017814ca2885a892ba008931ad3c042a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:50:41Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T12:50:41Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"fix(tests): stop the migrate_trials_db patches deleting settings for good\n\n`@patch(''django.conf.settings.DATABASES'', …, create=True)` does not restore the\nsetting. `create=True` makes mock skip the branch CPython labels \"needed for\nproxy objects like django settings\", so on exit it `delattr`s the attribute off\n`LazySettings` — which Django forwards to the underlying `Settings` — instead of\nputting the original back. `DATABASES` and `TRIALS_DB_MIGRATE` are simply gone\nfor the rest of the session.\n\nBoth settings exist in `exact/settings.py`, so `create=True` was never needed;\nwithout it mock takes the restore path and the settings survive.\n\nInvisible on `dev`, because nothing after this file reads either setting. It\nsurfaces the moment something does: merging the `feat/phr-federation` stack in\nbrings `tests/test_db_compat.py`, whose fixtures read `settings.DATABASES`, and\nthe combination gives 10 failures and 21 errors — all of them\n`AttributeError: ''Settings'' object has no attribute ''DATABASES''`, none of them\nin the code either side changed. `tests/test_db_compat.py` alone passes 52/52\nand the stack branch alone passes 920; only the pair fails.\n\nFull suite on the merge: 1076 passed, 6 skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RCfnBjgPjApVRZFHYzCFnV","tree":{"sha":"42ca9ebdff7509671d179155a95c891b269c0a5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/42ca9ebdff7509671d179155a95c891b269c0a5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/6d9b0135017814ca2885a892ba008931ad3c042a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_eve