2yZaTW\n=uTjH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T15:39:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/2b9f633ae80a296e1022b4ea5630ef3bba262279","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDJiOWY2MzNhZTgwYTI5NmUxMDIyYjRlYTU2MzBlZjNiYmEyNjIyNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","sha":"758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b","sha":"d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b"}],"sha":"2b9f633ae80a296e1022b4ea5630ef3bba262279","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/2b9f633ae80a296e1022b4ea5630ef3bba262279"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:31:56Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:31:56Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"fix(ci): don''t deploy on a fork PR''s `backend` run\n\n`head_branch == ''main''` reads like a branch gate, and is not one. This repo is\npublic and django.yml runs on bare `pull_request:`, so a fork PR produces a\n`backend` run whose `head_branch` is the branch name *in the fork* — `main`, for\nanyone who pushes to their fork''s default branch before opening the PR. That\nrun''s success satisfied both existing clauses, and this job would then execute\nin the base-repo context, holding RENDER_API_KEY, pinning `commitId` to an\nunreviewed fork commit.\n\nLatent in the base branch only because `workflows: [django]` matched nothing and\nthe whole `if:` was dead. Making the trigger fire and pinning the commit are\nwhat turn it into a live path, so it belongs to this branch. Requiring the\nupstream event to be a `push` excludes every PR run, fork or not, and is\nstricter than comparing repositories.\n\nAlso from the same round:\n\n`exact/health.py`''s import guard could not see `import trials.models`. The AST\nwalk records a plain `import x.y` with an empty module, so filtering on the\nmodule alone never matched it — and with no TRIALS_DATABASE_URL in CI the\nbehavioural counterpart skips, leaving that guard as the only live check on \"the\nprobe must not reach the external trials host\". Both import forms are now\ncaught, and both mutations fail the suite.\n\nThe wait step regained a diagnostic the rewrite dropped: an empty verdict, most\nplausibly the program dying on a missing COMMIT_ID, matched no `case` arm and\nproduced 90 blank lines over 30 minutes before \"Timed out\". It also gets\n`set -uo pipefail`, which the other two steps already had.\n\nThe deploy request body is built on its own line now. `set -e` ignores a\nnon-zero exit from a command substitution used as an argument, so a broken\ngenerator would have posted `-d \"\"` — the branch-tip deploy this all exists to\nprevent — rather than failing at the cause.\n\nSmaller test-infrastructure repairs, all from the same review: `_run_scripts`\nasserts it found as many named steps as there are `run:` keys, since it is keyed\non the step name and an unnamed step would otherwise overwrite its predecessor\nand quietly shrink the injection guard''s coverage; the body-escaping test\nlocates its program by `commitId`, the field being built, rather than by\n`json.dumps`, the function building it, so it fails for its actual reason; and\nthe embedded programs run under the system `python3` like the runner''s, not\nunder whatever interpreter runs pytest.\n\nThe compose comment no longer implies it closes the person-id IDOR for local\ndevelopment. docs/setup.md has you copy .env.example, which sets\nENVIRONMENT=local, so a developer who followed the setup has that gate open\nregardless; the flag is still right for the no-.env case, which is what it now\nsays.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"618623a9676f620b4045dc841bf7125f61e1cb73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/618623a9676f620b4045dc841bf7125f61e1cb73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKGQ3NTE0ZDJlZGNmMmFiY2I3MWQ5NWZjYzdiYWJhNjdmYWFkYzg2OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915","sha":"257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915"}],"sha":"d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/d7514d2edcf2abcb71d95fcc7baba67faadc869b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:15:57Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:15:57Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"fix(ci): confirm the deployed commit, don''t just request it\n\nPinning `commitId` on the POST states an intention; it does not establish that\nRender honoured it. The response is only checked when it happens to echo a\ncommit, so on its own the pin fails open — an API that stopped echoing the\nfield, or silently dropped `commitId` from the request, is indistinguishable\nfrom success, and the run would then wait on and green-light a build of the\ntracked branch''s tip.\n\nThe deploy detail endpoint reports the commit actually built, and the wait step\nalready polls it, so that is where the pin is now confirmed. A commit that\ndisagrees fails the run as soon as the API admits it, rather than after the\nfull 30-minute ceiling, and outranks a `live` status. A deploy that reaches\n`live` having never named a commit is reported as unverified and fails: nothing\nin that outcome shows what was built.\n\nTolerating a commit-less *POST* response stays deliberate — failing closed\nthere would break every deploy against an API that simply does not echo the\nfield, and the confirmation above is what makes the tolerance safe. The test\nthat accepts it now says so and points at the tests that close it.\n\nAn unparseable or empty answer still costs one poll rather than the deploy,\nwhich is the pre-existing behaviour and is pinned by a test now.\n\nFound by codex on the third review round. The wait step''s program is executed\nagainst synthetic deploy payloads the same way the other two are, and each\nbranch was mutation-checked: restoring the fail-open `live`, dropping the\nmismatch check, removing COMMIT_ID from the step''s env, and turning a transient\nparse failure into a hard failure each fail the suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf1daddb0393846f63c30d505f5cec1fbe1653f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/bf1daddb0393846f63c30d505f5cec1fbe1653f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDI1N2IwY2FlYzc1ZGQ2Yjc5NGJlMzM3NDY0ODZjMTMzNzc2NGI5MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569","sha":"a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569"}],"sha":"257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/257b0caec75dd6b794be33746486c1337764b915"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:14:33Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:09:03Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"fix(auth): gate the portal introspection fallback, bound its outbound calls\n\nCloses the blockers a fresh-context review found in #359, plus the tests that\nwould have caught them.\n\n1. The `alg` header selected the verification path. Dispatch was\n   `RS256 -> JWKS, everything else -> introspection`, and routing into this\n   provider takes only an *unverified* `iss` — so an anonymous caller chose\n   the network path, and with it whatever laxness the portal''s introspection\n   endpoint has, by writing one header field. Dispatch is now an allowlist:\n   RS256 offline, HS256/384/512 to introspection, everything else (`none`,\n   an unexpected asymmetric alg, junk) rejected locally. `isinstance(alg, str)`\n   guards the membership test, because the header is only guaranteed to be a\n   JSON object — `{\"alg\": [\"HS256\"]}` would otherwise raise TypeError out of\n   dispatch, which the caller logs at warning level, once per request, for a\n   caller who supplied the header.\n\n2. That introspection path had no cache, no floor and no rate limit, and\n   only *successful* verifications are cached upstream, so every failed\n   attempt re-issued a blocking 5s POST. DRF authenticates before it\n   throttles, so AnonRateThrottle could not reach it, and the service\n   doubled as a request amplifier against the portal. Now every check that\n   can be made without the network happens first (alg, token_type, exp — all\n   reject-only, since the payload is unverified), and the remaining calls\n   draw on a fixed-window budget, warning once per window rather than once\n   per rejected request. What the budget does not do is documented on the\n   class — it is not keyed by caller, it bounds rate rather than concurrency,\n   and it is per process. Worker exhaustion is closed by (3), not by this.\n\n3. The fallback was not gated to dev. Both PHR_*_URLs derive from one\n   PHR_BASE_URL, so every deployment configuring RS256 silently enabled\n   introspection too. It delegates the signature check to another service —\n   an `active` response is taken as vouching for the token, and where §2.2\n   leaves the response silent about the subject the unverified payload\n   supplies it — so a portal that introspects without fully verifying\n   signatures would let a forged token through. Now behind\n   PHR_ALLOW_INTROSPECTION, defaulting on only for DEBUG/local, and reading\n   ENVIRONMENT via os.environ.get so an unset value counts as deployed. The\n   module-level ENVIRONMENT defaults to ''local'', so the obvious form fails\n   OPEN in exactly the misconfigured deploy the gate exists for; this is the\n   same shape ENABLE_DRF_TOKEN_AUTH already uses.\n\n   Compose sets that flag directly rather than ENVIRONMENT=local, whose .env\n   is optional and which would also switch on EXACT_ALLOW_PERSON_ID_LOOKUP —\n   a gate deliberately closed for #150/#108, since the `?person_id=` resolver\n   reads from PROMOP under a static service token not bound to the caller.\n\nThe deploy workflow had two problems, and the first hid the second.\n\n`on.workflow_run` named `workflows: [django]`. That key matches a workflow''s\n`name:`, and django.yml is named `backend` — so the deploy never fired, every\n`if:` below it was unreachable, and nothing reported an error. Fixing that\nmakes the workflow live, which exposes the second: it posted `-d ''{}''`, and\nRender then builds whatever the tracked branch points at on arrival, not the\nrevision that passed the suite. A push landing while the suite ran would ship\nuntested — the race the gate exists to close. The request now pins `commitId`\nto the triggering run''s `head_sha`, passed via `env:` and serialised with\njson.dumps. Both response paths verify the commit they got back, so an API\nthat silently dropped the field could not pass as success; the 202 path, which\nadopts \"the most recent deploy\", additionally requires it to be in flight\nrather than merely not `live`. `workflow_dispatch` is now branch-guarded too:\nunpinned it always built the tracked branch, but pinned it would ship the\ndispatched ref''s untested tip.\n\nTwo smaller changes the tests forced. `exp` is now `require`d on the JWKS\npath: PyJWT''s expiry check is a no-op when the claim is absent, so a token\nminted without one never expired, and a suite documenting that as intended\nwould be worse than no suite. An introspection response is rejected unless\nit is an object whose `active` is literally `true` — the string \"false\" is\ntruthy — and a non-boolean is logged, since otherwise a portal answering `1`\n401s every sign-in with nothing to say why.\n\nThe class docstring claimed the \"phr:\" prefix was descriptive because\nIdentity is keyed on (issuer, sub). It is not: `Identity.sub` is\n`unique=True` globally, which makes the prefix the only thing keeping a\nportal id out of another issuer''s subject namespace. Corrected, since the\ncomment as written invited removing it.\n\nEvery fix here was mutation-checked: reverted one at a time, each now fails\nthe suite. Two rounds of review were needed to get there. The dispatch tests\nfirst passed with the allowlist reverted, because with the gate closed a\nrejected token looks identical either way — they now enable introspection and\nassert on the outbound-call lists. The workflow tests first passed with the\n`-d` argument deleted, because `''commitId'' in source` was satisfied by the\ncomment explaining it — they now parse the step''s script and, for the two\nembedded programs, execute them against synthetic Render responses, since a\nsource match proves a check is present and never that it is right.\n\ndocs/setup.md and .env.example gain all seven PHR_* variables. The env table\nthere already documents security-posture flags with their rationale, and the\none flag whoever configures a deployment most needs to find was missing.\n\nStill open from the same review, deliberately not in scope here: `/healthz`\ninherits AnonRateThrottle (500s when Redis is down), audience is never\nvalidated, and requirements.txt uses ranges against the repo''s `==`\nconvention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8b4407fd8e9ea9490aac2ea2056518ef6be173c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/8b4407fd8e9ea9490aac2ea2056518ef6be173c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKGE2MGJiZDUzNzc2MzA2ZGQzZmYxOTNmMWQzYTNhN2IzMmE0NzM1Njk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","sha":"758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b"}],"sha":"a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/a60bbd53776306dd3ff193f1d3a3a7b32a473569"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T03:11:45Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T03:20:19Z","email":"lmmobi98@gmail.com","name":"Leonid Morozov"},"message":"harden PHR auth: opt-in introspection, alg pinning, form-encoded RFC 7662, CD trigger fix\n\nReview of #359 surfaced an unauthenticated DoS/amplification vector plus a\nCD workflow that never triggers. Fixes both, base = feat/phr-federation.\n\n- Route only RS256 -> offline JWKS and HS256 -> introspection; reject every\n  other alg (none, RS384/PS256, HS256-for-RS256 confusion) instead of sending\n  it to a blocking outbound call.\n- Introspection is now OPT-IN: PHR_INTROSPECT_URL is no longer auto-derived\n  from PHR_BASE_URL, so an RS256 production deployment has no live introspect\n  surface a forged non-RS256 token could drive (JWKS path is throttled, this\n  one was not). docker-compose opts in explicitly so local HS256 federation\n  keeps working.\n- Introspection request is RFC 7662 §2.1-compliant: form-encoded body +\n  optional client auth via PHR_INTROSPECT_AUTH (\"id:secret\" -> HTTP Basic;\n  a value without \":\" is ignored with a warning, not sent as empty password).\n- deploy-render.yml listened for workflow `django`, but the CI workflow is\n  named `backend`; workflow_run matches the name, so the deploy never fired.\n\nAdds adversarial provider tests (alg routing, opt-in no-network guard,\naccess-vs-refresh, form-encoding/auth, response-subject authority); the\nno-network guard records calls and asserts after verify() returns, so it\nfails if the routing/opt-in hardening is reverted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4f5a913c748d8360471bc666f7889d84112c146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/b4f5a913c748d8360471bc666f7889d84112c146"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2562446?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LeonidMorozov","id":2562446,"login":"LeonidMorozov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjI0NDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LeonidMorozov","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDgwMjdmM2NkODEyMjVkNGNlYjkyZjUzZmEzM2VlNzY1MGE1ZmNmZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","sha":"758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b"}],"sha":"8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/8027f3cd81225d4ceb92f53fa33ee7650a5fcfd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/2edbe62b91d38bf679b3b61d9dd25b75320adcb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T00:17:03Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T00:17:03Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"Stop the eligibility table 500ing on a corpus behind the models\n\nPOST /trials/<id>/match/ returned 500 on staging:\n\n  trial_attributes.py:379  attr_value = getattr(trial, attr_name)\n  -> DeferredAttribute.__get__ -> refresh_from_db([...])\n  -> ProgrammingError: column trials_trial.omop_intervention_concept_ids\n     does not exist\n\n`details` walks every field the model declares and reads it, so deferring\nthe columns the corpus lacks was not enough — the deferred load fires on\nattribute access and names the missing column anyway. This is the limit\nrecorded in the previous commit, reached by a details view rather than a\nfilter.\n\nSkipping is the right answer here. A filter over data the corpus does not\ncarry should still fail loudly, because a silent empty match is a wrong\nclinical answer. A details view has no such problem: the corpus holds no\nvalue for the attribute, so there is nothing to render, and dropping the\nrow is what the user would see anyway if the column existed and were\nnull. Only this one site enumerates Trial''s fields.\n\nReproduced locally first, since staging was the only place with data: a\nlocal database migrated to the current schema, seeded through the same\nloaders the test suite uses, then stripped of exactly what the real\ncorpus is missing — the three columns, the three tables, and\ndjango_migrations. That reproduced the identical ProgrammingError, and\nnow returns 200.\n\nThe regression test drives the same shape through TrialAttributes with a\ncolumn that raises on read. Verified it fails without the skip. Suite is\n719 passed against 718 on the same baseline; the 19 failures there are\npre-existing and unrelated.","tree":{"sha":"7701d902727febe200309e1e9fbb8609f2b7c663","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/7701d902727febe200309e1e9fbb8609f2b7c663"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/2edbe62b91d38bf679b3b61d9dd25b75320adcb2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/2edbe62b91d38bf679b3b61d9dd25b75320adcb2","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDJlZGJlNjJiOTFkMzhiZjY3OWIzYjYxZDlkZDI1Yjc1MzIwYWRjYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c","sha":"1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c"}],"sha":"2edbe62b91d38bf679b3b61d9dd25b75320adcb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/2edbe62b91d38bf679b3b61d9dd25b75320adcb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:24:13Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:47:14Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"Let the trial endpoints work against a corpus behind the models\n\nThe trials corpus is data-only and externally owned: no django_migrations\ntable, and the router refuses to migrate the trials app into it precisely\nbecause its schema is somebody else''s to change. So the models drift\nahead of it and nothing notices until a query names a column that is not\nthere, at which point the endpoint 500s. That is the state today — the\ncorpus is missing sixteen columns on trials_trial alone, plus\nomop_concept_id on three therapy tables.\n\nWith TRIALS_DB_TOLERATE_MISSING_COLUMNS set, every manager in the app is\nwrapped so its querysets defer what the database lacks. Off by default,\nso a deployment whose database matches the models is untouched.\n\nApplied at the manager level rather than per view because per view does\nnot hold: fixing /trials/ alone left /form-settings/ failing on\ntrials_therapy.omop_concept_id, and the next endpoint over whichever\ntable drifts next would have followed.\n\nDeliberately narrow. A missing table defers nothing: that is a relation\nthe corpus has never held, and serving empty results for it would hide a\nreal gap. Deferred columns still raise if something reads them, because\nDjango reloads a deferred attribute on access — a filter over data the\ncorpus does not carry should fail loudly rather than quietly match on\nnothing. Introspection failure defers nothing either; if we cannot tell,\nwe do not guess. Related managers are not wrapped, which is one more\nreason this is a stopgap rather than an abstraction to build on.\n\nA stopgap for #360, not a replacement for it. The corpus and the models\nneed something tying them together; until that exists, a read-only\nconsumer needs a way to work against what is actually there.","tree":{"sha":"29cf0abbd43405bbfc3c156ef1e2942bebe8e40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/29cf0abbd43405bbfc3c156ef1e2942bebe8e40a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDFjMTNjZmQxZWIwNGIxNmUyNzg1NDI5MmUxNjI2MTJiMmZhOTllOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","sha":"758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b"}],"sha":"1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/1c13cfd1eb04b16e27854292e162612b2fa99e9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T20:08:33Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:47:07Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"Add a health endpoint and Render staging CD\n\n/healthz checks the default database rather than merely proving Django\nbooted: a probe that stays green through a deploy whose migrations never\nran lets the platform route traffic to a service that 500s on every real\nrequest. It deliberately skips the trials alias, which points at an\nexternal host — an outage there should not pull this service out of\nrotation when the trial endpoints already degrade on their own.\n\nThe Render workflow ships main alongside the existing Cloud Run one;\nneither platform is authoritative. It hangs off workflow_run for the\ndjango suite because none of this repo''s CI workflows are callable, and\nrewiring them is a larger change than this deploy justifies.","tree":{"sha":"9c65a3dd3f3b3b5038b2191a4f9ccd5f0ab9e575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/9c65a3dd3f3b3b5038b2191a4f9ccd5f0ab9e575"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDc1OGY3YTYyZmRiYTBiZDhkMjE3ZmJjMTU5Yjk1NDAwYTE1NjM5MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab","sha":"9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab"}],"sha":"758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/758f7a62fdba0bd8d217fbc159b95400a156390b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T19:40:31Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:47:07Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"Accept portal-issued tokens, and ship the federation remote in the image\n\nThree things stood between EXACT and the portal''s Find Trials page.\n\nAuth: PARTNER_AUTH_PROVIDERS listed only Firebase, so a patient arriving\nwith a portal token was rejected. PhrTokenProvider verifies RS256 tokens\nagainst the portal''s JWKS (cached, with a refresh floor so an unknown kid\ncannot drive an unbounded number of outbound fetches) and falls back to\nintrospection for deployments still on the HS256 dev key. Identities are\nprovisioned as sub=\"phr:<id>\" because Identity.sub is unique globally here\nrather than per issuer, so a raw portal id could collide with another\nissuer''s subject namespace.\n\nThe chain is env-driven, defaulting to both providers so existing\ndeployments are unchanged. Compose sets it to the portal provider alone,\nwhich is how a deployment with no Firebase should run.\n\nServing: nothing built the remote and nothing served it — the Dockerfile\nhad only a Python stage, and there was no whitenoise configuration at all.\nA node stage now builds the remote into the image, and whitenoise serves it\nfrom the site root at /remoteEntry.js with permissive CORS, since the host\nfetches it cross-origin.\n\nReproducible builds: frontend/ had no package-lock.json, unlike soc and\nhk-labs, so `npm ci` had nothing to install from. Generated one.\n\nLocal run: compose now points at a portal on the host. CORS is left\nallow-all locally rather than pinned to a dev port — vite moves to 5174,\n5175… whenever the previous port is taken, and a pinned list looks correct\nright up until it blocks the portal''s preflight.\n\nVerified against the running stack: /trials/ and /countries/ return 401\nwithout a token and 200 with a portal token, the identity lands as\nissuer=healthkey-phr sub=phr:1, and /remoteEntry.js is served with\nAccess-Control-Allow-Origin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5305f7ff558888276961531635b8d6787ccee6f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/5305f7ff558888276961531635b8d6787ccee6f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDliMmM4NWIwY2JjNTEwZjk2ZGE0MmVmZTBmNTY2NjQyZjhjYTFlYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/7a367b3b1f0494ec0d22da7aef9d54b0a6da8434","sha":"7a367b3b1f0494ec0d22da7aef9d54b0a6da8434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/7a367b3b1f0494ec0d22da7aef9d54b0a6da8434"}],"sha":"9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/9b2c85b0cbc510f96da42efe0f566642f8ca1eab"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/7a367b3b1f0494ec0d22da7aef9d54b0a6da8434/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T11:35:54Z","email":"adam@dplrn.com","name":"Adam Blum"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T11:35:54Z","email":"adam@dplrn.com","name":"Adam Blum"},"message":"docs: promote API reference to API_SURFACE.md and polish README\n\nRename docs/api.md → API_SURFACE.md (root-level, matching PROMOP convention),\nadd prominent callout link, end quickstart with a curl example, and merge the\ntwo duplicative docs/setup.md references into one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"deed0d6f39ce3e081b8dc8eff6abe32eccaee398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/trees/deed0d6f39ce3e081b8dc8eff6abe32eccaee398"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/git/commits/7a367b3b1f0494ec0d22da7aef9d54b0a6da8434","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/7a367b3b1f0494ec0d22da7aef9d54b0a6da8434","node_id":"C_kwDORYlqjNoAKDdhMzY3YjNiMWYwNDk0ZWMwZDIyZGE3YWVmOWQ1NGIwYTZkYTg0MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/exact/commit/172a4820e5f06f6b28c566f79db3dcc5d138d148","sha":"172a4820e5f06f6b28c566f79db3dcc5d138d148","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/exact/commits/172a4820e5f06f6b28c566f79db3dcc5d138d148"}]