low/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/f49c276ce1e7d8351fbc20ca6c6ba54ccc4d03b3","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKGY0OWMyNzZjZTFlN2Q4MzUxZmJjMjBjYTZjNmJhNTRjY2M0ZDAzYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/b6cc8f2f87ad1ca223cb10d8d3c63d77da97e0ae","sha":"b6cc8f2f87ad1ca223cb10d8d3c63d77da97e0ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/b6cc8f2f87ad1ca223cb10d8d3c63d77da97e0ae"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93","sha":"7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93"}],"sha":"f49c276ce1e7d8351fbc20ca6c6ba54ccc4d03b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/f49c276ce1e7d8351fbc20ca6c6ba54ccc4d03b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:04:44Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:04:44Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"test: retarget the office transactions dead-end at the door it now closes\n\n`rbac-dead-end-controls.spec.ts` drove the refused-list state with a user\nholding READ_OFFICETRANSACTION and not READ_OFFICE: the route admitted them and\nthe platform then refused `GET /officetransactions`, leaving column headers that\nread as \"there are no office transactions\".\n\nGating the route on READ_OFFICE — the code the platform actually checks — closes\nthat door, so the test was asserting a dead end this branch removed. It failed\non CI for exactly that reason. It now asserts the refusal, including that the\nquery string names the code the user is missing rather than the one they hold.\n\nThe component still carries the refused-load state, correctly, for every other\nway the request can fail, and no user can reach it through permissions any more.\nSo it moves to a unit test, which also covers a load that merely failed and a\npayload that is not the array the endpoint claims. The request is driven through\nHttpTestingController rather than by mocking the generated DefaultService, which\nwould have put an ADR 0006 boundary violation in a test file.\n\nVerified against a running Fineract: 8/8 in that spec, first attempt.","tree":{"sha":"281ab3f7d4055032e09e7b71cb5bfaa234f7718a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/281ab3f7d4055032e09e7b71cb5bfaa234f7718a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93","verification":{"payload":"tree 281ab3f7d4055032e09e7b71cb5bfaa234f7718a\nparent 30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791050684 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791050684 +0530\n\ntest: retarget the office transactions dead-end at the door it now closes\n\n`rbac-dead-end-controls.spec.ts` drove the refused-list state with a user\nholding READ_OFFICETRANSACTION and not READ_OFFICE: the route admitted them and\nthe platform then refused `GET /officetransactions`, leaving column headers that\nread as \"there are no office transactions\".\n\nGating the route on READ_OFFICE — the code the platform actually checks — closes\nthat door, so the test was asserting a dead end this branch removed. It failed\non CI for exactly that reason. It now asserts the refusal, including that the\nquery string names the code the user is missing rather than the one they hold.\n\nThe component still carries the refused-load state, correctly, for every other\nway the request can fail, and no user can reach it through permissions any more.\nSo it moves to a unit test, which also covers a load that merely failed and a\npayload that is not the array the endpoint claims. The request is driven through\nHttpTestingController rather than by mocking the generated DefaultService, which\nwould have put an ADR 0006 boundary violation in a test file.\n\nVerified against a running Fineract: 8/8 in that spec, first attempt.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasFDvgAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzTYEAP4/jjbGVaHfv6asXWMq9rLcIMnzxWhZbcNNarrTZCbgjwD/bJjjPfD4gtVz\nQGsh6pvLe8lo/K+LoZCPrUs+/xq9IQ4=\n=yPKC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T18:05:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDdiYjcxMTM3ODQ1NmY4YzA5MzlhOTIxNWU2NDg0NWEzMGM0ZDBjOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe","sha":"30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe"}],"sha":"7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/7bb711378456f8c0939a9215e64845a30c4d0c93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:58:12Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:58:12Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"fix(ci): download each comment artifact by name, so the diagram comment appears\n\nThe change sequence diagram has never been posted on a pull request. The job\nrendered it and the artifact uploaded fine — CI run 37140999866 holds an\n874-byte `pr-comment-diagram` — but the publisher skipped it every time and\nreported success.\n\n`pr-comments.yml` downloaded with `pattern: pr-comment-*`, and\ndownload-artifact resolves the destination as\n\n    isSingleArtifactDownload || mergeMultiple || artifacts.length === 1\n      ? path\n      : path/<artifact name>\n\nCI renders only the diagram, so the pattern always matched exactly one\nartifact and the file landed in `summaries/pr-diagram.md` with no directory.\nThe directory name is how `post-e2e-comments.js` binds a body to the marker it\nmay post under, so a missing one is indistinguishable from an artifact that was\nnever uploaded. The E2E summaries were unaffected because that run uploads two,\nwhich is why half the mechanism looked healthy.\n\nEach artifact is now downloaded by name into its own directory, so the layout no\nlonger depends on how many a run happened to produce.\n\nTwo further defects in the same mechanism:\n\n- The concurrency group was `<this workflow''s name>-<commit>`, identical for\n  CI''s publisher and E2E''s publisher. With cancel-in-progress, whichever run\n  finished second killed the first and dropped its comment. Keyed on\n  `workflow_run.workflow_id` as well now — the numeric id rather than the name,\n  which a `pull_request` run takes from the pull request''s own head.\n- Posting nothing logged three \"skipping\" lines and a green check. It now\n  reports what `summaries/` actually held, and names a root-level `.md` as the\n  collapsed-layout symptom.\n\n`post-e2e-comments.js` had no tests. It has seven, including one that pins the\nagreement between the allow-list, the `upload-artifact` names and the download\ndirectories — the only pre-merge check possible here, since a `workflow_run`\nworkflow always runs the copy on the default branch.","tree":{"sha":"5f9325a2a8ac72fc7952809e320bb079de1e6d17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/5f9325a2a8ac72fc7952809e320bb079de1e6d17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f9325a2a8ac72fc7952809e320bb079de1e6d17\nparent 2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791050292 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791050292 +0530\n\nfix(ci): download each comment artifact by name, so the diagram comment appears\n\nThe change sequence diagram has never been posted on a pull request. The job\nrendered it and the artifact uploaded fine — CI run 37140999866 holds an\n874-byte `pr-comment-diagram` — but the publisher skipped it every time and\nreported success.\n\n`pr-comments.yml` downloaded with `pattern: pr-comment-*`, and\ndownload-artifact resolves the destination as\n\n    isSingleArtifactDownload || mergeMultiple || artifacts.length === 1\n      ? path\n      : path/<artifact name>\n\nCI renders only the diagram, so the pattern always matched exactly one\nartifact and the file landed in `summaries/pr-diagram.md` with no directory.\nThe directory name is how `post-e2e-comments.js` binds a body to the marker it\nmay post under, so a missing one is indistinguishable from an artifact that was\nnever uploaded. The E2E summaries were unaffected because that run uploads two,\nwhich is why half the mechanism looked healthy.\n\nEach artifact is now downloaded by name into its own directory, so the layout no\nlonger depends on how many a run happened to produce.\n\nTwo further defects in the same mechanism:\n\n- The concurrency group was `<this workflow''s name>-<commit>`, identical for\n  CI''s publisher and E2E''s publisher. With cancel-in-progress, whichever run\n  finished second killed the first and dropped its comment. Keyed on\n  `workflow_run.workflow_id` as well now — the numeric id rather than the name,\n  which a `pull_request` run takes from the pull request''s own head.\n- Posting nothing logged three \"skipping\" lines and a green check. It now\n  reports what `summaries/` actually held, and names a root-level `.md` as the\n  collapsed-layout symptom.\n\n`post-e2e-comments.js` had no tests. It has seven, including one that pins the\nagreement between the allow-list, the `upload-artifact` names and the download\ndirectories — the only pre-merge check possible here, since a `workflow_run`\nworkflow always runs the copy on the default branch.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasFCNAAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzTNjAQCf0y4s+xxXq6gn4PqwjyFX3HKUz74I2BMpo563/L1W9AD/c19zAJQeCVYY\nWpPs24fUrvt8uP8cUQ7MSCv4MXO5Igw=\n=LWcH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:58:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDMwZDliOTFhNzJkNWE0NDM1NDI2MmQ4ODI4NWFhN2MwYmY2NDk3ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533","sha":"2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533"}],"sha":"30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/30d9b91a72d5a44354262d88285aa7c0bf6497fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:34:13Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:34:13Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"fix(scripts): stop disabling certificate validation to refresh the snapshot\n\nCodeQL flagged NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0 in the snapshot script as\nHigh, and it was right. Fineract''s e2e container publishes 8443 only with\nthe self-signed certificate it generates for itself, so there is no CA to\nvalidate against -- but disabling validation for the whole process is the\nkind of line that gets copied somewhere it matters.\n\nScoping it to one agent was the first attempt. It is genuinely narrower,\nand I added a guard that refused any non-loopback host, so an unvalidated\nconnection could not leave the machine. But `rejectUnauthorized: false`\nis the same sink wherever it sits, and it would have stayed a bad line in\nthe tree whether or not the scanner kept flagging it.\n\nSplitting the two jobs removes it instead. Obtaining the payload is the\noperator''s business and belongs in a shell script, where e2e-stack.sh\nalready does exactly this against exactly this endpoint:\n\n  curl -k -s -o /dev/null -w ''%{http_code}'' --max-time 5 \"$HEALTH_URL\"\n\nSo fetch-permission-codes.sh fetches and snapshot-permission-codes.mjs\nnormalises stdin. No TLS configuration is left in scanned code at all,\nand the pair now works for any way of getting the JSON -- the local\nstack, a real instance with a proper chain (FINERACT_CA_CERT, which drops\n-k), or a file saved earlier.\n\nThe normaliser is better for being pure: it validates what it is given\nrather than what it fetched. Empty stdin, an HTML error page, a Fineract\nerror object, and a truncated payload each fail with their own message,\nand the existing 500-code floor still refuses to overwrite a good\nsnapshot with a partial one. All four verified, with the snapshot intact\nafterwards.\n\nnpm run permissions:snapshot is unchanged for the caller.","tree":{"sha":"88ad9d0ed04dd080da856b1a5569326465e9a225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/88ad9d0ed04dd080da856b1a5569326465e9a225"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533","verification":{"payload":"tree 88ad9d0ed04dd080da856b1a5569326465e9a225\nparent c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791048853 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791048853 +0530\n\nfix(scripts): stop disabling certificate validation to refresh the snapshot\n\nCodeQL flagged NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0 in the snapshot script as\nHigh, and it was right. Fineract''s e2e container publishes 8443 only with\nthe self-signed certificate it generates for itself, so there is no CA to\nvalidate against -- but disabling validation for the whole process is the\nkind of line that gets copied somewhere it matters.\n\nScoping it to one agent was the first attempt. It is genuinely narrower,\nand I added a guard that refused any non-loopback host, so an unvalidated\nconnection could not leave the machine. But `rejectUnauthorized: false`\nis the same sink wherever it sits, and it would have stayed a bad line in\nthe tree whether or not the scanner kept flagging it.\n\nSplitting the two jobs removes it instead. Obtaining the payload is the\noperator''s business and belongs in a shell script, where e2e-stack.sh\nalready does exactly this against exactly this endpoint:\n\n  curl -k -s -o /dev/null -w ''%{http_code}'' --max-time 5 \"$HEALTH_URL\"\n\nSo fetch-permission-codes.sh fetches and snapshot-permission-codes.mjs\nnormalises stdin. No TLS configuration is left in scanned code at all,\nand the pair now works for any way of getting the JSON -- the local\nstack, a real instance with a proper chain (FINERACT_CA_CERT, which drops\n-k), or a file saved earlier.\n\nThe normaliser is better for being pure: it validates what it is given\nrather than what it fetched. Empty stdin, an HTML error page, a Fineract\nerror object, and a truncated payload each fail with their own message,\nand the existing 500-code floor still refuses to overwrite a good\nsnapshot with a partial one. All four verified, with the snapshot intact\nafterwards.\n\nnpm run permissions:snapshot is unchanged for the caller.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasE8lQAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzRsCAP0VR9iZj/53FFVC1Q0E1IHKJfijFrxErBFnEi0foRadIwEAqTZ6Cy+eAGbI\n4cTqorCrQz0THWR6XwA83iYstD56LQI=\n=S9YY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:34:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDJjMjdmYWFmMjQzMzU4OTRhNTBmODQyZWJkOTc4ZGUzMGEwZTM1MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66","sha":"c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66"}],"sha":"2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/2c27faaf24335894a50f842ebd978de30a0e3533"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:07:52Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:23:03Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"fix(savings): require the payment type a deposit cannot be made without\n\nThe savings transaction form left Payment Type optional, so Save was\nenabled without it and the platform refused the submission:\n\n  POST /savingsaccounts/{id}/transactions?command=deposit     400\n  POST /savingsaccounts/{id}/transactions?command=withdrawal  400\n  validation.msg.savingsaccount.transaction.paymentTypeId.cannot.be.blank\n\nThe only way to find out the field was mandatory was to fill the form,\nsubmit, and be rejected -- with the form still on screen and the amount\nstill typed in.\n\n`required` is scoped correctly by where the control already sits: inside\nthe same `@if (command() !== ''postInterestAsOn'')` block as\ntransactionAmount, which is also required. So it applies to the two cash\ncommands and not to the one command that posts no payment.\n\nFound while writing the non-admin savings spec, which is also why that\nspec now captures the POST response rather than inferring success from\nthe account view. A refusal fails on the submit line naming the platform''s\nreason, instead of three lines later as a balance that never appeared.","tree":{"sha":"0a26ef83c22b02197a9fc6a2c808e565faa785e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/0a26ef83c22b02197a9fc6a2c808e565faa785e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a26ef83c22b02197a9fc6a2c808e565faa785e8\nparent e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791047272 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791048183 +0530\n\nfix(savings): require the payment type a deposit cannot be made without\n\nThe savings transaction form left Payment Type optional, so Save was\nenabled without it and the platform refused the submission:\n\n  POST /savingsaccounts/{id}/transactions?command=deposit     400\n  POST /savingsaccounts/{id}/transactions?command=withdrawal  400\n  validation.msg.savingsaccount.transaction.paymentTypeId.cannot.be.blank\n\nThe only way to find out the field was mandatory was to fill the form,\nsubmit, and be rejected -- with the form still on screen and the amount\nstill typed in.\n\n`required` is scoped correctly by where the control already sits: inside\nthe same `@if (command() !== ''postInterestAsOn'')` block as\ntransactionAmount, which is also required. So it applies to the two cash\ncommands and not to the one command that posts no payment.\n\nFound while writing the non-admin savings spec, which is also why that\nspec now captures the POST response rather than inferring success from\nthe account view. A refusal fails on the submit line naming the platform''s\nreason, instead of three lines later as a balance that never appeared.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasE59wAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzb3cAP9e3ovuxUSWxfdtQwCAgohjbC+5mTmIcMmY26iMW3BbpgEA1TBQkB8KSNfq\nZ5BbMJclDr0yDsmj1FWmAP5mfix/Ogs=\n=6FK0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:24:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKGMyZjBiZGQwNjc2YTAxNTZjMzExMDQwZmEwNjA5Y2MyYTY0ZTdhNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128","sha":"e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128"}],"sha":"c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/c2f0bdd0676a0156c311040fa0609cc2a64e7a66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:03:57Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:23:02Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"test(e2e): reopen the savings view after an action, which redirects to the list\n\nThe savings approve and activate forms return to /products/savings-accounts,\nnot to the account -- unlike the loan approve form, which comes back to the\nloan. So the new status cannot be read from wherever Save left the page.\n\nFound by running it: the assertion was looking for ''Approved'' on the list.","tree":{"sha":"1c1731d482ceb89ddbb27e08b5c1a5821ec9fa40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/1c1731d482ceb89ddbb27e08b5c1a5821ec9fa40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c1731d482ceb89ddbb27e08b5c1a5821ec9fa40\nparent 7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791047037 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791048182 +0530\n\ntest(e2e): reopen the savings view after an action, which redirects to the list\n\nThe savings approve and activate forms return to /products/savings-accounts,\nnot to the account -- unlike the loan approve form, which comes back to the\nloan. So the new status cannot be read from wherever Save left the page.\n\nFound by running it: the assertion was looking for ''Approved'' on the list.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasE59wAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzWtFAQD/0/QGLde4+eGhf2QgSJRpCkzhX7qMSFjMf4W0LbEXwAEAk1c4qZBS3EC5\nUrKGNiN7tIFRendOfZuaHrl/3GRdRgI=\n=X4lB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:24:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKGU4YWFjOWI2MWQ1ZWJmNGZmYTVlYjFmMDZmNWMzMTI3NTk4YWYxMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a","sha":"7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a"}],"sha":"e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/e8aac9b61d5ebf4ffa5eb1f06f5c3127598af128"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:58:10Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:23:02Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"test(e2e): cover savings duties under non-admin roles, and invert the loan gate assertions\n\nAdds e2e/savings-flows-non-admin-roles.spec.ts, the companion to the loan\none: a savings account from application to funded across four separated\nduties -- officer, approver, activator, teller -- with every role, grant\nand account created by filling the forms. Fineract''s transaction_savings\ngrouping had no coverage at all before this.\n\nIt pins down the two defects fixed in this branch:\n\n  - the teller, holding only DEPOSIT_SAVINGSACCOUNT and\n    WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT, now reaches the deposit form and records a\n    deposit; an UPDATE_SAVINGSACCOUNT holder is refused both the control\n    and the URL.\n  - the cash-withdrawal control is asserted from both sides: offered to a\n    holder of WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT, refused to a holder of\n    WITHDRAW_SAVINGSACCOUNT. That is the one a code-existence check\n    cannot find, because both codes are real.\n\nThe loan spec''s two #691 cases now assert the fix rather than the defect.\nThe disburser holding only DISBURSE_LOAN drives the payout to Active, and\nthe repayment duty drives a repayment -- both end to end, because a gate\nthat admits the right user but a form that cannot submit would pass a\nnarrower assertion. A new case asserts that an unmapped command is still\nadmitted, so the decision not to guess a code stays visible.\n\nOne ordering trap worth recording. The editor''s test originally asserted\nthe Disburse button was refused, which broke once the disburser actually\ncompleted the payout: Disburse is gated on `@if (isLoanApproved)`, so on\nan active loan it is absent for everyone including a superuser. That\nassertion would have passed for a reason unrelated to permissions, which\nis how an assertion keeps passing after what it checked has broken. It\nnow asserts Repayment, which is offered on an active loan and which that\naccount genuinely lacks the code for.\n\nThe role- and user-building helpers move to e2e/utils/ui-rbac.ts now that\ntwo specs need them, along with platformAllows() and the refused/offered\nassertions. Its header records why these drive the forms rather than\nseed-api.ts, and the three Ionic locator traps each cost a test cycle:\nion-input carries `name` on the inner native input, ion-checkbox does not\nreflect `name` onto the host at all, and a `multiple` ion-select renders\ncheckbox options that select-option.ts cannot drive.\n\nAdds data-testid to the savings approve and activate buttons, which had\nnone. Like the Disburse button, they need one: when the permission\ndirective refuses a control it replaces the accessible name with the\nreason, so a name-based locator stops finding the button in exactly the\nstate a permission test needs to assert on.","tree":{"sha":"32d62f8b6149da7f29592dfb329fe3bd6ee0d351","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/32d62f8b6149da7f29592dfb329fe3bd6ee0d351"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 32d62f8b6149da7f29592dfb329fe3bd6ee0d351\nparent 4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791046690 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791048182 +0530\n\ntest(e2e): cover savings duties under non-admin roles, and invert the loan gate assertions\n\nAdds e2e/savings-flows-non-admin-roles.spec.ts, the companion to the loan\none: a savings account from application to funded across four separated\nduties -- officer, approver, activator, teller -- with every role, grant\nand account created by filling the forms. Fineract''s transaction_savings\ngrouping had no coverage at all before this.\n\nIt pins down the two defects fixed in this branch:\n\n  - the teller, holding only DEPOSIT_SAVINGSACCOUNT and\n    WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT, now reaches the deposit form and records a\n    deposit; an UPDATE_SAVINGSACCOUNT holder is refused both the control\n    and the URL.\n  - the cash-withdrawal control is asserted from both sides: offered to a\n    holder of WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT, refused to a holder of\n    WITHDRAW_SAVINGSACCOUNT. That is the one a code-existence check\n    cannot find, because both codes are real.\n\nThe loan spec''s two #691 cases now assert the fix rather than the defect.\nThe disburser holding only DISBURSE_LOAN drives the payout to Active, and\nthe repayment duty drives a repayment -- both end to end, because a gate\nthat admits the right user but a form that cannot submit would pass a\nnarrower assertion. A new case asserts that an unmapped command is still\nadmitted, so the decision not to guess a code stays visible.\n\nOne ordering trap worth recording. The editor''s test originally asserted\nthe Disburse button was refused, which broke once the disburser actually\ncompleted the payout: Disburse is gated on `@if (isLoanApproved)`, so on\nan active loan it is absent for everyone including a superuser. That\nassertion would have passed for a reason unrelated to permissions, which\nis how an assertion keeps passing after what it checked has broken. It\nnow asserts Repayment, which is offered on an active loan and which that\naccount genuinely lacks the code for.\n\nThe role- and user-building helpers move to e2e/utils/ui-rbac.ts now that\ntwo specs need them, along with platformAllows() and the refused/offered\nassertions. Its header records why these drive the forms rather than\nseed-api.ts, and the three Ionic locator traps each cost a test cycle:\nion-input carries `name` on the inner native input, ion-checkbox does not\nreflect `name` onto the host at all, and a `multiple` ion-select renders\ncheckbox options that select-option.ts cannot drive.\n\nAdds data-testid to the savings approve and activate buttons, which had\nnone. Like the Disburse button, they need one: when the permission\ndirective refuses a control it replaces the accessible name with the\nreason, so a name-based locator stops finding the button in exactly the\nstate a permission test needs to assert on.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasE59gAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzXacAP9zj8RKU1GXFwdNKWWqPhOGF0uQnrGMdDZCuTeOIPEVdgEA4QM/a7CgIVlR\ncMgtyk5ltqsb2NPCTRYADWhq5pLhMgk=\n=R2bA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:24:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDdhZmM3MGVmZTMzZjM3ODFjM2Q1YWQ3YjMyZDFiNWNlMWZhOGNmMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d","sha":"4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d"}],"sha":"7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/7afc70efe33f3781c3d5ad7b32d1b5ce1fa8cf0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:43:10Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:22:45Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"fix(rbac): name permission codes the platform actually defines\n\nThree action gates named a code that cannot authorise what they do. All\nthree were found by diffing every code the application names against a\nlive GET /v1/permissions, not by anyone using the app -- which is the\npoint of the check this also adds.\n\n1. The savings cash-withdrawal button asked for WITHDRAW_SAVINGSACCOUNT.\n   Both codes exist, one letter apart, and they are strictly not\n   interchangeable:\n\n     transactions?command=withdrawal   WITHDRAWAL_ 400   WITHDRAW_ 403\n     ?command=withdrawnByApplicant     WITHDRAWAL_ 403   WITHDRAW_ 400\n\n   WITHDRAW_SAVINGSACCOUNT withdraws the *application*, which is what the\n   Withdrawn-by-applicant button above it correctly uses. This one\n   withdraws *cash*. So a teller holding WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT was\n   shown a disabled button, and a holder of the application code was\n   offered an enabled one the platform refuses.\n\n2. UNDOWITHDRAW_CLIENT does not exist. The real code is\n   UNDOWITHDRAWAL_CLIENT -- the same missing \"AL\" -- confirmed at 400\n   against undoWithdrawal while WITHDRAW_CLIENT answers 403.\n\n3. UPDATE_LOAN_AVAILABLE_DISBURSEMENT_AMOUNT does not exist either, and\n   there is no narrower code to replace it with: a role granted all 721\n   grantable codes is still refused PUT /loans/{id}/available-\n   disbursement-amount, while the superuser gets 400 on the same request.\n   Found by bisecting the whole catalogue. It now declares ALL_FUNCTIONS,\n   which is the true requirement and makes the refusal hint name\n   something an administrator can act on.\n\n(2) and (3) are the failure DOCS/RBAC.md already warns about -- a gate on\na code no role can hold is worse than no gate, because the control is\ndisabled forever and looks exactly like one the viewer is not entitled\nto.\n\ncheck-permission-codes.mjs makes that class impossible to reintroduce. It\ncompares every code named in an action gate, structural gate, route, nav\nentry, data table or command map against a committed snapshot of the\ncatalogue, so it runs in CI with no Fineract started. The snapshot drifts\nonly as Fineract adds codes, which is a false pass and never a false\nfailure; permissions:snapshot refreshes it.\n\nWhat it deliberately cannot catch is (1): a code that exists but is wrong\nfor the operation. Only a run against a real platform separates those,\nwhich is what the backend RBAC specs are for. Both halves are stated in\nthe script''s header so nobody mistakes a green check for proof the codes\nare right.\n\nVerified by mutation: reintroducing UNDOWITHDRAW_CLIENT fails, a\nhollowed-out snapshot fails the sanity floor rather than passing\nvacuously, and swapping the savings code back to the wrong-but-real one\npasses -- confirming the stated limitation is real and not a claim.","tree":{"sha":"599de6a0c9d6ee81e1cd6cb8e34649ac93b5eff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/599de6a0c9d6ee81e1cd6cb8e34649ac93b5eff0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d","verification":{"payload":"tree 599de6a0c9d6ee81e1cd6cb8e34649ac93b5eff0\nparent a3004df1b11b979cfb11f8dc6dd32781da5b13da\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791045790 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791048165 +0530\n\nfix(rbac): name permission codes the platform actually defines\n\nThree action gates named a code that cannot authorise what they do. All\nthree were found by diffing every code the application names against a\nlive GET /v1/permissions, not by anyone using the app -- which is the\npoint of the check this also adds.\n\n1. The savings cash-withdrawal button asked for WITHDRAW_SAVINGSACCOUNT.\n   Both codes exist, one letter apart, and they are strictly not\n   interchangeable:\n\n     transactions?command=withdrawal   WITHDRAWAL_ 400   WITHDRAW_ 403\n     ?command=withdrawnByApplicant     WITHDRAWAL_ 403   WITHDRAW_ 400\n\n   WITHDRAW_SAVINGSACCOUNT withdraws the *application*, which is what the\n   Withdrawn-by-applicant button above it correctly uses. This one\n   withdraws *cash*. So a teller holding WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT was\n   shown a disabled button, and a holder of the application code was\n   offered an enabled one the platform refuses.\n\n2. UNDOWITHDRAW_CLIENT does not exist. The real code is\n   UNDOWITHDRAWAL_CLIENT -- the same missing \"AL\" -- confirmed at 400\n   against undoWithdrawal while WITHDRAW_CLIENT answers 403.\n\n3. UPDATE_LOAN_AVAILABLE_DISBURSEMENT_AMOUNT does not exist either, and\n   there is no narrower code to replace it with: a role granted all 721\n   grantable codes is still refused PUT /loans/{id}/available-\n   disbursement-amount, while the superuser gets 400 on the same request.\n   Found by bisecting the whole catalogue. It now declares ALL_FUNCTIONS,\n   which is the true requirement and makes the refusal hint name\n   something an administrator can act on.\n\n(2) and (3) are the failure DOCS/RBAC.md already warns about -- a gate on\na code no role can hold is worse than no gate, because the control is\ndisabled forever and looks exactly like one the viewer is not entitled\nto.\n\ncheck-permission-codes.mjs makes that class impossible to reintroduce. It\ncompares every code named in an action gate, structural gate, route, nav\nentry, data table or command map against a committed snapshot of the\ncatalogue, so it runs in CI with no Fineract started. The snapshot drifts\nonly as Fineract adds codes, which is a false pass and never a false\nfailure; permissions:snapshot refreshes it.\n\nWhat it deliberately cannot catch is (1): a code that exists but is wrong\nfor the operation. Only a run against a real platform separates those,\nwhich is what the backend RBAC specs are for. Both halves are stated in\nthe script''s header so nobody mistakes a green check for proof the codes\nare right.\n\nVerified by mutation: reintroducing UNDOWITHDRAW_CLIENT fails, a\nhollowed-out snapshot fails the sanity floor rather than passing\nvacuously, and swapping the savings code back to the wrong-but-real one\npasses -- confirming the stated limitation is real and not a claim.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasE55QAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzaK6AQDSLMkNgfKrH8sM57qg+gaA8Rlh/IKHWRYl4yRFqboVIwEA18cBObcVK43Q\nbAmCtGYNgJyumNPXOxgB1sB9CxJ/KAs=\n=GwJU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:24:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDRhODAxNmYwMDJjZGZmYmIwMmU4ZmU4OWQ0OWMwOGMxOTM1MmFkMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/a3004df1b11b979cfb11f8dc6dd32781da5b13da","sha":"a3004df1b11b979cfb11f8dc6dd32781da5b13da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/a3004df1b11b979cfb11f8dc6dd32781da5b13da"}],"sha":"4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/4a8016f002cdffbb02e8fe89d49c08c19352ad1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/a3004df1b11b979cfb11f8dc6dd32781da5b13da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T16:30:21Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T17:22:45Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"fix(rbac): gate transaction routes on the code each command needs\n\nCloses #691. Closes #665.\n\nThree dispatch routes declared one permission for many commands, and the\ncode they named was not one Fineract accepts for any of them.\n\n  /loans/:loanId/transactions/:type              UPDATE_LOAN\n  /products/savings-accounts/.../:command        UPDATE_SAVINGSACCOUNT\n\nBoth are in Fineract''s `portfolio` grouping while the commands they serve\nare in `transaction_loan` and `transaction_savings`. Measured with an\nempty body, which separates authorisation from validation without\nwriting anything:\n\n  DISBURSE_LOAN             -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  REPAYMENT_LOAN            -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  UPDATE_LOAN               -> 403 refused       route admitted them\n  DEPOSIT_SAVINGSACCOUNT    -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  UPDATE_SAVINGSACCOUNT     -> 403 refused       route admitted them\n\nThe action gates on the buttons were already right, so the two layers\ndisagreed: the only control the loan screen offered a disburser led to\nAccess Denied, and an editor was led into a form that could only 403.\n\ndata.permissions now also accepts a function of the route''s params, so a\ndispatch route resolves the code from :type or :command. The 26 codes in\ncommand-permissions.ts were each confirmed against a running Fineract at\nthe endpoint the form actually posts to -- they are not derivable from\nthe command names: withdrawnByClient needs WITHDRAW_LOAN, waiveinterest\nneeds WAIVEINTERESTPORTION_LOAN, close-rescheduled needs\nCLOSEASRESCHEDULED_LOAN, and prepayLoan needs REPAYMENT_LOAN because a\nprepayment is a repayment.\n\nFour commands are deliberately left unmapped, because the probe gave no\nclean answer and a guessed code refuses a user the platform would allow\n-- the more damaging and less visible half of this bug.\nundoContractTermination and reAmortize answer 403 at the endpoint the\nform uses and 400 at the other shape; undowriteoff answers 503;\npostInterestAsOn is refused for both its apparent code and the one the\nroute used to declare. Those fall through to no client-side gate, the\nsame position the products action dispatch route is already in.\n\nOffice transactions (#665) turned out to need the opposite of what that\nissue proposed. READ_OFFICETRANSACTION does nothing for either endpoint:\n\n  READ_OFFICE alone            -> GET /officetransactions 200\n  READ_OFFICETRANSACTION alone -> 403\n  READ_CLIENT alone (control)  -> 403\n\nSo requiring both codes -- the issue''s recommendation -- would still\nrefuse a READ_OFFICE holder the platform serves. The list route and its\nnav entry now declare READ_OFFICE. The create route declares both, since\nGET /officetransactions/template is also refused without READ_OFFICE, so\na holder of the create code alone reached a form whose office picker\ncould never populate.\n\ncheck-route-permissions.mjs learns the dynamic form, with a PER_COMMAND\nregistry mirroring UNRESTRICTED: a dispatch route has to be recorded with\nits reason to be accepted, and the script reads the map it names and\nfails if it is missing or empty. Verified by mutation -- renaming the\nidentifier, pointing the registry at a map that does not exist, and\nemptying the map each produce a distinct failure.","tree":{"sha":"177150e16e482e8570ee013ff2f8a4a32ab6fa7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/177150e16e482e8570ee013ff2f8a4a32ab6fa7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/a3004df1b11b979cfb11f8dc6dd32781da5b13da","verification":{"payload":"tree 177150e16e482e8570ee013ff2f8a4a32ab6fa7a\nparent b6cc8f2f87ad1ca223cb10d8d3c63d77da97e0ae\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791045021 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791048165 +0530\n\nfix(rbac): gate transaction routes on the code each command needs\n\nCloses #691. Closes #665.\n\nThree dispatch routes declared one permission for many commands, and the\ncode they named was not one Fineract accepts for any of them.\n\n  /loans/:loanId/transactions/:type              UPDATE_LOAN\n  /products/savings-accounts/.../:command        UPDATE_SAVINGSACCOUNT\n\nBoth are in Fineract''s `portfolio` grouping while the commands they serve\nare in `transaction_loan` and `transaction_savings`. Measured with an\nempty body, which separates authorisation from validation without\nwriting anything:\n\n  DISBURSE_LOAN             -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  REPAYMENT_LOAN            -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  UPDATE_LOAN               -> 403 refused       route admitted them\n  DEPOSIT_SAVINGSACCOUNT    -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  WITHDRAWAL_SAVINGSACCOUNT -> 400 authorised    route refused them\n  UPDATE_SAVINGSACCOUNT     -> 403 refused       route admitted them\n\nThe action gates on the buttons were already right, so the two layers\ndisagreed: the only control the loan screen offered a disburser led to\nAccess Denied, and an editor was led into a form that could only 403.\n\ndata.permissions now also accepts a function of the route''s params, so a\ndispatch route resolves the code from :type or :command. The 26 codes in\ncommand-permissions.ts were each confirmed against a running Fineract at\nthe endpoint the form actually posts to -- they are not derivable from\nthe command names: withdrawnByClient needs WITHDRAW_LOAN, waiveinterest\nneeds WAIVEINTERESTPORTION_LOAN, close-rescheduled needs\nCLOSEASRESCHEDULED_LOAN, and prepayLoan needs REPAYMENT_LOAN because a\nprepayment is a repayment.\n\nFour commands are deliberately left unmapped, because the probe gave no\nclean answer and a guessed code refuses a user the platform would allow\n-- the more damaging and less visible half of this bug.\nundoContractTermination and reAmortize answer 403 at the endpoint the\nform uses and 400 at the other shape; undowriteoff answers 503;\npostInterestAsOn is refused for both its apparent code and the one the\nroute used to declare. Those fall through to no client-side gate, the\nsame position the products action dispatch route is already in.\n\nOffice transactions (#665) turned out to need the opposite of what that\nissue proposed. READ_OFFICETRANSACTION does nothing for either endpoint:\n\n  READ_OFFICE alone            -> GET /officetransactions 200\n  READ_OFFICETRANSACTION alone -> 403\n  READ_CLIENT alone (control)  -> 403\n\nSo requiring both codes -- the issue''s recommendation -- would still\nrefuse a READ_OFFICE holder the platform serves. The list route and its\nnav entry now declare READ_OFFICE. The create route declares both, since\nGET /officetransactions/template is also refused without READ_OFFICE, so\na holder of the create code alone reached a form whose office picker\ncould never populate.\n\ncheck-route-permissions.mjs learns the dynamic form, with a PER_COMMAND\nregistry mirroring UNRESTRICTED: a dispatch route has to be recorded with\nits reason to be accepted, and the script reads the map it names and\nfails if it is missing or empty. Verified by mutation -- renaming the\nidentifier, pointing the registry at a map that does not exist, and\nemptying the map each produce a distinct failure.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasE55QAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzZq7AQDc3Yw//EXSVjrKb7aA6mdQQ6lOQ2CDvLJrEauIeZ/oUAEAwKSDl1y1ycqc\ngCLyl5SnSzWfP1fmPD6h9eQFftyW7wE=\n=wxZ9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:24:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://