d22437"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/62882e8e4a959410fb59918b645c8fc41d0c7ffb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T15:49:26Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T15:49:26Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"test(e2e): assert refused loan actions as disabled, not absent\n\nThe first draft of the non-admin spec expected a refused Approve or\nDisburse button to be absent. It is not, and should not be:\nappRequiresPermission disables the control and names the missing code\non it, while the sibling appHasPermission removes the element. The\ndirective documents why the two differ, and the reasoning holds — an\naction on the record on screen is a fact about the user''s role that\nthey need in order to act on it, so hiding the button would leave them\nto conclude the feature is missing.\n\nSo the assertions now check for the refusal marker (the\napp-requires-permission class, aria-disabled, and the reason naming\nthe code) rather than for an empty locator, which would have been\nasserting the wrong design.\n\nTwo locator hazards worth recording, both found by running this:\n\n  - Ionic hoists host aria-* into ion-button''s shadow root, so the\n    accessible name the directive binds is not on the element a\n    data-testid resolves to. The reason is read off `title` instead.\n    Same shape as the folded name ionSelect() documents.\n  - Ionic does not reflect ion-checkbox''s `name` onto the host either\n    — it goes into a hidden input.aux-input — so the permission matrix\n    is addressed by accessible name with `exact`, which also stops\n    READ_LOAN from matching READ_LOANPRODUCT.\n\nAdds data-testid=\"loan-disburse-action\", which the button lacked.\nWithout it there is no stable locator for a refused Disburse: the\ndirective replaces the accessible name with the reason in exactly the\nstate a permission test needs.\n\nWith these, all nine cases pass and both halves of #691 are confirmed\nagainst a real platform: a DISBURSE_LOAN holder is offered the control\nand refused the route, and an UPDATE_LOAN holder is admitted to a form\nthe platform will refuse.","tree":{"sha":"f017194157865d67bd40067f923fe7aa171f9570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/f017194157865d67bd40067f923fe7aa171f9570"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/62882e8e4a959410fb59918b645c8fc41d0c7ffb","verification":{"payload":"tree f017194157865d67bd40067f923fe7aa171f9570\nparent 5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791042566 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791042566 +0530\n\ntest(e2e): assert refused loan actions as disabled, not absent\n\nThe first draft of the non-admin spec expected a refused Approve or\nDisburse button to be absent. It is not, and should not be:\nappRequiresPermission disables the control and names the missing code\non it, while the sibling appHasPermission removes the element. The\ndirective documents why the two differ, and the reasoning holds — an\naction on the record on screen is a fact about the user''s role that\nthey need in order to act on it, so hiding the button would leave them\nto conclude the feature is missing.\n\nSo the assertions now check for the refusal marker (the\napp-requires-permission class, aria-disabled, and the reason naming\nthe code) rather than for an empty locator, which would have been\nasserting the wrong design.\n\nTwo locator hazards worth recording, both found by running this:\n\n  - Ionic hoists host aria-* into ion-button''s shadow root, so the\n    accessible name the directive binds is not on the element a\n    data-testid resolves to. The reason is read off `title` instead.\n    Same shape as the folded name ionSelect() documents.\n  - Ionic does not reflect ion-checkbox''s `name` onto the host either\n    — it goes into a hidden input.aux-input — so the permission matrix\n    is addressed by accessible name with `exact`, which also stops\n    READ_LOAN from matching READ_LOANPRODUCT.\n\nAdds data-testid=\"loan-disburse-action\", which the button lacked.\nWithout it there is no stable locator for a refused Disburse: the\ndirective replaces the accessible name with the reason in exactly the\nstate a permission test needs.\n\nWith these, all nine cases pass and both halves of #691 are confirmed\nagainst a real platform: a DISBURSE_LOAN holder is offered the control\nand refused the route, and an UPDATE_LOAN holder is admitted to a form\nthe platform will refuse.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasEkBgAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzbgOAP92XZTm6MweLkfYnl/z3x2xxgfiZjW+wzuIN8oekbhbkQEA/BQw0tIGu+oe\nAhta54/kj4A811ukZz4oOqhiGOKMTwk=\n=vnvE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T15:49:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/62882e8e4a959410fb59918b645c8fc41d0c7ffb","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDYyODgyZThlNGE5NTk0MTBmYjU5OTE4YjY0NWM4ZmM0MWQwYzdmZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c","sha":"5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c"}],"sha":"62882e8e4a959410fb59918b645c8fc41d0c7ffb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/62882e8e4a959410fb59918b645c8fc41d0c7ffb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T15:39:04Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T15:39:04Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"fix(security): send permission codes in Fineract''s own spelling\n\nThe role permission matrix could not save. Fineract publishes five\npermission codes with a trailing space, and READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION\nexists only in that form:\n\n    \"CREATE_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"   \"DELETE_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"\n    \"READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"     \"UPDATE_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"\n    \"READ_ClientSummary \"\n\nrole-form trimmed each code on the way in, which is right -- every\nroute''s data.permissions uses the trimmed spelling, and DOCS/RBAC.md\nrecords that a gate on READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION is unsatisfiable\nwithout the trim. It then sent the trimmed keys back, and because the\npayload is the whole code-to-boolean map, the request failed for every\nrole and every administrator whatever was ticked:\n\n    PUT /roles/153/permissions -> 404\n    \"Permission with Code READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION does not exist\"\n\nNothing caught it: the component spec mocks the call, its fixture had\nno padded code, and every RBAC e2e spec grants permissions over HTTP\nthrough seed-api.ts rather than through this screen.\n\nROLE_API''s RolePermission now carries both spellings -- code as the\nplatform sends it, label trimmed -- and setPermissions takes typed\nselections rather than a code-keyed map, so passing the display\nspelling is unreachable rather than merely discouraged.\n\nAlso puts roles and users behind contracts (ROLE_API, USER_API),\nclearing six files and dropping local/no-generated-api-import from 435\nto 429. The migration removed three casts the generated types never\nneeded: permissionUsageData through Record<string, unknown> (it is\ntyped), allowedOffices likewise (which is how office[''id''] escaped\nstrictTemplates), and selectedRoles.map(r => r.id!), where an\nundefined id silently revoked a role on the next save.\n\nAdds e2e/loan-flows-non-admin-roles.spec.ts: the loan lifecycle across\nfour separated duties -- officer, approver, disburser, repayment --\nwith every role, grant and account created by filling the forms rather\nthan seeded. That is what found this bug, and it covers Fineract''s\ntransaction_loan grouping, which the suite had no coverage of.","tree":{"sha":"31d4613b9dfa2a8d5a303195261ffd2b6240238f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/31d4613b9dfa2a8d5a303195261ffd2b6240238f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c","verification":{"payload":"tree 31d4613b9dfa2a8d5a303195261ffd2b6240238f\nparent 89f914801795dabd9f3eddeb2e74a3c5e48bf11a\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791041944 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1791041944 +0530\n\nfix(security): send permission codes in Fineract''s own spelling\n\nThe role permission matrix could not save. Fineract publishes five\npermission codes with a trailing space, and READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION\nexists only in that form:\n\n    \"CREATE_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"   \"DELETE_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"\n    \"READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"     \"UPDATE_STANDINGINSTRUCTION \"\n    \"READ_ClientSummary \"\n\nrole-form trimmed each code on the way in, which is right -- every\nroute''s data.permissions uses the trimmed spelling, and DOCS/RBAC.md\nrecords that a gate on READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION is unsatisfiable\nwithout the trim. It then sent the trimmed keys back, and because the\npayload is the whole code-to-boolean map, the request failed for every\nrole and every administrator whatever was ticked:\n\n    PUT /roles/153/permissions -> 404\n    \"Permission with Code READ_STANDINGINSTRUCTION does not exist\"\n\nNothing caught it: the component spec mocks the call, its fixture had\nno padded code, and every RBAC e2e spec grants permissions over HTTP\nthrough seed-api.ts rather than through this screen.\n\nROLE_API''s RolePermission now carries both spellings -- code as the\nplatform sends it, label trimmed -- and setPermissions takes typed\nselections rather than a code-keyed map, so passing the display\nspelling is unreachable rather than merely discouraged.\n\nAlso puts roles and users behind contracts (ROLE_API, USER_API),\nclearing six files and dropping local/no-generated-api-import from 435\nto 429. The migration removed three casts the generated types never\nneeded: permissionUsageData through Record<string, unknown> (it is\ntyped), allowedOffices likewise (which is how office[''id''] escaped\nstrictTemplates), and selectedRoles.map(r => r.id!), where an\nundefined id silently revoked a role on the next save.\n\nAdds e2e/loan-flows-non-admin-roles.spec.ts: the loan lifecycle across\nfour separated duties -- officer, approver, disburser, repayment --\nwith every role, grant and account created by filling the forms rather\nthan seeded. That is what found this bug, and it covers Fineract''s\ntransaction_loan grouping, which the suite had no coverage of.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCasEhmAAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzevvAQClzDNq8l55IP8R3Rlm95l1wk6QORvtNoXYQyQtSPjwdQEAwAHYCh+Ln98l\nB6aYL6sKbxuByou96ktp3QhMGaNdwwM=\n=17vI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T15:39:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDVlZTM4YjI5OTA3NzhlNmVlMjMyODdlMDc1NmI5MDJjY2ZlZjE1NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/89f914801795dabd9f3eddeb2e74a3c5e48bf11a","sha":"89f914801795dabd9f3eddeb2e74a3c5e48bf11a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/89f914801795dabd9f3eddeb2e74a3c5e48bf11a"}],"sha":"5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/5ee38b2990778e6ee23287e0756b902ccfef155c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://ap