ollowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/9a5f7d4d2677f345e07bd38ea3bee8b9a763e67c","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDlhNWY3ZDRkMjY3N2YzNDVlMDdiZDM4ZWEzYmVlOGI5YTc2M2U2N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/3e32f1c0a6ee22a62528752d5a8b8e20a30db331","sha":"3e32f1c0a6ee22a62528752d5a8b8e20a30db331","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/3e32f1c0a6ee22a62528752d5a8b8e20a30db331"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/40a699ae3dc555c295423a88e163535d7f6a7ec8","sha":"40a699ae3dc555c295423a88e163535d7f6a7ec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/40a699ae3dc555c295423a88e163535d7f6a7ec8"}],"sha":"9a5f7d4d2677f345e07bd38ea3bee8b9a763e67c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/9a5f7d4d2677f345e07bd38ea3bee8b9a763e67c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/40a699ae3dc555c295423a88e163535d7f6a7ec8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T17:38:57Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T17:38:57Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"refactor(organization): put staff and holidays behind API contracts\n\nAdds STAFF_API and HOLIDAY_API, gives OFFICE_API the get/create/update its own doc\ncomment said to add once a caller existed, and migrates 14 files. Offices, staff and\nholidays are one domain in Fineract''s model - all three are scoped by office - so they\nmove together. The no-generated-api-import baseline falls from 458 to 444.\n\nEvery disagreement below was verified against a running apache/fineract.\n\nStaff fixes a display defect. staff-form read GET /staff/{id}''s joiningDate through\nformatArrayDate(), which answers the literal string ''-'' for anything that is not a\n[y, m, d] array - and this endpoint sends a string:\n\n    GET /staff/1  -> \"joiningDate\":\"2020-01-01\"     string\n    GET /offices  -> \"openingDate\":[2009,1,1]       array\n\nSo the staff edit form showed a dash where the joining date should be. The control is\ndisabled in edit mode and onSubmit() does not send it, so nothing was persisted\nwrongly. Its spec passed throughout on a fixture that invented [2026, 1, 5].\n\nThe lesson is not \"trust the generated type\": StaffData declares joiningDate as a\nstring and is correct. It is that a screen cannot tell from the type which encoding it\nis getting, and should not have to. toIsoFineractDate accepts both.\n\nHolidays are the familiar direction, three times over. GetHolidaysResponse declares\nfromDate, toDate and repaymentsRescheduledTo as string and all three arrive as arrays;\ndescription and reschedulingType are sent and never declared, so the form recovered the\nrescheduling rule by checking whether a reschedule date happened to be set. And\nPutHolidaysHolidayIdRequest declares only name and description while the endpoint\naccepts everything the form sends - the PUT answers with the dates in its `changes`\nblock - so the form cast a Record<string, unknown> to a type that declared none of it.\n\nThat domain is where the duplication is clearest. Before this, toIsoFineractDate''s\nlogic existed in five places: the shared helper, formatArrayDate in\ncore/utils/date-formatter.ts, a local formatArrayDate method on holidays-list, and\npickerDate in holiday-form - the same function rewritten line for line. Two of those\nare gone here.\n\nTwo transport concerns moved off their screens. Blank optional text fields: sending\nmobileNo: '''' is not an omission, Fineract rejects the whole submission with \"mobileNo\nmust contain only digits\", and staff-form carried a withoutBlanks() helper for it. And\nOfficeApi.create answers the new office''s id, because create-office-dialog dismisses\nwith it so the form that opened it can select the office just created.\n\nVerification: 1922 unit tests pass (285 files, 54 new). Lint and prettier clean.\nSix mutations applied and killed: dropping the string branch of the staff joining\ndate, sending blanks instead of omitting them, deriving a holiday''s isPending from the\nwrong field, sending a reschedule date under the rule that forbids one, dropping the\ndateFormat Fineract parses the opening date against, and discarding the id a create\nanswers.\n\nThat last one survived the first mutation run. The dialog''s own spec mocks the\ncontract, so a create() that answered nothing was invisible to it; it took an\nadapter-level test to catch, and that test is in this commit.\n\nOne self-inflicted bug worth recording: holiday.api.ts imports its adapter for the\ninjection-token factory, so the adapter importing RESCHEDULING_TYPE - a value - back\nfrom the contract closed a runtime cycle and every one of the 285 spec files failed to\nload. The other contracts only ever get types back, which erase. The constant now\nlives in holiday-rescheduling-type.ts, which imports nothing.","tree":{"sha":"c251c613c6f3eac95496d95524fa3def4b0860da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/c251c613c6f3eac95496d95524fa3def4b0860da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/40a699ae3dc555c295423a88e163535d7f6a7ec8","verification":{"payload":"tree c251c613c6f3eac95496d95524fa3def4b0860da\nparent 3e32f1c0a6ee22a62528752d5a8b8e20a30db331\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790962737 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790962737 +0530\n\nrefactor(organization): put staff and holidays behind API contracts\n\nAdds STAFF_API and HOLIDAY_API, gives OFFICE_API the get/create/update its own doc\ncomment said to add once a caller existed, and migrates 14 files. Offices, staff and\nholidays are one domain in Fineract''s model - all three are scoped by office - so they\nmove together. The no-generated-api-import baseline falls from 458 to 444.\n\nEvery disagreement below was verified against a running apache/fineract.\n\nStaff fixes a display defect. staff-form read GET /staff/{id}''s joiningDate through\nformatArrayDate(), which answers the literal string ''-'' for anything that is not a\n[y, m, d] array - and this endpoint sends a string:\n\n    GET /staff/1  -> \"joiningDate\":\"2020-01-01\"     string\n    GET /offices  -> \"openingDate\":[2009,1,1]       array\n\nSo the staff edit form showed a dash where the joining date should be. The control is\ndisabled in edit mode and onSubmit() does not send it, so nothing was persisted\nwrongly. Its spec passed throughout on a fixture that invented [2026, 1, 5].\n\nThe lesson is not \"trust the generated type\": StaffData declares joiningDate as a\nstring and is correct. It is that a screen cannot tell from the type which encoding it\nis getting, and should not have to. toIsoFineractDate accepts both.\n\nHolidays are the familiar direction, three times over. GetHolidaysResponse declares\nfromDate, toDate and repaymentsRescheduledTo as string and all three arrive as arrays;\ndescription and reschedulingType are sent and never declared, so the form recovered the\nrescheduling rule by checking whether a reschedule date happened to be set. And\nPutHolidaysHolidayIdRequest declares only name and description while the endpoint\naccepts everything the form sends - the PUT answers with the dates in its `changes`\nblock - so the form cast a Record<string, unknown> to a type that declared none of it.\n\nThat domain is where the duplication is clearest. Before this, toIsoFineractDate''s\nlogic existed in five places: the shared helper, formatArrayDate in\ncore/utils/date-formatter.ts, a local formatArrayDate method on holidays-list, and\npickerDate in holiday-form - the same function rewritten line for line. Two of those\nare gone here.\n\nTwo transport concerns moved off their screens. Blank optional text fields: sending\nmobileNo: '''' is not an omission, Fineract rejects the whole submission with \"mobileNo\nmust contain only digits\", and staff-form carried a withoutBlanks() helper for it. And\nOfficeApi.create answers the new office''s id, because create-office-dialog dismisses\nwith it so the form that opened it can select the office just created.\n\nVerification: 1922 unit tests pass (285 files, 54 new). Lint and prettier clean.\nSix mutations applied and killed: dropping the string branch of the staff joining\ndate, sending blanks instead of omitting them, deriving a holiday''s isPending from the\nwrong field, sending a reschedule date under the rule that forbids one, dropping the\ndateFormat Fineract parses the opening date against, and discarding the id a create\nanswers.\n\nThat last one survived the first mutation run. The dialog''s own spec mocks the\ncontract, so a create() that answered nothing was invisible to it; it took an\nadapter-level test to catch, and that test is in this commit.\n\nOne self-inflicted bug worth recording: holiday.api.ts imports its adapter for the\ninjection-token factory, so the adapter importing RESCHEDULING_TYPE - a value - back\nfrom the contract closed a runtime cycle and every one of the 285 spec files failed to\nload. The other contracts only ever get types back, which erase. The constant now\nlives in holiday-rescheduling-type.ts, which imports nothing.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCar/sMQAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzZwxAQDoRE/B1ki+wMRnSo/gsAd4eEAo9dg2ivtQ0TeizOuK8QD/YVf+I3hgLvqk\nObhHkqJfRRQq7k1DihHPGEzN68o+vAo=\n=F2Na\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T17:39:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organiza