T16:32:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/c7d4f153a20eb9045ce1045da4d546371a11c4ef","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKGM3ZDRmMTUzYTIwZWI5MDQ1Y2UxMDQ1ZGE0ZDU0NjM3MWExMWM0ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575","sha":"3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520","sha":"0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520"}],"sha":"c7d4f153a20eb9045ce1045da4d546371a11c4ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/c7d4f153a20eb9045ce1045da4d546371a11c4ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T15:54:20Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T15:59:39Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"refactor(loans): put loan and loan-transaction behind API contracts\n\nAdds LOAN_API and LOAN_TRANSACTION_API under the ADR 0006 boundary and migrates the\nfour files that can move without cascading into loan-view: the loans list, the\ntransaction detail dialog, the chargeback dialog and the dialogs'' shared spec.\nThe no-generated-api-import baseline falls from 462 to 458.\n\nEach disagreement below was verified against a running apache/fineract, not read\noff the spec.\n\nGetLoansLoanIdStatus does not declare `value`, which every loan status carries, and\ndoes declare `description`, which no payload sends. The loans list compared that\nundeclared field against English display text to decide which actions to offer:\n\n    @if (loan.status?.value === ''Approved'') { ... offers Disburse ... }\n\n`value` comes from a localisable enum, so a platform serving any other locale\noffered neither Approve nor Disburse and said nothing about why. Nothing caught it:\nthe buttons sit in an <ng-template appCellTemplate> whose let-loan context is `any`,\nso strictTemplates never checked a field the generated model does not declare. The\ngates now read Fineract''s own flags, pendingApproval and waitingForDisbursal.\n\nTransactions show the same problem twice. The generated client has two types for one\npayload - GetLoansLoanIdLoanTransactionEnumData declares `value`, GetLoansType does\nnot - and `date` is declared string on both while arriving as [2026, 10, 2]. The\ndetail dialog converted that date twice, two different ways, each through a cast or\nan `unknown`, and reached the type label through a Record<string, unknown> cast with\na three-way fallback. GetPaymentTypeOptions likewise omits the `codeName` the\nchargeback dialog selects its default payment type by; that lookup does work today,\nwhich is the point - nothing was checking whether it still would.\n\nAlso recorded, not fixed here: the loans list passes its search box to Fineract''s\naccountNo parameter, which is an exact match. accountNo=000000053 returns the loan;\naccountNo=0000 and accountNo=E2E return nothing. GET /loans has no free-text\nparameter to point it at, so correcting that needs a product decision. LoanQuery\nnames the field accountNo so the next caller does not assume otherwise.\n\ntoIsoFineractDate moves to fineract-date.ts now that two adapters convert inbound\ndates; a second copy would be a second place for the month base to be wrong.\n\nVerification: 1874 unit tests pass (282 files, 30 new). Eight mutations killed -\ndropping waitingForDisbursal, misplacing accountNo in the positional argument list,\nreverting displayName to the generated type''s phantom field, dropping codeName,\ndropping the dateFormat the platform parses against, and restoring the original\nEnglish-text gates. That last one failed exactly one test, the non-English-locale\ncase, while the four English-status tests still passed, which is the discrimination\nthe fix is about.","tree":{"sha":"93207e364e050969c94898f86f10175cc30d0f7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/93207e364e050969c94898f86f10175cc30d0f7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520","verification":{"payload":"tree 93207e364e050969c94898f86f10175cc30d0f7f\nparent 3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790956460 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790956779 +0530\n\nrefactor(loans): put loan and loan-transaction behind API contracts\n\nAdds LOAN_API and LOAN_TRANSACTION_API under the ADR 0006 boundary and migrates the\nfour files that can move without cascading into loan-view: the loans list, the\ntransaction detail dialog, the chargeback dialog and the dialogs'' shared spec.\nThe no-generated-api-import baseline falls from 462 to 458.\n\nEach disagreement below was verified against a running apache/fineract, not read\noff the spec.\n\nGetLoansLoanIdStatus does not declare `value`, which every loan status carries, and\ndoes declare `description`, which no payload sends. The loans list compared that\nundeclared field against English display text to decide which actions to offer:\n\n    @if (loan.status?.value === ''Approved'') { ... offers Disburse ... }\n\n`value` comes from a localisable enum, so a platform serving any other locale\noffered neither Approve nor Disburse and said nothing about why. Nothing caught it:\nthe buttons sit in an <ng-template appCellTemplate> whose let-loan context is `any`,\nso strictTemplates never checked a field the generated model does not declare. The\ngates now read Fineract''s own flags, pendingApproval and waitingForDisbursal.\n\nTransactions show the same problem twice. The generated client has two types for one\npayload - GetLoansLoanIdLoanTransactionEnumData declares `value`, GetLoansType does\nnot - and `date` is declared string on both while arriving as [2026, 10, 2]. The\ndetail dialog converted that date twice, two different ways, each through a cast or\nan `unknown`, and reached the type label through a Record<string, unknown> cast with\na three-way fallback. GetPaymentTypeOptions likewise omits the `codeName` the\nchargeback dialog selects its default payment type by; that lookup does work today,\nwhich is the point - nothing was checking whether it still would.\n\nAlso recorded, not fixed here: the loans list passes its search box to Fineract''s\naccountNo parameter, which is an exact match. accountNo=000000053 returns the loan;\naccountNo=0000 and accountNo=E2E return nothing. GET /loans has no free-text\nparameter to point it at, so correcting that needs a product decision. LoanQuery\nnames the field accountNo so the next caller does not assume otherwise.\n\ntoIsoFineractDate moves to fineract-date.ts now that two adapters convert inbound\ndates; a second copy would be a second place for the month base to be wrong.\n\nVerification: 1874 unit tests pass (282 files, 30 new). Eight mutations killed -\ndropping waitingForDisbursal, misplacing accountNo in the positional argument list,\nreverting displayName to the generated type''s phantom field, dropping codeName,\ndropping the dateFormat the platform parses against, and restoring the original\nEnglish-text gates. That last one failed exactly one test, the non-English-locale\ncase, while the four English-status tests still passed, which is the discrimination\nthe fix is about.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCar/U6wAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzQ0vAP9AQESIGKmJiQeGDpsQf9ALveWvqYRzID6bS8gVyJlGywD7BXzOB9fEJKAX\ng+S/e2XR1RvlK4Am6i6q/m8DEi8hqQ4=\n=45bt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T16:04:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDBhZjllMTYzNzJlYjQyOGM0Yjg5NTA0NjAxYTdmMWM2NzFhY2Q1MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575","sha":"3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575"}],"sha":"0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/0af9e16372eb428c4b89504601a7f1c671acd520"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/5fe19cc7750c4c7b8e6de94c50d6da36071e4e99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:53:07Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T15:57:48Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"test(e2e): cover the collection sheet filter against a real Fineract\n\nThe unit tests drive the component through mocked HTTP. This drives the screen\nin a browser against the platform, which is where two of the three defects\nactually lived.\n\n  - Staff is scoped to the office. The select stays disabled until an office is\n    chosen, and GET /staff?officeId=N is what fills it.\n  - The chosen staff member reaches the wire. This reads the outgoing request\n    body rather than the form, because the form was never the broken part:\n    staffId was collected and then dropped by buildBody(), so the control\n    looked and behaved correctly while doing nothing.\n  - An empty sheet reports itself. Nothing is due on a seeded instance with no\n    meeting calendars, so Generate exercises the branch that used to render the\n    word \"null\" with a live Save button under it. Save is asserted absent and\n    Back present.\n\nMutation tested. Dropping staffId from buildBody() again fails on exactly the\nmissing field:\n\n    Object {\n      \"officeId\": 1,\n  -   \"staffId\": 15,\n    }\n\nwhich is the assertion that matters here, since the defect was invisible from\nthe UI: the dropdown populated, an officer could be picked, the form submitted\nand a result came back.\n\nUses the shared selectOption() helper rather than hand-rolling the overlay\ninteraction. These selects are interface=\"popover\", which commits on click and\nhas no OK button, so a hand-rolled click-radio-then-OK sequence waits for a\nbutton that never exists.\n\nThe populated-sheet path is deliberately absent: it needs a group with a\nmeeting calendar and repayments falling on the meeting date, and the shape\nFineract returns is not the one the generated client declares. See #670.","tree":{"sha":"cb97f0b6b35dca6c5c3f9ea59c16db267a610b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/cb97f0b6b35dca6c5c3f9ea59c16db267a610b30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/5fe19cc7750c4c7b8e6de94c50d6da36071e4e99","verification":{"payload":"tree cb97f0b6b35dca6c5c3f9ea59c16db267a610b30\nparent 3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790952787 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790956668 +0530\n\ntest(e2e): cover the collection sheet filter against a real Fineract\n\nThe unit tests drive the component through mocked HTTP. This drives the screen\nin a browser against the platform, which is where two of the three defects\nactually lived.\n\n  - Staff is scoped to the office. The select stays disabled until an office is\n    chosen, and GET /staff?officeId=N is what fills it.\n  - The chosen staff member reaches the wire. This reads the outgoing request\n    body rather than the form, because the form was never the broken part:\n    staffId was collected and then dropped by buildBody(), so the control\n    looked and behaved correctly while doing nothing.\n  - An empty sheet reports itself. Nothing is due on a seeded instance with no\n    meeting calendars, so Generate exercises the branch that used to render the\n    word \"null\" with a live Save button under it. Save is asserted absent and\n    Back present.\n\nMutation tested. Dropping staffId from buildBody() again fails on exactly the\nmissing field:\n\n    Object {\n      \"officeId\": 1,\n  -   \"staffId\": 15,\n    }\n\nwhich is the assertion that matters here, since the defect was invisible from\nthe UI: the dropdown populated, an officer could be picked, the form submitted\nand a result came back.\n\nUses the shared selectOption() helper rather than hand-rolling the overlay\ninteraction. These selects are interface=\"popover\", which commits on click and\nhas no OK button, so a hand-rolled click-radio-then-OK sequence waits for a\nbutton that never exists.\n\nThe populated-sheet path is deliberately absent: it needs a group with a\nmeeting calendar and repayments falling on the meeting date, and the shape\nFineract returns is not the one the generated client declares. See #670.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCar/UfAAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzYdmAQDrqIDemAGAEJ/0J6/I4z0UXSzJhw2MxCsoGK2sUB5d8AD+JfmpJHjGftUj\nUxFcYucG/VNrxT0PneduvAZIUnvjjgw=\n=aqIZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T15:59:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/5fe19cc7750c4c7b8e6de94c50d6da36071e4e99","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKDVmZTE5Y2M3NzUwYzRjN2I4ZTZkZTk0YzUwZDZkYTM2MDcxZTRlOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575","sha":"3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/3e50a62647faa404ae6fe0ba64224926ad652575"}],"sha":"5fe19cc7750c4c7b8e6de94c50d6da36071e4e99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/5fe19cc7750c4c7b8e6de94c50d6da36071e4e99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User