lse,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/e69015664777020d6c72d88dacf166f405882a71","node_id":"C_kwDORYqbY9oAKGU2OTAxNTY2NDc3NzAyMGQ2YzcyZDg4ZGFjZjE2NmY0MDU4ODJhNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/6fcff6f40e58b093cf2e54886b2442d227ca91b1","sha":"6fcff6f40e58b093cf2e54886b2442d227ca91b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/6fcff6f40e58b093cf2e54886b2442d227ca91b1"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commit/461f270236edc53fd2b4c310358a009eae193860","sha":"461f270236edc53fd2b4c310358a009eae193860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/461f270236edc53fd2b4c310358a009eae193860"}],"sha":"e69015664777020d6c72d88dacf166f405882a71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/e69015664777020d6c72d88dacf166f405882a71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32237955?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aman-Mittal","id":32237955,"login":"Aman-Mittal","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjM3OTU1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aman-Mittal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/commits/330064d6c4e948d47b2a487655907f0ba09b3fab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:45:06Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T14:45:06Z","email":"aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com","name":"Aman Mittal"},"message":"test(e2e): pin the transaction controls to the states the platform accepts\n\n#667 withheld the loan Repayment button and the savings Deposit and Withdraw\nbuttons unless the record is in a state the platform will act on. That landed\nwith unit tests over a stubbed loan and account, and nothing against the\nplatform that defines the rule — so a future template edit could reintroduce\neither defect and every check would stay green.\n\nTwo backend specs, each with two halves that fail for different reasons:\n\n  - A walk through the states. A loan awaiting approval offers no Repayment;\n    approved and awaiting disbursal, still none; active, it is back. A savings\n    account awaiting approval offers neither Deposit nor Withdraw; activated,\n    both return. Each negative assertion is paired with a control on the same\n    screen — the Approve button — so a screen that simply failed to render\n    cannot pass the test.\n\n  - A direct probe of the platform rule, so the gate is pinned to the behaviour\n    it mirrors rather than to itself:\n\n      POST /loans/{id}/transactions?command=repayment\n        400 error.msg.loan.must.be.active.fully.paid.or.overpaid\n      POST /savingsaccounts/{id}/transactions?command=deposit\n        400 error.msg.savingsaccount.transaction.account.is.not.active\n\n    Without these the specs would still pass if Fineract began accepting those\n    commands, at which point the gates would be wrong rather than right.\n\nBoth were mutation tested before being trusted. Reintroducing each defect\nfailed exactly the assertion that describes it:\n\n  getByTestId(''loan-repayment-action'')   expected 0, received 1\n  getByTestId(''savings-deposit-action'')  expected 0, received 1\n\nand in both runs the API probe kept passing while the UI assertion failed,\nwhich is the division of labour working: a probe alone would have looked\nthorough and caught nothing.\n\nSeeding gains seedSubmittedLoan and seedSubmittedSavingsAccount, which stop\nbefore approval, plus approveLoan, disburseLoan and activateSavingsAccount so a\nspec can watch a record change state. seedActiveLoan and\nseedSavingsAccountWithTransactions are rebuilt on them rather than duplicating\nthe application bodies.\n\n5 tests, all passing against a live instance. Both specs are registered in\nBACKEND_SPECS; the backend project goes from 119 tests to 123.","tree":{"sha":"caa77cb569e51d75c6f49729f49265c06d5b38b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/trees/caa77cb569e51d75c6f49729f49265c06d5b38b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/fineract-backoffice-ui/git/commits/330064d6c4e948d47b2a487655907f0ba09b3fab","verification":{"payload":"tree caa77cb569e51d75c6f49729f49265c06d5b38b6\nparent e6596a21e51ccc88574da5708b592cbab2fff0dd\nauthor Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790952306 +0530\ncommitter Aman Mittal <aman.mittal3052000@gmail.com> 1790952306 +0530\n\ntest(e2e): pin the transaction controls to the states the platform accepts\n\n#667 withheld the loan Repayment button and the savings Deposit and Withdraw\nbuttons unless the record is in a state the platform will act on. That landed\nwith unit tests over a stubbed loan and account, and nothing against the\nplatform that defines the rule — so a future template edit could reintroduce\neither defect and every check would stay green.\n\nTwo backend specs, each with two halves that fail for different reasons:\n\n  - A walk through the states. A loan awaiting approval offers no Repayment;\n    approved and awaiting disbursal, still none; active, it is back. A savings\n    account awaiting approval offers neither Deposit nor Withdraw; activated,\n    both return. Each negative assertion is paired with a control on the same\n    screen — the Approve button — so a screen that simply failed to render\n    cannot pass the test.\n\n  - A direct probe of the platform rule, so the gate is pinned to the behaviour\n    it mirrors rather than to itself:\n\n      POST /loans/{id}/transactions?command=repayment\n        400 error.msg.loan.must.be.active.fully.paid.or.overpaid\n      POST /savingsaccounts/{id}/transactions?command=deposit\n        400 error.msg.savingsaccount.transaction.account.is.not.active\n\n    Without these the specs would still pass if Fineract began accepting those\n    commands, at which point the gates would be wrong rather than right.\n\nBoth were mutation tested before being trusted. Reintroducing each defect\nfailed exactly the assertion that describes it:\n\n  getByTestId(''loan-repayment-action'')   expected 0, received 1\n  getByTestId(''savings-deposit-action'')  expected 0, received 1\n\nand in both runs the API probe kept passing while the UI assertion failed,\nwhich is the division of labour working: a probe alone would have looked\nthorough and caught nothing.\n\nSeeding gains seedSubmittedLoan and seedSubmittedSavingsAccount, which stop\nbefore approval, plus approveLoan, disburseLoan and activateSavingsAccount so a\nspec can watch a record change state. seedActiveLoan and\nseedSavingsAccountWithTransactions are rebuilt on them rather than duplicating\nthe application bodies.\n\n5 tests, all passing against a live instance. Both specs are registered in\nBACKEND_SPECS; the backend project goes from 119 tests to 123.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRMUFMGQx7zDp8s+wGPRtpRmnokzQUCar/DcgAKCRCPRtpRmnok\nzbN1AP4ks6UqqqjrJg+jfp3zRxL69