rs/KazW","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/6e44a7d3e157f38625128fcdc388575c2b465a9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T08:12:44Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T08:12:44Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"message":"chore(deps): bump passport service-auth to v0.1.0\n\nPulls in passport''s auth.NewSchemeDispatch and auth.AlwaysFail —\nthe explicit-scheme dispatch middleware. Drops the local replace\ndirective that carried us through the migration window; build now\nresolves passport from the published module proxy tag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a05fac42fe48b7582269e09c9badfe4eb7b3ac91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/trees/a05fac42fe48b7582269e09c9badfe4eb7b3ac91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/commits/6e44a7d3e157f38625128fcdc388575c2b465a9b","verification":{"payload":"tree a05fac42fe48b7582269e09c9badfe4eb7b3ac91\nparent b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298\nauthor Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776586364 -0600\ncommitter Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776586364 -0600\n\nchore(deps): bump passport service-auth to v0.1.0\n\nPulls in passport''s auth.NewSchemeDispatch and auth.AlwaysFail —\nthe explicit-scheme dispatch middleware. Drops the local replace\ndirective that carried us through the migration window; build now\nresolves passport from the published module proxy tag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/wfa09mYovkTIpmBDKaxr+x8j2\nH8LU4Ovj81kHmEUf8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMq17sAbJMFRpo7ZPPbLa/MsPnfGDBagufV8ZdIFsWkeTT7mYaC3U+bvPDcV5n1LHw\nlsJ5udS/piWSDFVuAobAc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T08:12:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/598968?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KazW","id":598968,"login":"KazW","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commit/6e44a7d3e157f38625128fcdc388575c2b465a9b","node_id":"C_kwDORY6Hf9oAKDZlNDRhN2QzZTE1N2YzODYyNTEyOGZjZGMzODg1NzVjMmI0NjVhOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commit/b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298","sha":"b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298"}],"sha":"6e44a7d3e157f38625128fcdc388575c2b465a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/6e44a7d3e157f38625128fcdc388575c2b465a9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/598968?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KazW","id":598968,"login":"KazW","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T07:50:54Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T08:11:50Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"message":"test(e2e): document scheme-dispatch invariant + assert Bearer-for-APIkey 401\n\nPassport''s middleware no longer falls through from JWT to API-key on\nparse failure (post-2026-04-19 scheme split), so the historical\nconcern about silently authenticating malformed JWTs is impossible by\nconstruction. Update the doc comment on ValidBridgeAPIKey to reflect\nthe new invariant; signJWT itself stays for inbound-middleware tests.\n\nExport ValidBridgeAPIKey (was unexported validBridgeAPIKey), add\nJWKSStub.APIKeyVerifyCount() counter (atomic int64 incremented on\nevery /v1/verify-api-key hit), and expose the stub as Daemon.JWKS\nso e2e tests can assert on verify-api-key call counts.\n\nAdds a regression-prevention e2e test that GETs /api/v1/channels\nwith a valid API-key string under \"Bearer\" and asserts 401 + zero\nverify-api-key calls. This proves the inbound middleware now rejects\nthe wrong scheme even for a string the verify-api-key endpoint would\naccept under ApiKey-v1 — the load-bearing closure of Cluster 3b at\nthe daemon boundary.\n\nAlso updates StartJWKSStub signature to return (*JWKSStub, addr,\nstop, signJWT) — harness.go updated to capture the new first value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba7f64228b4783ea758bf5082313f4de4c446953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/trees/ba7f64228b4783ea758bf5082313f4de4c446953"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/commits/b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298","verification":{"payload":"tree ba7f64228b4783ea758bf5082313f4de4c446953\nparent cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca\nauthor Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776585054 -0600\ncommitter Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776586310 -0600\n\ntest(e2e): document scheme-dispatch invariant + assert Bearer-for-APIkey 401\n\nPassport''s middleware no longer falls through from JWT to API-key on\nparse failure (post-2026-04-19 scheme split), so the historical\nconcern about silently authenticating malformed JWTs is impossible by\nconstruction. Update the doc comment on ValidBridgeAPIKey to reflect\nthe new invariant; signJWT itself stays for inbound-middleware tests.\n\nExport ValidBridgeAPIKey (was unexported validBridgeAPIKey), add\nJWKSStub.APIKeyVerifyCount() counter (atomic int64 incremented on\nevery /v1/verify-api-key hit), and expose the stub as Daemon.JWKS\nso e2e tests can assert on verify-api-key call counts.\n\nAdds a regression-prevention e2e test that GETs /api/v1/channels\nwith a valid API-key string under \"Bearer\" and asserts 401 + zero\nverify-api-key calls. This proves the inbound middleware now rejects\nthe wrong scheme even for a string the verify-api-key endpoint would\naccept under ApiKey-v1 — the load-bearing closure of Cluster 3b at\nthe daemon boundary.\n\nAlso updates StartJWKSStub signature to return (*JWKSStub, addr,\nstop, signJWT) — harness.go updated to capture the new first value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/wfa09mYovkTIpmBDKaxr+x8j2\nH8LU4Ovj81kHmEUf8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNGgPbSPbBC2VgXNKLHD+4JImfPz56sd6bwNZS/b3TBEY8fbrRLfqhLbUnrRIc68DV\nRq5HiXsmXYeObTkHyyqgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T08:12:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/598968?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KazW","id":598968,"login":"KazW","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commit/b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298","node_id":"C_kwDORY6Hf9oAKGI1ZmJkYTBlMWYwYTkzNTdiY2RmZTE2OWRhMjcxOGVjMzk4YTUyOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commit/cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca","sha":"cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca"}],"sha":"b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/b5fbda0e1f0a9357bcdfe169da2718ec398a5298"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/598968?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KazW","id":598968,"login":"KazW","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T07:40:42Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T08:11:50Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"message":"feat(mcpbridge): send API key as ApiKey-v1 on all three outbound paths\n\nRequired by passport''s scheme-dispatch middleware (Bearer is now\nJWT-only).\n\nAlso updates pkg/daemon/server.go to use auth.NewSchemeDispatch\ninstead of the removed auth.NewFromValidators (the passport branch\nreplaced the old fallthrough-based combinator with the new\nscheme-dispatch middleware as part of the same plan).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ae688c9be445964d82597136beb500298017dbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/trees/2ae688c9be445964d82597136beb500298017dbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/commits/cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ae688c9be445964d82597136beb500298017dbb\nparent f27df3ec93e6cf501cc7ae86683d029bd86691a9\nauthor Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776584442 -0600\ncommitter Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776586310 -0600\n\nfeat(mcpbridge): send API key as ApiKey-v1 on all three outbound paths\n\nRequired by passport''s scheme-dispatch middleware (Bearer is now\nJWT-only).\n\nAlso updates pkg/daemon/server.go to use auth.NewSchemeDispatch\ninstead of the removed auth.NewFromValidators (the passport branch\nreplaced the old fallthrough-based combinator with the new\nscheme-dispatch middleware as part of the same plan).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/wfa09mYovkTIpmBDKaxr+x8j2\nH8LU4Ovj81kHmEUf8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHIrKefdwWbGkv3mpP8Q1ixavuoI0huHk2EeQJy6l0oJWWaLgTXKlIeiKzKIq+0h2h\n0KRKlue2ESjfCrrzCoqAM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T08:12:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/598968?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KazW","id":598968,"login":"KazW","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commit/cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca","node_id":"C_kwDORY6Hf9oAKGNkMjYxNDY3ZGFmMWE4ZTk5MzY5OTMzOTRiODA0NmVmNmFiZTM1Y2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commit/f27df3ec93e6cf501cc7ae86683d029bd86691a9","sha":"f27df3ec93e6cf501cc7ae86683d029bd86691a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/f27df3ec93e6cf501cc7ae86683d029bd86691a9"}],"sha":"cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/cd261467daf1a8e9936993394b8046ef6abe35ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/598968?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KazW","id":598968,"login":"KazW","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk2OA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/commits/f27df3ec93e6cf501cc7ae86683d029bd86691a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T07:39:31Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T08:11:50Z","email":"me@kazatron.com","name":"Kaz Walker"},"message":"feat(client): drop WithToken; API keys travel under ApiKey-v1\n\nEvery WithToken caller in tests (rest_client_test.go ×14,\nclient_test.go ×4) is migrated to WithAPIKey; the JWT-side test\n(TestAuthHeaders) is deleted because the option no longer exists.\nThe corresponding Bearer-with-API-key assertions\n(rest_client_test.go:36-37, client_test.go:793-794) flip to ApiKey-v1.\n\nWS Dial and reconnectLoop also updated in the same commit: removing\nthe token field from clientOpts forced both call sites to be fixed\natomically. Both send ApiKey-v1 instead of Bearer.\n\nRemoving WithToken closes the latent-bug class where callers passed\na wf-svc_* API key into WithToken and accidentally got accepted via\npassport''s validator fallthrough.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"544a511293069be1d1398f4c0ca9e75a0ff0e8e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/trees/544a511293069be1d1398f4c0ca9e75a0ff0e8e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/commits/f27df3ec93e6cf501cc7ae86683d029bd86691a9","verification":{"payload":"tree 544a511293069be1d1398f4c0ca9e75a0ff0e8e7\nparent 3034931c50888f74b908fc9ea1846237370c2047\nauthor Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776584371 -0600\ncommitter Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776586310 -0600\n\nfeat(client): drop WithToken; API keys travel under ApiKey-v1\n\nEvery WithToken caller in tests (rest_client_test.go ×14,\nclient_test.go ×4) is migrated to WithAPIKey; the JWT-side test\n(TestAuthHeaders) is deleted because the option no longer exists.\nThe corresponding Bearer-with-API-key assertions\n(rest_client_test.go:36-37, client_test.go:793-794) flip to ApiKey-v1.\n\nWS Dial and reconnectLoop also updated in the same commit: removing\nthe token field from clientOpts forced both call sites to be fixed\natomically. Both send ApiKey-v1 instead of Bearer.\n\nRemoving WithToken closes the latent-bug class where callers passed\na wf-svc_* API key into WithToken and accidentally got accepted via\npassport''s validator fallthrough.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/wfa09mYovkTIpmBDKaxr+x8j2\nH8LU4Ovj81kHmEUf8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIhv1lGxLUzqqHSQsfrgohTsyNqOqh9ll0Fy4KBS5voiLhq3sHFUvYsMWvrhB20Xv9\n5+7uO6jfUXLyxcbarWcQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-19T08:12:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.github