ing for a WS dial and read-pump goroutine. The\nexisting *Client stays unchanged for realtime consumers; new surface\nis strictly additive.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b0522302f59844c9a0a9278f2d1c1237007a22e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/trees/6b0522302f59844c9a0a9278f2d1c1237007a22e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Work-Fort/Sharkfin/git/commits/0e76f79d721960b31a6c73fcb6ce9d5fef8d6c7d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b0522302f59844c9a0a9278f2d1c1237007a22e\nparent c8797ed3e934e62311e91aebf19df5638f07b8a5\nauthor Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776551864 -0600\ncommitter Kaz Walker <me@kazatron.com> 1776552125 -0600\n\ndocs(client): add REST-variants implementation plan\n\nIntroduce an implementation plan for adding REST-variant methods to\nthe sharkfin Go client. The plan adds a new RESTClient type whose\nconstructor does not open a WebSocket, so consumers that receive\nevents via webhook (Flow, future service bots) can call command-style\noperations without paying for a WS dial and read-pump goroutine. The\nexisting *Client stays unchanged for realtime consumers; new surface\nis strictly additive.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/wfa09mYovkTIpmBDKaxr+x8j2\nH8LU4Ovj81kHmEUf8AAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQP1QBWfCijg1ZChPF3rH2aIwyQWTE2AgPEMqH+I8u1LpOfd+2cyEdp1rFmRnLBFy76\nVQD1AcpeMHlLcWI9iLnwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-18T23:06:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/598968?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KazW/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaz