l":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/2c8250d2d84f5fbba697798c2db484a9284306e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T08:00:24Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T08:00:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(bucket-api): bind router test server to 127.0.0.1 to fix loopback flake (#47)\n\nThe `withServer` harness in `router.test.ts` spins an ephemeral Express server\nwith `app.listen(0)` (no host), which binds the IPv6 dual-stack wildcard `::`.\nThat ephemeral-port allocator is blind to IPv4-specific `127.0.0.1:*` listeners\nother local processes hold (IDEs, language servers, lima, …), so under heavy\nparallel load (a full `pnpm test`) it can hand the server a port number one of\nthem already owns on IPv4. The test then dials `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (IPv4)\nand the kernel routes to the more-specific foreign listener — so the request\nreads THAT server''s reply (a stray 403/404/405) and the assertion fails\nintermittently (e.g. `POST /copy` expecting 404 saw 400; `GET /download`\nexpecting 200 saw 405). It passes in isolation and on re-runs because the\ncolliding port has to be live at that instant.\n\nThis is not a body-parsing or undici race: captured anomalies showed responses\nwith no `X-Powered-By: Express` header and `text/plain \"Forbidden\"` bodies, and\n`lsof` pinned the exact offending ports to JetBrains/Antigravity listeners.\n\nFix: bind `127.0.0.1` explicitly so the ephemeral port is allocated in the same\nnamespace the client dials. The OS won''t hand out an IPv4 port another listener\nalready holds, so every request reaches this server.\n\nVerified: 640 oversubscribed suite runs + 3 consecutive full `pnpm test` runs,\nzero failures (the flake reproduced reliably before the fix).","tree":{"sha":"ffea4f36c2efbe6fb6cf29a8f51296b18b1720be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/ffea4f36c2efbe6fb6cf29a8f51296b18b1720be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/2c8250d2d84f5fbba697798c2db484a9284306e1","verification":{"payload":"tree ffea4f36c2efbe6fb6cf29a8f51296b18b1720be\nparent f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780819224 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780819224 +0800\n\ntest(bucket-api): bind router test server to 127.0.0.1 to fix loopback flake (#47)\n\nThe `withServer` harness in `router.test.ts` spins an ephemeral Express server\nwith `app.listen(0)` (no host), which binds the IPv6 dual-stack wildcard `::`.\nThat ephemeral-port allocator is blind to IPv4-specific `127.0.0.1:*` listeners\nother local processes hold (IDEs, language servers, lima, …), so under heavy\nparallel load (a full `pnpm test`) it can hand the server a port number one of\nthem already owns on IPv4. The test then dials `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (IPv4)\nand the kernel routes to the more-specific foreign listener — so the request\nreads THAT server''s reply (a stray 403/404/405) and the assertion fails\nintermittently (e.g. `POST /copy` expecting 404 saw 400; `GET /download`\nexpecting 200 saw 405). It passes in isolation and on re-runs because the\ncolliding port has to be live at that instant.\n\nThis is not a body-parsing or undici race: captured anomalies showed responses\nwith no `X-Powered-By: Express` header and `text/plain \"Forbidden\"` bodies, and\n`lsof` pinned the exact offending ports to JetBrains/Antigravity listeners.\n\nFix: bind `127.0.0.1` explicitly so the ephemeral port is allocated in the same\nnamespace the client dials. The OS won''t hand out an IPv4 port another listener\nalready holds, so every request reaches this server.\n\nVerified: 640 oversubscribed suite runs + 3 consecutive full `pnpm test` runs,\nzero failures (the flake reproduced reliably before the fix).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJSUYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwVMQAJyFvS8s9N+EEb6Hx4VkAYSd\ntPh2uELice8luuzcQCQS8ZSpX+0Cf1pQ64w8kAXMhXNNYEfTxvAh8uL/pH+3EYG9\nTZe8GZ7MsHQsb3JGTAG7EnhnMLEH9nMkw9Ico9JKXAeRcB0Cb+wCeHdjeQqSZD0y\nW0SEpkvBCs1lz/6t+QnLSVdQ31BWFJHH0QrNKK5es6+CVqlNfKw2MGk54eMrnvtU\np3gtIGd2i4eaA/9aCPaVVLD1oMWe/fw2182Wzyi/vsodiKrKgxde+TaYQ6lwRnPf\nuPHwdibVArB3gHiBXE/FKsJc9IzIr3OdS4kk8VjYPu0Kqr+SXyIRcopUPk4srvYP\nRFBPXgIoVF6M1U9A27SVBhAX+8qvXNT+QtWSZvSdYpxTTCRzEwiPQ8g/px2DWr5r\ncCqEo5DUg3SQzFuB4XUwTGlrNRvjofCEnWAjIIshE6yS7EhugO0aNFPdgCXwanut\npw0SNdwR1RMEzV9lXu80Eq1GIe/0UCiA6DJINkSupzXukd05r3w+k7YGtJqLe9Ls\nR7RZVTU2YwmPZVYcY9+9N1Da3IqpV6svjBs9Qk7K34KsgjFgJfz4BaQzcjERwhP8\nBj/wBvXjXfXNc/GZTGrK9owlOfuTqI6jK9dnBs5y3lN4zL6RLqwQM24LcWSVybUp\n2o499nF2FC2G8x3fb3QH\n=2nYB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T08:00:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/2c8250d2d84f5fbba697798c2db484a9284306e1","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDJjODI1MGQyZDg0ZjVmYmJhNjk3Nzk4YzJkYjQ4NGE5Mjg0MzA2ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2","sha":"f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2"}],"sha":"2c8250d2d84f5fbba697798c2db484a9284306e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/2c8250d2d84f5fbba697798c2db484a9284306e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T07:26:23Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T07:26:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(s3-browser): pause/resume uploads + per-part status (#46)\n\n* feat(s3-browser): pause/resume uploads + per-part status\n\nPause/resume: UploadManager gains pause()/resume(). Pausing aborts the\nin-flight transfer with an UPLOAD_PAUSED reason that tells uploadOneLarge to\nkeep the multipart upload AND its resumable session alive (instead of the\ncancel path''s server-side AbortMultipartUpload + session clear), so resume()\ncontinues via the existing ListParts skip-confirmed-parts flow. A queued task\nparks without starting; cancelling a paused task drops its local session so it\nwon''t silently resume (server-side parts are reaped by the bucket''s\nincomplete-upload lifecycle, as with a crash/reload). Small proxy uploads\nsimply restart.\n\nPer-part status: uploadOneLarge emits an aggregate {total, completed, active}\nvia a new onPart callback — an aggregate, not per-part rows, since a\nthousand-part upload can''t render individually. The manager threads it into\nthe task snapshot; UploadPanel shows \"Parts N/M · K uploading\", pause/resume\ncontrols, and a paused state (neutral muted, within the 4-color palette).\n\nTests: manager pause→resume, queued-pause, cancel-paused-clears-session, and\nper-part snapshot; uploader pause-keeps-session vs cancel-tears-down, plus\naggregate per-part emission.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): abort a paused multipart upload server-side on cancel\n\nCancelling a paused large upload deleted the local session — the only holder\nof the uploadId — without calling /multipart/abort, orphaning the already-\nuploaded parts on the bucket (and losing any handle to abort them later).\n\nUse the saved session to abort server-side (best-effort, fire-and-forget)\nBEFORE removing it, mirroring the in-flight cancel path. Small uploads keep\nno session, so it stays a plain session-remove for them.","tree":{"sha":"b2b095cf0e9330134214f6865afcef45a29d1d78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/b2b095cf0e9330134214f6865afcef45a29d1d78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2","verification":{"payload":"tree b2b095cf0e9330134214f6865afcef45a29d1d78\nparent 91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780817183 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780817183 +0800\n\nfeat(s3-browser): pause/resume uploads + per-part status (#46)\n\n* feat(s3-browser): pause/resume uploads + per-part status\n\nPause/resume: UploadManager gains pause()/resume(). Pausing aborts the\nin-flight transfer with an UPLOAD_PAUSED reason that tells uploadOneLarge to\nkeep the multipart upload AND its resumable session alive (instead of the\ncancel path''s server-side AbortMultipartUpload + session clear), so resume()\ncontinues via the existing ListParts skip-confirmed-parts flow. A queued task\nparks without starting; cancelling a paused task drops its local session so it\nwon''t silently resume (server-side parts are reaped by the bucket''s\nincomplete-upload lifecycle, as with a crash/reload). Small proxy uploads\nsimply restart.\n\nPer-part status: uploadOneLarge emits an aggregate {total, completed, active}\nvia a new onPart callback — an aggregate, not per-part rows, since a\nthousand-part upload can''t render individually. The manager threads it into\nthe task snapshot; UploadPanel shows \"Parts N/M · K uploading\", pause/resume\ncontrols, and a paused state (neutral muted, within the 4-color palette).\n\nTests: manager pause→resume, queued-pause, cancel-paused-clears-session, and\nper-part snapshot; uploader pause-keeps-session vs cancel-tears-down, plus\naggregate per-part emission.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): abort a paused multipart upload server-side on cancel\n\nCancelling a paused large upload deleted the local session — the only holder\nof the uploadId — without calling /multipart/abort, orphaning the already-\nuploaded parts on the bucket (and losing any handle to abort them later).\n\nUse the saved session to abort server-side (best-effort, fire-and-forget)\nBEFORE removing it, mirroring the in-flight cancel path. Small uploads keep\nno session, so it stays a plain session-remove for them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJR0fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1jYQACSa4FjGIFD18UttI93o6Fpo\n+6w2NJ7Jwee/p/WwRjbifCEQIPmbXn7luGTdsC+0Z8QzxA+XhF8U/Dny4GtQNxTg\nIbtr+BLG3GLw9weIpXxUeTDumdTEn3Mh8B9H+FqcimkxdAp1l/8ySgybbNoV0b+r\nwIWADYP6Wq5wWQAVarzW6sZoMQgbFdZFVBDl0sbDRhnNlIpN3GslUpAD2Fo4HWT1\n/qUSSf+5Kc6tiKfu1/ZQicZUpuKjgdAjMDsFVKIETtuEvqbrnn8RQVOyZkAWSyWq\nMaL+1iuqcmPlvODpUpAkLjdyvbql8vMDXESXVzej/XIJzrIVAz61Bch+JCKApZ8N\n0aKSIseouL3WF/cbV7btyj2AzPgx0HRVzTmx6UwJLo08ul3L/x3oV5MgxQhHWg4c\naxXyH/dLiEswEgzJSWRyDDIIX4lMhxpzB496Vjd+HAxAPWgnTViVc6OQD79XQaFy\nXuKFXVXVhdnpRfairofJ1hWepW/K/K3fwsutCpeHa4LAG9BAnbUZB+c3jMcOzpol\n0KFetYvmedtXRiKugMttd/FJ/wtyUXe5SqpVX5XHzlKF2iQiOly97qqbpu8wBXy6\n7edwiFp8cSV09bpTkPCSlUMqyPJQ2I85ci+hthSULnTewlzS943MbjrGMa6lyur5\nyYH51VUTODO7E9QUuVGf\n=iuYX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T07:26:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKGY2YWFkYWZlMTVmYjExYWE5OGEwNTFlNWViMTc4MWRkM2EzYjgxYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946","sha":"91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946"}],"sha":"f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/f6aadafe15fb11aa98a051e5eb1781dd3a3b81a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T07:19:17Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T07:19:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(bucket-api): spool small proxy uploads in memory, disk only as fallback (#44)\n\n* perf(bucket-api): spool small proxy uploads in memory, disk only as fallback\n\nuploadStreamToS3 always mkdtemp''d a temp file, wrote the whole body to it,\nthen read it back for PutObject — 2× disk I/O on every proxy upload, even\ntiny ones. Busboy gives no per-file Content-Length and S3 rejects chunked\nPutObject, so we must learn the size before sending; but not on disk.\n\nA new SpoolSink buffers the body in memory and spills to a temp file only\nonce it passes a cap (UPLOAD_MEMORY_SPOOL_MAX_BYTES, default 10 MiB = the\nproxy size limit), so by default every in-limit proxy upload stays entirely\nin memory. The cap is exposed as the uploadMemorySpoolMaxBytes router\noption for operators who raise the proxy limit and want to bound memory.\nThe busboy consumption path (pipeline + size limit + abort-on-oversize) is\nunchanged.\n\nTests: in-memory (Body is a Buffer), disk spill past the cap, and the\nmemory→disk ordering across the boundary.\n\n* fix(bucket-api): handle temp-file write errors during proxy upload spill\n\nSpoolSink only attached an ''error'' listener to the temp WriteStream in\n_final. A write that doesn''t need backpressure returns synchronously, so an\nasync failure (disk full, permissions) during the spill would be an\nunhandled ''error'' event — crashing the BFF instead of failing the upload.\n\nAttach the error listener as soon as the stream is created, record the first\nerror, and surface it from every write and from _final, so the upload\nrejects cleanly and a partial spool is never PutObject''d.\n\nTest: a temp-file write failure now rejects the upload without calling send.","tree":{"sha":"51955ffbeb6e9415dc5808de6670fb6b024e94a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/51955ffbeb6e9415dc5808de6670fb6b024e94a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946","verification":{"payload":"tree 51955ffbeb6e9415dc5808de6670fb6b024e94a2\nparent e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780816757 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780816757 +0800\n\nperf(bucket-api): spool small proxy uploads in memory, disk only as fallback (#44)\n\n* perf(bucket-api): spool small proxy uploads in memory, disk only as fallback\n\nuploadStreamToS3 always mkdtemp''d a temp file, wrote the whole body to it,\nthen read it back for PutObject — 2× disk I/O on every proxy upload, even\ntiny ones. Busboy gives no per-file Content-Length and S3 rejects chunked\nPutObject, so we must learn the size before sending; but not on disk.\n\nA new SpoolSink buffers the body in memory and spills to a temp file only\nonce it passes a cap (UPLOAD_MEMORY_SPOOL_MAX_BYTES, default 10 MiB = the\nproxy size limit), so by default every in-limit proxy upload stays entirely\nin memory. The cap is exposed as the uploadMemorySpoolMaxBytes router\noption for operators who raise the proxy limit and want to bound memory.\nThe busboy consumption path (pipeline + size limit + abort-on-oversize) is\nunchanged.\n\nTests: in-memory (Body is a Buffer), disk spill past the cap, and the\nmemory→disk ordering across the boundary.\n\n* fix(bucket-api): handle temp-file write errors during proxy upload spill\n\nSpoolSink only attached an ''error'' listener to the temp WriteStream in\n_final. A write that doesn''t need backpressure returns synchronously, so an\nasync failure (disk full, permissions) during the spill would be an\nunhandled ''error'' event — crashing the BFF instead of failing the upload.\n\nAttach the error listener as soon as the stream is created, record the first\nerror, and surface it from every write and from _final, so the upload\nrejects cleanly and a partial spool is never PutObject''d.\n\nTest: a temp-file write failure now rejects the upload without calling send.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJRt1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj4QQAFTTLvE0UtWiwEqsOGY3nfdD\nqQ36YzuC6Cg1G4+LN56Nswsk7FEmOSCMoOxXKV6f2+ivr9FfUqsSTGyRCe5dpOs0\n3vFRBF1bHEszr+cy1ZZZcqaXiIhUZctYswwcq94YYfglLMKkZMYh69uOqocxI3Qq\nh8x0zasQMH6Xxhc2n9TfqO4oThIXOPQJqbX/csd7A7fnTU2m4QO8KAWZS1Se5/0F\nWr1WLEyzR201XG0GSUo++Pxt7kmTpfUZx1m3AeGuPEHXbNhxHODasVF24KJLnrJC\nwEoAHU6PCsaxhFM7QbdIUzdjRTwZ9+LGvIlJgmJXQ5hQ68rM83zcnjoPyvf3ESv8\nrHJHYNNHa1Gd1ONWEdKp9Q84jGui23TNoiIy3dB5tusX55Bc0YjmifigaAA8lItI\nQBm82JoZub9RT7evjz2pEEEO9fo/iR1CXI+99azEvTDQGxQXwm+bmxFfm8aWVyLO\n1FibyZLb1VyLbIRwDXozdHKXJ95FPo684kWLH9n1D1Rh8PaTxnRB8ulD6vOGgRH6\n0czOOrxgg0rSq0cobhsn7WOlu5INHjGBpf3DFcoy5D4rODWRULauWr4c29TZYATz\nC6R5AApeTcWcsFYsgddOmZIh0x+sfbC0Q1Xavs9HWksh2rCd41BNwUtlNYHbh7uY\np3ijTnjcnMK5jOcP/xlN\n=pkM8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T07:19:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDkxYjdmN2FmMTE3NTg2ZGFiZDc2OWNiYjNiMDNiNTBkNGIwMTM5NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e","sha":"e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e"}],"sha":"91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/91b7f7af117586dabd769cbb3b03b50d4b013946"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T06:55:26Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T06:55:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(s3-browser): default control-plane timeout + recurring presign re-sign (#45)\n\nA) The embedded FileBrowser''s axios client had no timeout, so a half-open\nconnection on any control-plane call (list / object / presign / delete /\ncopy / cors-status / multipart control) could hang the request — and the\nprogress UI waiting on it — forever. Extract the client into\ncreateBackendHttp() with a 30s default timeout. The long-running\nstreaming/finalize ops opt OUT with timeout: 0: GET /download (3 sites),\nPOST /upload (proxy body), POST /multipart/complete (server-side stitch,\ncan take minutes).\n\nC) uploadPart re-signed an expired presigned URL only ONCE. A part queued\nbehind the global concurrency limit can age past two signing windows, so\nthe second 403/400 became fatal. Allow re-signs to recur, bounded by\nmaxAttempts so a backend that always reports \"expired\" (or a genuinely\nmalformed 400) can''t spin forever.\n\nTests: createBackendHttp sets the timeout and merges auth/extra headers;\n/multipart/complete and /upload assert timeout: 0; a second-expiry re-sign\nnow recovers (the old one-shot guard would have made it fatal).","tree":{"sha":"2ffd46bd8b50d8e6a8ec3597b4329256c8e290c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/2ffd46bd8b50d8e6a8ec3597b4329256c8e290c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ffd46bd8b50d8e6a8ec3597b4329256c8e290c7\nparent 9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780815326 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780815326 +0800\n\nfix(s3-browser): default control-plane timeout + recurring presign re-sign (#45)\n\nA) The embedded FileBrowser''s axios client had no timeout, so a half-open\nconnection on any control-plane call (list / object / presign / delete /\ncopy / cors-status / multipart control) could hang the request — and the\nprogress UI waiting on it — forever. Extract the client into\ncreateBackendHttp() with a 30s default timeout. The long-running\nstreaming/finalize ops opt OUT with timeout: 0: GET /download (3 sites),\nPOST /upload (proxy body), POST /multipart/complete (server-side stitch,\ncan take minutes).\n\nC) uploadPart re-signed an expired presigned URL only ONCE. A part queued\nbehind the global concurrency limit can age past two signing windows, so\nthe second 403/400 became fatal. Allow re-signs to recur, bounded by\nmaxAttempts so a backend that always reports \"expired\" (or a genuinely\nmalformed 400) can''t spin forever.\n\nTests: createBackendHttp sets the timeout and merges auth/extra headers;\n/multipart/complete and /upload assert timeout: 0; a second-expiry re-sign\nnow recovers (the old one-shot guard would have made it fatal).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJRXeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5xcQAEEKIrhj8T/21DJyqmMKaS4A\ndKXyuWRlsJSccXEn/K2LWYmR9RAUk/qpmPnpMGyJ47t4A8hTDDVN+2iDJQKEKaoC\nlo0WfzLilNGaHeEVod2zwD1N4MIv3Dx1PyV5C+2tzagk90kNq+sz3iUXbD6L5WM6\nRYSf5xZQ6a6u9abzP601DldOGto48Ao/7LroR4+TJrY0MymIQCW076L4O/VRtKzf\nWIaE2+j/GzDkbMw1mMoQMDHrB5inC1qNiXEpkbODCVmZ1mtF08J68Y0Iqlh0RHxT\nNCZXhGBStV/6SolxJlYZq53juzPujM761nNHN1eg0IXqZdx0A9c8l581wU03fSNf\nGKEZhUZMGTknBso/V2VbkiCMInoTWAOV2wphlDtDhCSi0Nw7Sl08GOI+tYEerKDM\nrUPQ63VIpfNtuivoUrblNE3/bIJpehyoOg2lBXFVt3YyYynUEcp0YUFegWnt2thZ\ngYlCn3yXSvzDPod2ttwaIPqBtjtyDfi+VOgLedbOzTr5PmshXu5y/xMFmJBX1fUP\nNQEa7kPqQyhxF6SNkmOOVnMNjSPLNYGKl1Ou/yVo2I/MWC7+3vg7X/dAtrxMTDew\nLl9VeteiUaeX/vT9CP2pagP1Zo+5ZJgihiQfLpIIaR25sIqawv4mbSenUZYVsiYo\nc5Gr9ucnxNqSYLsmAdur\n=6jR6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T06:55:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKGU3MTlkNzg1NzNlOTYyNTBlMzQxODI1NTg1N2IyNWMzNWZkNDViN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9","sha":"9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9"}],"sha":"e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/e719d78573e96250e3418255857b25c35fd45b7e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T06:33:59Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T06:33:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bucket-api): scope auto-CORS to a concrete origin, never a wildcard (#43)\n\ncorsOriginsFor fell back to [''*''] when a request carried no Origin header\nand no operator origins were configured. On the provisioning paths\n(presign getObject, multipart/create) that wrote a blanket `*` CORS rule\nto the bucket for non-browser callers and fragmented the per-origin CORS\ncache.\n\ncorsOriginsFor now returns null when no concrete origin is available, and\nthe provisioning paths skip ensureBucketCors entirely in that case — a\nnon-browser caller doesn''t need browser CORS. The read-only /cors-status\ndiagnostic treats a missing origin as \"any origin\" ([''*'']) since it never\nwrites a rule.\n\nTests: new router cases for the scoped / skip / operator-configured paths;\nthe s3-browser CORS-cache-identity test now sends a browser Origin.","tree":{"sha":"295a33c3d665c2d7897e1aa4f41b209b82855c3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/295a33c3d665c2d7897e1aa4f41b209b82855c3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9","verification":{"payload":"tree 295a33c3d665c2d7897e1aa4f41b209b82855c3f\nparent baabe3480841359b64c7c1fb8804b0b9e209e5e5\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780814039 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780814039 +0800\n\nfix(bucket-api): scope auto-CORS to a concrete origin, never a wildcard (#43)\n\ncorsOriginsFor fell back to [''*''] when a request carried no Origin header\nand no operator origins were configured. On the provisioning paths\n(presign getObject, multipart/create) that wrote a blanket `*` CORS rule\nto the bucket for non-browser callers and fragmented the per-origin CORS\ncache.\n\ncorsOriginsFor now returns null when no concrete origin is available, and\nthe provisioning paths skip ensureBucketCors entirely in that case — a\nnon-browser caller doesn''t need browser CORS. The read-only /cors-status\ndiagnostic treats a missing origin as \"any origin\" ([''*'']) since it never\nwrites a rule.\n\nTests: new router cases for the scoped / skip / operator-configured paths;\nthe s3-browser CORS-cache-identity test now sends a browser Origin.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJRDXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9IIQACKO8lgshdfq2y4RBwYyUhl7\nroDX3TvfWJrBWWqE+JwjV0EKpocRCHlfd1cRyP+WS21vLJP8rdmsD/r3Aa/vFKhl\nmFXklQbPDn3TujgbV4McSRsd/gL65nQXJ5hYK/+x+dwSoHbvXRhC2wKBahUhb9gk\nBGo90rUaxsWXoqaWiXK+vRcnWYtTAHs6rwbhnYqze/jRjO1aawitiahSOIyhc5+x\naSUH5aY4HQXIJVgidUagIbysQxXZVPDuFq5B+RVYgjwx7TIvTfUhESCo02i+O5o2\nKRRDgeavYEqCyBnOthdO8Rm7rnKh0l7qYQhzKmi0RPH5fOg8SPg0iiFZnj6rETMN\nAFvAOCuABwCLg5XOW0wwLppTZlzgOqjgrcnxHCxDZxI67GFPd/bce4Js9Ka+lnZ0\nmVmu2lOb9vWVAQml834GbdFJvZ+2JZwIuh4hjJlQStMaqh/xEsMP91Blx2//LTRo\nB+anwawEnyNkD8A/Mq/kGieZ4YQbePKFCwUlPAdG5VkiLPws6S82LTmnHm8n0emD\n4rdGjTfQWiCn9+dJwkfisRg7z5+J2A8fmJ7v3AnX6US29SQ4fkYc1bLWyqxcnySf\nOFc27CKw2YkSK2wuUD9tocv1GETfynIcVw7wg2AgoqBqpb0QdFrKpu/JRRn4eqZX\nq/L5FxSDq2U4nxL0ulV9\n=5G3z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T06:33:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDk0MjFmNDllNTIyOGU4MjUxZTk2MjA4ZTk3MjIyOTExZTk2ZGZlYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/baabe3480841359b64c7c1fb8804b0b9e209e5e5","sha":"baabe3480841359b64c7c1fb8804b0b9e209e5e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/baabe3480841359b64c7c1fb8804b0b9e209e5e5"}],"sha":"9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/9421f49e5228e8251e96208e97222911e96dfeb9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/baabe3480841359b64c7c1fb8804b0b9e209e5e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T06:06:14Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T06:06:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(bucket-api): cover 413 over-limit upload + partial-failure batch delete (#41)\n\n* test(bucket-api): cover 413 over-limit upload + partial-failure batch delete\n\nAdds two baseline contract cases from the upload-reliability plan that\nnever landed, so the suite is true drift-insurance between both BFFs:\n\n- POST /upload returns 413 when a single file exceeds the proxy size cap\n  (the 10 MiB LARGE_FILE_THRESHOLD_BYTES default; neither BFF overrides\n  it), echoing the limit and storing nothing — the cue to fall back to\n  the multipart flow. Previously only unit-tested via decideUploadResponse.\n- DELETE /objects partial-failure batch: one real key + one missing key\n  proves deleted[] and errors[] are both populated and partitioned by key.\n  Garage returns a per-key NoSuchKey error for a missing key in a batch\n  DeleteObjects (unlike AWS S3''s idempotent delete), which reliably\n  exercises the error-mapping path; the 2-key payload also forces the\n  batch DeleteObjects branch (the single-key shortcut always returns []).\n\nBoth paths live in the shared @garage/bucket-api-server router, so the\nresult holds for both flavors. Verified offline (skips cleanly) and live\nagainst the Garage dev cluster (connections flavor): 23/23 pass.\n\n* test(bucket-api): make mixed-batch delete assertion backend-agnostic\n\nAddresses review feedback: the partial-failure delete case baked in\nGarage''s nonstandard missing-key semantics (a missing key in a batch\nDeleteObjects yields a per-key error). Against AWS-S3-compatible endpoints\n— which the connections flavor can legitimately target — a missing-key\ndelete is an idempotent success that echoes the key in deleted[] with no\nerrors[], so the old assertion would fail even though the shared router\nmaps the upstream response correctly.\n\nThere''s no portable way to *guarantee* a partial failure via the batch-\ndelete API, so pin the BFF''s { deleted, errors } partitioning contract\ninstead: the real key always deletes, the missing key is accounted for in\nexactly one array (XOR — never dropped, never double-counted), and when a\nbackend DID report a per-key failure the mapped error carries a non-empty\nmessage. On Garage (this repo''s backend) that still exercises the errors[]\nmapping; on AWS-compatible endpoints it passes via the deleted[] path.\n\nVerified live against Garage: 23/23 pass.","tree":{"sha":"a217b7cc037118e1d2ee7329d452bc0875187822","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/a217b7cc037118e1d2ee7329d452bc0875187822"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/baabe3480841359b64c7c1fb8804b0b9e209e5e5","verification":{"payload":"tree a217b7cc037118e1d2ee7329d452bc0875187822\nparent d0006043a18b2d4b26e3b329b79e7ebbec269324\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780812374 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780812374 +0800\n\ntest(bucket-api): cover 413 over-limit upload + partial-failure batch delete (#41)\n\n* test(bucket-api): cover 413 over-limit upload + partial-failure batch delete\n\nAdds two baseline contract cases from the upload-reliability plan that\nnever landed, so the suite is true drift-insurance between both BFFs:\n\n- POST /upload returns 413 when a single file exceeds the proxy size cap\n  (the 10 MiB LARGE_FILE_THRESHOLD_BYTES default; neither BFF overrides\n  it), echoing the limit and storing nothing — the cue to fall back to\n  the multipart flow. Previously only unit-tested via decideUploadResponse.\n- DELETE /objects partial-failure batch: one real key + one missing key\n  proves deleted[] and errors[] are both populated and partitioned by key.\n  Garage returns a per-key NoSuchKey error for a missing key in a batch\n  DeleteObjects (unlike AWS S3''s idempotent delete), which reliably\n  exercises the error-mapping path; the 2-key payload also forces the\n  batch DeleteObjects branch (the single-key shortcut always returns []).\n\nBoth paths live in the shared @garage/bucket-api-server router, so the\nresult holds for both flavors. Verified offline (skips cleanly) and live\nagainst the Garage dev cluster (connections flavor): 23/23 pass.\n\n* test(bucket-api): make mixed-batch delete assertion backend-agnostic\n\nAddresses review feedback: the partial-failure delete case baked in\nGarage''s nonstandard missing-key semantics (a missing key in a batch\nDeleteObjects yields a per-key error). Against AWS-S3-compatible endpoints\n— which the connections flavor can legitimately target — a missing-key\ndelete is an idempotent success that echoes the key in deleted[] with no\nerrors[], so the old assertion would fail even though the shared router\nmaps the upstream response correctly.\n\nThere''s no portable way to *guarantee* a partial failure via the batch-\ndelete API, so pin the BFF''s { deleted, errors } partitioning contract\ninstead: the real key always deletes, the missing key is accounted for in\nexactly one array (XOR — never dropped, never double-counted), and when a\nbackend DID report a per-key failure the mapped error carries a non-empty\nmessage. On Garage (this repo''s backend) that still exercises the errors[]\nmapping; on AWS-compatible endpoints it passes via the deleted[] path.\n\nVerified live against Garage: 23/23 pass.","reason":"valid","signa