L byte (0x00)\nembedded in the template literal instead of the JS escape. Replace the\nraw control byte with the `\\0` escape so the file is plain UTF-8 text\nagain. Runtime behavior is identical — compositeKey still emits a NUL\nseparator.","tree":{"sha":"691c8367cb77b4d0233d52813687a83507d1f7bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/691c8367cb77b4d0233d52813687a83507d1f7bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/9b9563f02a427fd54143efa33189c98f056fbfcb","verification":{"payload":"tree 691c8367cb77b4d0233d52813687a83507d1f7bf\nparent 9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780811486 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780811486 +0800\n\nfix(s3-browser): store upload-sessions key separator as \\0 escape, not raw NUL (#40)\n\nupload-sessions.ts was committed as a binary blob because the\ncompositeKey field separator was written as a literal NUL byte (0x00)\nembedded in the template literal instead of the JS escape. Replace the\nraw control byte with the `\\0` escape so the file is plain UTF-8 text\nagain. Runtime behavior is identical — compositeKey still emits a NUL\nseparator.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJQbeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHysQAFPCwEUKLNtyYs7506jj/YQJ\nXXDfPhWnEsoQo3OmbtuqJ/khzNK8VKGZj4jhmFgQ/lpf2F+cto0cERpKPt0IJtHR\njuRl0uRQeEO9AYDig1upmQbzdC4nchPko3DcLfZn/o95zjo44oGgOy3uViQK/VsQ\nxScMATsCJq6pGgxWbM/e7n6bsPNfD7Jlntc2KIS3s40EXszN1vu3R7HwuWkPKmDT\ndX5/s9qNLCDiYKgPnZK0+K4WAfsuXYrtvyLSMEzNm5BY31viqU1dcfZ+z/kSc2or\nnxr1FLU2DNXDcY5W1gh+6dgMPsxQKGId7uEatbF6C8qMHyvD6uU5crhSzSb6Uqed\n9zrLSfIkIona7PvB6xs3aAgDOVperSDdqYdFNybUf0v0DRs+ztWc9qls10ZLVNCo\n0QPkfrindHUxuzYcHlsm5nLulaMu7fTu5pqCC+d+N98BNGnyzOh8wsOUNX5inDbl\ntqemS+vCOoWTAE7/tBSm60xqPCxFLKdr5F0XnIRCFE9R3YlkuhoGBGFvFRWgdKR7\n/DaocNqPj/1a0UQ445s3Uu2t3xG0s10SiA/BO90L5L7AUmNRqq2OO6btMjzXm6NU\nylSq6dERnPnx1sZiyDavUYwj0goaweXJ08TQ8rjzJCOFEAsBW7/cRuwjnhkhSbzQ\nXEjI+lkm6tPtX4MJNNHe\n=UyH7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T05:51:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/9b9563f02a427fd54143efa33189c98f056fbfcb","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDliOTU2M2YwMmE0MjdmZDU0MTQzZWZhMzMxODljOThmMDU2ZmJmY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34","sha":"9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34"}],"sha":"9b9563f02a427fd54143efa33189c98f056fbfcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/9b9563f02a427fd54143efa33189c98f056fbfcb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T05:27:50Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T05:27:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 5 (final) — resumable uploads + CORS diagnostics (#39)\n\n* feat: add /multipart/parts (resume) and /cors-status (diagnostic) routes\n\nPhase 5 (server) — two additive, backward-compatible routes on the shared\n@garage/bucket-api-server, the foundation for resumable uploads and an\nactionable CORS diagnostic. Both BFFs inherit them.\n\n- POST /multipart/parts: lists the parts already uploaded for an in-progress\n  multipart upload (ListParts, paginated up to MULTIPART_MAX_PARTS at 1000/page,\n  etags normalized). 404 on an unknown upload. The client uses it to RESUME —\n  re-selecting an interrupted file skips parts already on the server.\n- GET /cors-status: read-only CORS assessment for browser-direct transfers.\n  Reports { sufficient, reason: ok|no-config|insufficient|unreadable,\n  checkedOrigins, recommendedRule, status } so the client can explain whether a\n  failed direct upload is a CORS problem and how to fix it (instead of an opaque\n  failure). Never writes. New classifyBucketCors/recommendedCorsRule in cors.ts.\n\nTests: router.test.ts cases for parts (pagination + 404) and cors-status\n(ok/insufficient/no-config/unreadable); cors.test.ts for classifyBucketCors;\ncontract suite gains live parts (list a real uploaded part, 404 on unknown) and\ncors-status (shape) cases. docs/bucket-api.md documents both routes.\n\n* feat(s3-browser): resumable uploads + CORS diagnostic in the upload panel\n\nPhase 5 (frontend) — frontend-only; the Admin embed inherits it via MF.\n\nResume:\n- New lib/upload-sessions.ts: a localStorage-backed session store keyed by\n  backend baseUrl + file fingerprint (name+size+lastModified). Persists only\n  {key, uploadId, partSize, createdAt} (the server''s ListParts is the source of\n  truth for which parts landed), prunes entries older than 48h on construction.\n- uploadOneLarge persists a session on create and, when the same file is\n  re-selected after an interruption, calls /multipart/parts to skip the parts\n  already on the server and upload only the missing ones — then completes with\n  all of them. A stale session (404) is discarded and the upload restarts. The\n  session is cleared on success/abort; only a crash/reload leaves one to resume.\n- The upload manager wires its session store into every large file.\n\nCORS diagnostic:\n- New CorsDiagnostic surfaced in the panel when a task fails: a \"Check bucket\n  CORS\" action calls GET /cors-status and explains the result — purple \"apply\n  this rule\" (with the copyable recommended rule) when insufficient/unreadable,\n  green when CORS looks fine. The dev playground mocks /cors-status.\n\nTests: upload-sessions (round-trip, namespacing, TTL prune, corrupt blob) and\nuploadOneFile resume (skip server-confirmed parts, fresh-when-no-session,\ndiscard-stale-on-404). Browser-verified the diagnostic in the playground.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): only discard a resume session on 404, not transient errors\n\nThe resume probe''s catch cleared the saved session on ANY /multipart/parts\nfailure and started a fresh upload. That''s only correct for 404 (NoSuchUpload).\nOn a transient failure (timeout / 5xx / network drop) or a user abort the\nalready-uploaded parts are still valid, so dropping the session loses\nresumability (and orphans the parts behind a brand-new upload). Now only a 404\ndiscards the session; any other error propagates so a retry resumes from the\nsame session. Adds a test asserting a 503 probe keeps the session and issues no\nfresh create.\n\n* feat: operator-configurable S3 checksum mode (S3_CHECKSUM_MODE)\n\nThe S3 client''s checksum behavior was hardcoded to WHEN_REQUIRED (load-bearing:\nthe SDK''s CRC32 default breaks direct-to-Garage presigned PUTs). Make it an\nopt-in operator knob while keeping that safe default.\n\n- createS3Client gains a checksumMode option (''when_required'' default |\n  ''when_supported''), mapped to requestChecksumCalculation/responseChecksumValidation;\n  included in the client cache key so flipping the env yields a fresh client.\n- readChecksumMode parses/validates S3_CHECKSUM_MODE (shared; throws at startup\n  on a bad value). Both BFFs read it and pass it into getCachedS3Client (and the\n  S3 Browser connection-test probe).\n\nTests: readChecksumMode (default/parse/throw) + cache-key keys on the mode.\n\n* docs: document upload-reliability env knobs and refresh stale docs\n\nFinalize the upload-reliability docs sweep:\n- deployment.md (+ deployment_zh.md): S3_MULTIPART_BASE_PART_SIZE /\n  S3_MULTIPART_TARGET_PARTS / S3_MULTIPART_MAX_PART_SIZE / S3_CHECKSUM_MODE in\n  both production env tables; note they''re read by both BFFs.\n- development.md: new \"Bucket Backend API tuning (both BFFs)\" env subsection\n  (CORS + multipart + checksum knobs).\n- both api/.env.example: commented S3_MULTIPART_* + S3_CHECKSUM_MODE examples.\n- testing.md: refresh the now-stale bucket-api-server / s3-browser-web / contract\n  coverage descriptions (retry/concurrency/JIT/watchdog/resume, router routes,\n  /multipart/parts, /cors-status, classify/checksum helpers).\n- architecture.md: a \"Large-file upload reliability\" subsection.\n- contract-tests README + s3-browser/web README: list the new routes/runtime.","tree":{"sha":"d8dfbc2409f9346045a588fecd65a01ee8343b60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/d8dfbc2409f9346045a588fecd65a01ee8343b60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34","verification":{"payload":"tree d8dfbc2409f9346045a588fecd65a01ee8343b60\nparent cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780810070 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780810070 +0800\n\nfeat: Phase 5 (final) — resumable uploads + CORS diagnostics (#39)\n\n* feat: add /multipart/parts (resume) and /cors-status (diagnostic) routes\n\nPhase 5 (server) — two additive, backward-compatible routes on the shared\n@garage/bucket-api-server, the foundation for resumable uploads and an\nactionable CORS diagnostic. Both BFFs inherit them.\n\n- POST /multipart/parts: lists the parts already uploaded for an in-progress\n  multipart upload (ListParts, paginated up to MULTIPART_MAX_PARTS at 1000/page,\n  etags normalized). 404 on an unknown upload. The client uses it to RESUME —\n  re-selecting an interrupted file skips parts already on the server.\n- GET /cors-status: read-only CORS assessment for browser-direct transfers.\n  Reports { sufficient, reason: ok|no-config|insufficient|unreadable,\n  checkedOrigins, recommendedRule, status } so the client can explain whether a\n  failed direct upload is a CORS problem and how to fix it (instead of an opaque\n  failure). Never writes. New classifyBucketCors/recommendedCorsRule in cors.ts.\n\nTests: router.test.ts cases for parts (pagination + 404) and cors-status\n(ok/insufficient/no-config/unreadable); cors.test.ts for classifyBucketCors;\ncontract suite gains live parts (list a real uploaded part, 404 on unknown) and\ncors-status (shape) cases. docs/bucket-api.md documents both routes.\n\n* feat(s3-browser): resumable uploads + CORS diagnostic in the upload panel\n\nPhase 5 (frontend) — frontend-only; the Admin embed inherits it via MF.\n\nResume:\n- New lib/upload-sessions.ts: a localStorage-backed session store keyed by\n  backend baseUrl + file fingerprint (name+size+lastModified). Persists only\n  {key, uploadId, partSize, createdAt} (the server''s ListParts is the source of\n  truth for which parts landed), prunes entries older than 48h on construction.\n- uploadOneLarge persists a session on create and, when the same file is\n  re-selected after an interruption, calls /multipart/parts to skip the parts\n  already on the server and upload only the missing ones — then completes with\n  all of them. A stale session (404) is discarded and the upload restarts. The\n  session is cleared on success/abort; only a crash/reload leaves one to resume.\n- The upload manager wires its session store into every large file.\n\nCORS diagnostic:\n- New CorsDiagnostic surfaced in the panel when a task fails: a \"Check bucket\n  CORS\" action calls GET /cors-status and explains the result — purple \"apply\n  this rule\" (with the copyable recommended rule) when insufficient/unreadable,\n  green when CORS looks fine. The dev playground mocks /cors-status.\n\nTests: upload-sessions (round-trip, namespacing, TTL prune, corrupt blob) and\nuploadOneFile resume (skip server-confirmed parts, fresh-when-no-session,\ndiscard-stale-on-404). Browser-verified the diagnostic in the playground.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): only discard a resume session on 404, not transient errors\n\nThe resume probe''s catch cleared the saved session on ANY /multipart/parts\nfailure and started a fresh upload. That''s only correct for 404 (NoSuchUpload).\nOn a transient failure (timeout / 5xx / network drop) or a user abort the\nalready-uploaded parts are still valid, so dropping the session loses\nresumability (and orphans the parts behind a brand-new upload). Now only a 404\ndiscards the session; any other error propagates so a retry resumes from the\nsame session. Adds a test asserting a 503 probe keeps the session and issues no\nfresh create.\n\n* feat: operator-configurable S3 checksum mode (S3_CHECKSUM_MODE)\n\nThe S3 client''s checksum behavior was hardcoded to WHEN_REQUIRED (load-bearing:\nthe SDK''s CRC32 default breaks direct-to-Garage presigned PUTs). Make it an\nopt-in operator knob while keeping that safe default.\n\n- createS3Client gains a checksumMode option (''when_required'' default |\n  ''when_supported''), mapped to requestChecksumCalculation/responseChecksumValidation;\n  included in the client cache key so flipping the env yields a fresh client.\n- readChecksumMode parses/validates S3_CHECKSUM_MODE (shared; throws at startup\n  on a bad value). Both BFFs read it and pass it into getCachedS3Client (and the\n  S3 Browser connection-test probe).\n\nTests: readChecksumMode (default/parse/throw) + cache-key keys on the mode.\n\n* docs: document upload-reliability env knobs and refresh stale docs\n\nFinalize the upload-reliability docs sweep:\n- deployment.md (+ deployment_zh.md): S3_MULTIPART_BASE_PART_SIZE /\n  S3_MULTIPART_TARGET_PARTS / S3_MULTIPART_MAX_PART_SIZE / S3_CHECKSUM_MODE in\n  both production env tables; note they''re read by both BFFs.\n- development.md: new \"Bucket Backend API tuning (both BFFs)\" env subsection\n  (CORS + multipart + checksum knobs).\n- both api/.env.example: commented S3_MULTIPART_* + S3_CHECKSUM_MODE examples.\n- testing.md: refresh the now-stale bucket-api-server / s3-browser-web / contract\n  coverage descriptions (retry/concurrency/JIT/watchdog/resume, router routes,\n  /multipart/parts, /cors-status, classify/checksum helpers).\n- architecture.md: a \"Large-file upload reliability\" subsection.\n- contract-tests README + s3-browser/web README: list the new routes/runtime.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJQFWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuMwQAHsZTnQKSl5+Alq7pSEa5IkT\nZKIxFmHE/aWvAmbX3b/vfEYziszNR8fnb7RyrxrG1rQVJIFGv+Zr+OvN2pjIzPJK\nuWU63L9uhpeBoYHnSQ1PgXfaXxhE+CIjOmocsH9LIS10pNmNoZc4R9mKIqIHkS5Z\ndABi3WupfOG2Z3Qp4bfri2Hs2eRwVmsyZWHsXispWThWoAF1Y3JuzaqQ3CKqI/GJ\nqvkjuiGga5q27kbnlO/TiA8SJLAX7h5Pcc6mQu1uL9JM8S2A16WsPWJADmDhCxR9\nQZ9pTPzGLl9iYYtlRkOxgiLUwmaTFFgYnmA4wV7+YyUxBf4d+tVSbRCQFwC/eXFQ\nDk2SkjoLRIlC/iwFjEjejx+sS9CoWN/jSt+sVaiQioTeyOz0px6B3+mGBL8B4n9/\naO2s6mbsnJSocaDxVGfdP2Tgjkxo5/WIHLyrrgALDa79UCp1s/6gyTbuvIewZT75\nEblUWRTcTmBqr5WJDGO9AyvFQCmykJlBKMMhTA1ywyDmhLbW3vyvzTQl7DCHfg6J\nar514SNgzXqVgHgvp5p9GOdZOzJxgubrY6GlTRsLAENBWrpExcKRO/7ng/5iDKEA\nKH0Bimx2pR0PBTVHzkfv+z9c5PIMZyJJSKU1oSk6thov6FvJvcziYd0CzvkrsxWm\nZ1uWae985k5gmytqi4TL\n=gh4G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T05:27:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDkzMDFkZDMxMTdiYjhkOGNhYTFjNTNlMTc3Y2IyODVkNjQ5NDliMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195","sha":"cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195"}],"sha":"9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/9301dd3117bb8d8caa1c53e177cb285d64949b34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T03:16:54Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T03:16:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(s3-browser): Phase 4 — background upload manager + non-blocking panel (#38)\n\n* feat(s3-browser): background upload manager (queue, per-file control)\n\nPhase 4 (store) — a framework-agnostic UploadManager that turns the one-shot\nuploader into a reopenable, non-blocking queue with PER-FILE control. Frontend\nonly; the Admin embed inherits it via Module Federation.\n\n- New uploadOneFile(): the per-file primitive (small → proxy /upload, large →\n  direct multipart), extracted from runUploadJob (now sharing resolveReliability)\n  so the manager and the one-shot batch API run the same tested core.\n- UploadManager: per-file tasks each with their own AbortController (so one file\n  can be cancelled/retried without touching siblings — fixing the old single-\n  controller-per-job), a file-level concurrency cap (the global part-PUT\n  Semaphore still bounds bytes underneath), and a useSyncExternalStore-shaped\n  surface (subscribe + immutable snapshot). Status machine:\n  queued→uploading→done|error|canceled; cancel/cancelAll/retry/remove/clearFinished.\n\nTests: new upload-manager.test.ts covers the concurrency cap, complete→next,\nisolated per-file error, in-flight + queued cancel, retry, clearFinished, and\nsubscriber notification. isAbortError matches name/code so it classifies both\nDOMException(''AbortError'') (XHR path) and axios CanceledError/ERR_CANCELED\n(proxy path) as cancels rather than errors.\n\n* feat(s3-browser): non-blocking upload panel; dialog enqueues in the background\n\nPhase 4 (UI) — the upload dialog is now a file PICKER that hands files to the\nbackground UploadManager and closes, so it never blocks and uploads survive\nnavigating away. Progress, per-file retry/cancel and partial-failure reporting\nmove to a floating, reopenable UploadPanel.\n\n- context: one UploadManager per backend (created in the provider, not the\n  dialog, so it survives the dialog closing); a useUploadTasks() hook exposes the\n  snapshot via useSyncExternalStore; an effect subscribes and refreshes a\n  prefix''s listing once per file that lands (manager stays a pure store).\n- UploadPanel: floating bottom-right, minimizable, with per-file progress and\n  cancel/retry/remove + cancel-all/clear. Palette stays within the four colors\n  (orange in progress, green done, red error; neutral for queued/canceled).\n- Verified in the playground: dialog→enqueue→panel→listing refresh, minimize,\n  and clear all work; no console errors.","tree":{"sha":"3cd0bae9aff1494b46c8e40e728c9c6f1aa37057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/3cd0bae9aff1494b46c8e40e728c9c6f1aa37057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cd0bae9aff1494b46c8e40e728c9c6f1aa37057\nparent a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780802214 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780802214 +0800\n\nfeat(s3-browser): Phase 4 — background upload manager + non-blocking panel (#38)\n\n* feat(s3-browser): background upload manager (queue, per-file control)\n\nPhase 4 (store) — a framework-agnostic UploadManager that turns the one-shot\nuploader into a reopenable, non-blocking queue with PER-FILE control. Frontend\nonly; the Admin embed inherits it via Module Federation.\n\n- New uploadOneFile(): the per-file primitive (small → proxy /upload, large →\n  direct multipart), extracted from runUploadJob (now sharing resolveReliability)\n  so the manager and the one-shot batch API run the same tested core.\n- UploadManager: per-file tasks each with their own AbortController (so one file\n  can be cancelled/retried without touching siblings — fixing the old single-\n  controller-per-job), a file-level concurrency cap (the global part-PUT\n  Semaphore still bounds bytes underneath), and a useSyncExternalStore-shaped\n  surface (subscribe + immutable snapshot). Status machine:\n  queued→uploading→done|error|canceled; cancel/cancelAll/retry/remove/clearFinished.\n\nTests: new upload-manager.test.ts covers the concurrency cap, complete→next,\nisolated per-file error, in-flight + queued cancel, retry, clearFinished, and\nsubscriber notification. isAbortError matches name/code so it classifies both\nDOMException(''AbortError'') (XHR path) and axios CanceledError/ERR_CANCELED\n(proxy path) as cancels rather than errors.\n\n* feat(s3-browser): non-blocking upload panel; dialog enqueues in the background\n\nPhase 4 (UI) — the upload dialog is now a file PICKER that hands files to the\nbackground UploadManager and closes, so it never blocks and uploads survive\nnavigating away. Progress, per-file retry/cancel and partial-failure reporting\nmove to a floating, reopenable UploadPanel.\n\n- context: one UploadManager per backend (created in the provider, not the\n  dialog, so it survives the dialog closing); a useUploadTasks() hook exposes the\n  snapshot via useSyncExternalStore; an effect subscribes and refreshes a\n  prefix''s listing once per file that lands (manager stays a pure store).\n- UploadPanel: floating bottom-right, minimizable, with per-file progress and\n  cancel/retry/remove + cancel-all/clear. Palette stays within the four colors\n  (orange in progress, green done, red error; neutral for queued/canceled).\n- Verified in the playground: dialog→enqueue→panel→listing refresh, minimize,\n  and clear all work; no console errors.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJOKmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4vwQAE2FkxmMMMSQ7/nrbJTsxABa\nQDVEkZcyNAG3GcuPlok6sjUvR1lISgYn3y3IsEiLWahA1AbH1jy9sdBRZGfEHgWt\nUyNYf1B0SO9CVCrSw/ZC04dhrzr19U35bydATEsnGJCNc9pR0Xu2YRvB9k9U1wqG\njdh1V2TYn6k2pYOkdnsnuh1Bs/ZHcjJmRV1SmcJvGqveW81gvAeiULbg9W76qDVA\nwisEed9vJKVRoosri7ITVXr0w1ucz3ja5IfNHcPbptBNjemaU7zuv6BCxc0JljWV\nbNhb482QEEZR53YAlFLJzZQzWMb/k8eLpVzQlAT49bGADSkNBJDJRy0wWO/NeEAv\njG164CVvHOghQEWvm0HBRS1895n7UQTSLg/TzQvXbAzYkQbge+t3KNs2V4p50WSn\nwILYkzSIG4MS1kCIEgWmyFB6jbkPJnhexAt9uDSPRIrHOxtDIEsX8tKYjRwsD5+/\nGucbSZtlyNUrN8jMDqp9gzJ4Uuf54eh4F+0mXrtCmuMUVDYBosGfyqfz2KVBlOYa\n3xwFVj3yRkCQQry0SNssPXDl3EADcLodr65rydJ9rc1ELXT6pyUzF9c71ZGcRRt2\n+qxWE3hFRY/czKgPYhbC19L025317MyTxZVE1Kji/xUzPcH9itc5hQO0/t/BiDcC\nFv/1wjhjdinws6nmrhbI\n=IY+J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T03:16:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKGNkOWMwMjUzNWVhMjI2MzRlNzNmODg5NTY0OGM5YjYxM2Y0NTcxOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b","sha":"a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b"}],"sha":"cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/cd9c02535ea22634e73f8895648c9b613f457195"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T02:48:52Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T02:48:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 3 — adaptive multipart part size + S3_MULTIPART_* config (#37)\n\n* feat: adaptive multipart part size + S3_MULTIPART_* config (Bucket API)\n\nPhase 3 — POST /multipart/create now scales the returned part size to the file\nsize so the part count stays bounded as files grow, reaching S3''s full 5 TiB\nobject range while each PUT stays independently retryable. In the shared\n@garage/bucket-api-server, backward compatible.\n\n- New computeMultipartPartSize(fileSize): doubling ladder from an 8 MiB base up\n  to a 1 GiB top, climbing until the part count is at/below a ~2000 soft target,\n  with a hard guarantee that it never exceeds MULTIPART_MAX_PARTS (10k) up to\n  S3''s 5 GiB per-part ceiling. Returns >= the 5 MiB S3 floor.\n- POST /multipart/create accepts an optional `fileSize`: present → adaptive part\n  size; absent → the static 8 MiB default (so an un-rebuilt Admin host is\n  unaffected). New createBucketRouter options multipartTargetParts /\n  multipartMaxPartSize (multipartPartSize is now the ladder base).\n- readMultipartPolicyEnv parses + validates S3_MULTIPART_BASE_PART_SIZE /\n  S3_MULTIPART_TARGET_PARTS / S3_MULTIPART_MAX_PART_SIZE (shared by both BFFs so\n  the parsing isn''t forked inline; throws at startup on bad config).\n\nTests: new offline multipart-policy.test.ts (ladder across 100 MiB→20 TiB, the\n5 MiB floor, custom options, the hard cap, and env parse/validation) +\nrouter.test.ts create cases (default 8 MiB vs scaled); contract suite asserts a\nlarge fileSize scales partSize up and keeps the part count under maxParts.\ndocs/bucket-api.md documents the optional field + env knobs.\n\n* feat: send fileSize from the uploader and wire S3_MULTIPART_* into both BFFs\n\n- s3-browser/web: the multipart uploader passes `fileSize` to /multipart/create\n  so it gets an adaptive part size (it already trusts the returned partSize, so\n  no slicing change).\n- Both BFFs (s3-browser/api + garage-admin-console/api) read the shared\n  readMultipartPolicyEnv() and pass the policy into createBucketRouter, so the\n  S3_MULTIPART_* knobs apply to both products.","tree":{"sha":"8a49d3ce4b716bfebcbaa3eee99b86e74be4a8c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/8a49d3ce4b716bfebcbaa3eee99b86e74be4a8c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a49d3ce4b716bfebcbaa3eee99b86e74be4a8c7\nparent 4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780800532 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780800532 +0800\n\nfeat: Phase 3 — adaptive multipart part size + S3_MULTIPART_* config (#37)\n\n* feat: adaptive multipart part size + S3_MULTIPART_* config (Bucket API)\n\nPhase 3 — POST /multipart/create now scales the returned part size to the file\nsize so the part count stays bounded as files grow, reaching S3''s full 5 TiB\nobject range while each PUT stays independently retryable. In the shared\n@garage/bucket-api-server, backward compatible.\n\n- New computeMultipartPartSize(fileSize): doubling ladder from an 8 MiB base up\n  to a 1 GiB top, climbing until the part count is at/below a ~2000 soft target,\n  with a hard guarantee that it never exceeds MULTIPART_MAX_PARTS (10k) up to\n  S3''s 5 GiB per-part ceiling. Returns >= the 5 MiB S3 floor.\n- POST /multipart/create accepts an optional `fileSize`: present → adaptive part\n  size; absent → the static 8 MiB default (so an un-rebuilt Admin host is\n  unaffected). New createBucketRouter options multipartTargetParts /\n  multipartMaxPartSize (multipartPartSize is now the ladder base).\n- readMultipartPolicyEnv parses + validates S3_MULTIPART_BASE_PART_SIZE /\n  S3_MULTIPART_TARGET_PARTS / S3_MULTIPART_MAX_PART_SIZE (shared by both BFFs so\n  the parsing isn''t forked inline; throws at startup on bad config).\n\nTests: new offline multipart-policy.test.ts (ladder across 100 MiB→20 TiB, the\n5 MiB floor, custom options, the hard cap, and env parse/validation) +\nrouter.test.ts create cases (default 8 MiB vs scaled); contract suite asserts a\nlarge fileSize scales partSize up and keeps the part count under maxParts.\ndocs/bucket-api.md documents the optional field + env knobs.\n\n* feat: send fileSize from the uploader and wire S3_MULTIPART_* into both BFFs\n\n- s3-browser/web: the multipart uploader passes `fileSize` to /multipart/create\n  so it gets an adaptive part size (it already trusts the returned partSize, so\n  no slicing change).\n- Both BFFs (s3-browser/api + garage-admin-console/api) read the shared\n  readMultipartPolicyEnv() and pass the policy into createBucketRouter, so the\n  S3_MULTIPART_* knobs apply to both products.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJNwVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU9oQACkr9ezoRvB5a6araJHalKZH\niYO3zU+mKTOfG3iez4yX/BeZNkfnr7bQC9NNF6u/w4LIkCd0VeaQiJoYy8ro0Svy\nMukxLbbPAIxdQZS69wT2Hl2dxrQ2C5RwhI1usIQ4pZe25Bpfh9PtE84XysGgzy9t\nK7nz6hzkse6T2utpsGhdfEdI/5XkHYj/6rg6uddM75hJItqF4nSAH7lCdPkTElT/\nBUJaCwZ7LFHEloq1vUgNHTwpknKa8c3c0XehRk4ZAIkunWcBUZ2V8AhKtvzzKoeD\nLehJmFBifU80pbMQew69WF2fbJzW4cKD+J4OhPNBx6w9FcuEIM7ORtIbRiLRCAjg\nh2Gr66jsVHOGyWPI7NlPyRScYkBpurKoIi0VJYGfAAvEl8eb245wzr4NCK0UDEMb\nMnYyzzLowSOFVUci4NgHR3IlDCGwfGv+4K7/scFi8g+rk16RBw0UMo2jtKKr7pY7\nr5eVlkKgjxfK6h4pqa4D/7Sgvm1GYBhGQtZeOudRYv8xn/XKJ/oCyzLryHs4Oe4z\nZ1nzzukJS6rm2LGYHR6b4iosW+akmYIKdf5dDzNERe5Cvi3c3ZMCIITFZRzgh2lf\n9kQayQU8g68fflqSanI+2P6W5bRoXR80helzP7e+yGnbZfGRmYae+a6eh4xJzsyL\nHEwWC41zinR53AyLh0e+\n=1msE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T02:48:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKGExYzYxYmFkZTliZjRmMGYzNDkyYjQwMmYxZDIyY2I0ODFiMDkxOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a","sha":"4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a"}],"sha":"a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/a1c61bade9bf4f0f3492b402f1d22cb481b0919b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T02:24:45Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T02:24:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Phase 2 — harden /download streaming + >5 GiB multipart copy (Bucket API) (#36)\n\n* feat: harden /download streaming and add >5 GiB multipart copy (Bucket API)\n\nPhase 2 — server-side reliability in the shared @garage/bucket-api-server, so\nboth BFFs (S3 Browser + Admin Console) inherit it. Backward compatible: route\nshapes and well-formed responses are unchanged.\n\nGET /download:\n- Replace the bare `body.pipe(res)` with `stream.pipeline`, split into a fetch\n  phase (clean JSON errors incl. 404 before any bytes) and a stream phase. A\n  mid-stream upstream error now destroys the response (truncated, never a short\n  body read as complete) and a client disconnect tears the S3 read stream down\n  instead of leaking the upstream socket.\n\nPOST /copy:\n- HeadObject first, then branch on size: <= 5 GiB keeps the single CopyObject;\n  larger sources use a server-side multipart copy (CreateMultipartUpload +\n  ranged UploadPartCopy + CompleteMultipartUpload, AbortMultipartUpload on\n  failure), carrying the source''s content metadata. This lifts the 5 GiB single-\n  copy ceiling that copy/move/rename hit. CopySourceRange is inclusive with the\n  last part clamped to size-1 (verified byte-perfect against a live Garage\n  cluster). Missing source now returns a clean 404.\n\nTests: new offline router.test.ts (ephemeral Express + mock S3 client) covers\ndownload full/range/404/mid-stream-error/client-disconnect and copy\nsingle/multipart-ranges/abort-on-failure; contract suite gains live download\nfull + ranged (206) round-trips. docs/bucket-api.md updated.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): re-sign expired presigned part URLs on 400 or 403\n\nThe expired-URL re-sign backstop only triggered on 403, but a live probe showed\nGarage returns 400 InvalidRequest \"Date is too old\" for an expired presigned\nUploadPart URL (AWS S3 / MinIO use 403 \"Request has expired\"). On Garage the\nbackstop therefore never fired and 400 was treated as fatal. Trigger the one-\nshot re-sign on 400 OR 403 (endpoint-agnostic); worst case is one wasted PUT on\na genuinely malformed 400. JIT windowed signing remains the primary defense.\n\nAdds a 400 re-sign test; switches the fatal-path tests to 404 (cleanly non-\nretryable and not an expired-URL signal).","tree":{"sha":"3995b886db989e886a2142bd6b3de27055271015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/3995b886db989e886a2142bd6b3de27055271015"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a","verification":{"payload":"tree 3995b886db989e886a2142bd6b3de27055271015\nparent 08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780799085 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780799085 +0800\n\nfeat: Phase 2 — harden /download streaming + >5 GiB multipart copy (Bucket API) (#36)\n\n* feat: harden /download streaming and add >5 GiB multipart copy (Bucket API)\n\nPhase 2 — server-side reliability in the shared @garage/bucket-api-server, so\nboth BFFs (S3 Browser + Admin Console) inherit it. Backward compatible: route\nshapes and well-formed responses are unchanged.\n\nGET /download:\n- Replace the bare `body.pipe(res)` with `stream.pipeline`, split into a fetch\n  phase (clean JSON errors incl. 404 before any bytes) and a stream phase. A\n  mid-stream upstream error now destroys the response (truncated, never a short\n  body read as complete) and a client disconnect tears the S3 read stream down\n  instead of leaking the upstream socket.\n\nPOST /copy:\n- HeadObject first, then branch on size: <= 5 GiB keeps the single CopyObject;\n  larger sources use a server-side multipart copy (CreateMultipartUpload +\n  ranged UploadPartCopy + CompleteMultipartUpload, AbortMultipartUpload on\n  failure), carrying the source''s content metadata. This lifts the 5 GiB single-\n  copy ceiling that copy/move/rename hit. CopySourceRange is inclusive with the\n  last part clamped to size-1 (verified byte-perfect against a live Garage\n  cluster). Missing source now returns a clean 404.\n\nTests: new offline router.test.ts (ephemeral Express + mock S3 client) covers\ndownload full/range/404/mid-stream-error/client-disconnect and copy\nsingle/multipart-ranges/abort-on-failure; contract suite gains live download\nfull + ranged (206) round-trips. docs/bucket-api.md updated.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): re-sign expired presigned part URLs on 400 or 403\n\nThe expired-URL re-sign backstop only triggered on 403, but a live probe showed\nGarage returns 400 InvalidRequest \"Date is too old\" for an expired presigned\nUploadPart URL (AWS S3 / MinIO use 403 \"Request has expired\"). On Garage the\nbackstop therefore never fired and 400 was treated as fatal. Trigger the one-\nshot re-sign on 400 OR 403 (endpoint-agnostic); worst case is one wasted PUT on\na genuinely malformed 400. JIT windowed signing remains the primary defense.\n\nAdds a 400 re-sign test; switches the fatal-path tests to 404 (cleanly non-\nretryable and not an expired-URL signal).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJNZtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZM0QAEOjz9oiTSbRVTfhSs9lJYyu\n34v2csRx6SiovQfvU+83vH1DfLSYskI1bwfn92UZ7sVYURr17AXlRAdWgpBbkzIH\nj4JxszOTpxzb1ycGQzIrMdVzMdvEtPfYpFyvD/2F20mELKZejh3Qj38HmNytxRKW\nbwx2oyIvsBjR5DXJUulP5TENiYlH3fx7y38dvozuhuAslGWjX1BRnIbbnSgG+3dk\nu7PiJCTm1mhgRfdbVgGbZgRwtZ3eHOBtOv00srI78/MUViRJgSnSaNGYOCiRG+9u\n7t9ntM3f9Yg2vLV7TiUoQPU49YEyM1ZnP/UJYKIZmY0iTNPseOPx1C/05iNabUx/\nhk+swiYqZTpyfuKKl+AvXsM0M716OFBESwfPNgVb2GEl///dm9PjzmVxjbrvdWx2\nVwkFUJCFxObV+p5key+h7N5XAQBvSezj9mVj4qr4zLSD1PMYVP37ZxbKsWD3Kjmv\nVhrURsmdCKSpdaKd/lQGCAKL9hl5iUjjtAemDpkrLssSUI5QERvzdz7tHmNcWaP/\nTQY8QS78wqYknjvfuUmIOLscwTWUg7oC2IVaqiLrvV0sOyoatvVvxVslqAHSCTWc\n1fjhcb3rx0nN4MRbmMdWRpn4UY4/HUVQsmZ4XKm35u739IdDCoNEiGaPLgXgiLZX\nqSAS7415BcdR2cmdFnnO\n=ivwv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T02:24:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDQ3MjRkNDRjMDVmMTc1MjlkY2RlMWVlN2M0MmQzMjc2MDNlZmUyOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad","sha":"08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad"}],"sha":"4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/4724d44c05f17529dcde1ee7c42d327603efe29a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T01:53:24Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T01:53:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(s3-browser): harden large-file uploads (Phase 1 reliability) (#35)\n\n* feat(s3-browser): harden large-file uploads (Phase 1 reliability)\n\nMove multipart upload from \"can handle large files\" to \"reliably handles\nlarge files\", entirely in the federated remote so the Admin Console embed\ninherits the fixes via Module Federation — no change to the shared\n@garage/bucket-api-server router or its contract.\n\n- Per-part retry: 4 attempts with full-jitter exponential backoff; retries\n  network errors and 408/429/5xx; an expired-URL 403 re-signs that one part\n  and retries once; 4xx/missing-ETag stay fatal.\n- Global concurrency cap: one module-level Semaphore(6) shared across every\n  file and job (browser per-origin reality) instead of partConcurrency ×\n  file-count (~40 PUTs for 10 files).\n- Just-in-time windowed signing: sign part URLs in sliding windows with an\n  expiry-skew re-sign, replacing the all-upfront 1h presign that could lapse\n  in the upload queue.\n- Failure isolation: Promise.allSettled so one file''s failure no longer\n  aborts its siblings; each file aborts only its own multipart upload.\n- Stall watchdog: per-part inactivity timer aborts+retries a half-open\n  socket; mandatory (a non-positive value falls back to the default) so it\n  can''t be disabled into a shared-permit deadlock.\n- Control-plane timeouts on create/sign/complete/abort.\n- Partial success surfaced via UploadJobError carrying the stored files; the\n  dialog refreshes the listing and reports \"N uploaded; the rest failed\"\n  instead of hiding stored siblings behind a total-failure message.\n\nTests: part retry, 403 re-sign, stall recovery, sibling-survives-failure,\nprogress-no-double-count, global-cap, user-cancel (AbortError + abort\ncleanup, cancel-wins-over-concurrent-error), and a standalone Semaphore\nsuite.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): leave /multipart/complete untimed (can take minutes)\n\nCompleteMultipartUpload stitches every part server-side and AWS documents\nit as potentially taking several minutes. The blanket 30s control-plane\ntimeout was also applied to /multipart/complete, so a large upload could be\nrejected AFTER all parts were uploaded, fall into the catch path, and fire\n/multipart/abort — destroying or racing an upload the backend was still\nfinalizing.\n\nScope the 30s timeout to the quick metadata calls (create/sign/abort) and\nleave /multipart/complete untimed (BFF handling + socket timeout are the\nbackstops); also keep the user signal off complete so a cancel can''t race\nthe finalize. Adds a regression test asserting complete carries no timeout\nwhile create/sign do.","tree":{"sha":"3cfbb872dd7dacd86f8348bc9dc9ac86b9ea08a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/3cfbb872dd7dacd86f8348bc9dc9ac86b9ea08a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cfbb872dd7dacd86f8348bc9dc9ac86b9ea08a9\nparent e23b279ef4b70e0402dbc2cd7e5cf01c3770a5b0\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780797204 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780797204 +0800\n\nfeat(s3-browser): harden large-file uploads (Phase 1 reliability) (#35)\n\n* feat(s3-browser): harden large-file uploads (Phase 1 reliability)\n\nMove multipart upload from \"can handle large files\" to \"reliably handles\nlarge files\", entirely in the federated remote so the Admin Console embed\ninherits the fixes via Module Federation — no change to the shared\n@garage/bucket-api-server router or its contract.\n\n- Per-part retry: 4 attempts with full-jitter exponential backoff; retries\n  network errors and 408/429/5xx; an expired-URL 403 re-signs that one part\n  and retries once; 4xx/missing-ETag stay fatal.\n- Global concurrency cap: one module-level Semaphore(6) shared across every\n  file and job (browser per-origin reality) instead of partConcurrency ×\n  file-count (~40 PUTs for 10 files).\n- Just-in-time windowed signing: sign part URLs in sliding windows with an\n  expiry-skew re-sign, replacing the all-upfront 1h presign that could lapse\n  in the upload queue.\n- Failure isolation: Promise.allSettled so one file''s failure no longer\n  aborts its siblings; each file aborts only its own multipart upload.\n- Stall watchdog: per-part inactivity timer aborts+retries a half-open\n  socket; mandatory (a non-positive value falls back to the default) so it\n  can''t be disabled into a shared-permit deadlock.\n- Control-plane timeouts on create/sign/complete/abort.\n- Partial success surfaced via UploadJobError carrying the stored files; the\n  dialog refreshes the listing and reports \"N uploaded; the rest failed\"\n  instead of hiding stored siblings behind a total-failure message.\n\nTests: part retry, 403 re-sign, stall recovery, sibling-survives-failure,\nprogress-no-double-count, global-cap, user-cancel (AbortError + abort\ncleanup, cancel-wins-over-concurrent-error), and a standalone Semaphore\nsuite.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): leave /multipart/complete untimed (can take minutes)\n\nCompleteMultipartUpload stitches every part server-side and AWS documents\nit as potentially taking several minutes. The blanket 30s control-plane\ntimeout was also applied to /multipart/complete, so a large upload could be\nrejected AFTER all parts were uploaded, fall into the catch path, and fire\n/multipart/abort — destroying or racing an upload the backend was still\nfinalizing.\n\nScope the 30s timeout to the quick metadata calls (create/sign/abort) and\nleave /multipart/complete untimed (BFF handling + socket timeout are the\nbackstops); also keep the user signal off complete so a cancel can''t race\nthe finalize. Adds a regression test asserting complete carries no timeout\nwhile create/sign do.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJM8UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIK4QAHqkKjCoYFexMJ8nHvFfHune\nH3ZsZ6ZfBpRz3lIwz+Jpfp6MyoG8RVTT31X5LdeIKcS69qZq453mKHnxr7lq5Ecc\npZl43NkxWK0QcP8WR2muXlb6IillfpwQhdkvhIYkYrx6s6EbjpOC16xgosGR3Zbv\n13rNNH70/jokD+QujbXm3XMGuombfGoN2cFd42DfOt3LS3SI0JeKqb7QkeSXsb6S\nzFJKt70SYnEM3s4iCxYQAUZwV+X837m7fWRcSoEr26/gAausLLthXDU3ul/oMtxT\nIRZn07buoPSmB67b+zsVmQGXvy5oWzKlR7k99aKSvSDPL6UBKrXQnJNpS9Mi5/R0\nyMCehpOBXE6ig26KfBeT7E/isUpkb96wGekA6G3nOcB6fgGpx663Y+FNOCZRM4W4\njzobzTPwRAIthecJZVY56/w8xL+daW9AxfZPleFD00JPgPIdp2C213S+/502VRL9\ngfhmoNwdA1RnB3pqtFdNZoIYigLuXN2i9MYrrV1+oTX6LCX8LCzhDoj6yNwq0XK1\nuzyKh2uf1lkgjEbarf4WckeJVerUZNMzShnKcuFDfX4oz4+yOpLho+dzee8TvrcW\nQ/GJiSjM8LYLYcQeG/FkzjPUiMKXWNy/xz3LtWYIqOi90bPn7c4t4EnVSnXC/UO4\ndSAx0HkgD8uk4HUKWcqv\n=1DRg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T01:53:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDA4ZWRmZDYwYmVkYzM1MDI1MmU1NDhmMGU2NTJhZWJjMTE2ZjE3YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/e23b279ef4b70e0402dbc2cd7e5cf01c3770a5b0","sha":"e23b279ef4b70e0402dbc2cd7e5cf01c3770a5b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/e23b279ef4b70e0402dbc2cd7e5cf01c3770a5b0"}],"sha":"08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/08edfd60bedc350252e548f0e652aebc116f17ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/e23b279ef4b70e0402dbc2cd7e5cf01c3770a5b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T00:28:28Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T00:28:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: installable PWAs with transparent JWT token refresh (#32)\n\n* feat: add transparent JWT refresh-token flow\n\nReplace the single 1-day access token with a short-lived access token\n(15m) plus a long-lived refresh token (14d) — both stateless HS256 JWTs\ndistinguished by a `type` claim. The shared api-client refreshes\ntransparently on a 401 (single-flight + replay) and proactively before\nexpiry, so users (including an installed PWA) stay signed in without\nre-entering the password. Global sign-out = rotating JWT_SECRET.\n\n- server-config: createAuthRouter issues an access+refresh pair and adds\n  POST /auth/refresh; authenticateToken rejects non-access tokens.\n  ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL / REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL are optional env knobs.\n- web-shared api-client: refresh-on-401, proactive exp-based refresh,\n  and refresh-token storage helpers.\n- both apps: store/clear both tokens on login/logout; the embedded\n  FileBrowser hosts pass the access token reactively so a background\n  refresh propagates without a reload.\n\nPrereq for the PWA work (avoids the daily /login bounce on an installed\napp). Note: legacy typeless tokens are rejected, so deploying this forces\na one-time re-login.\n\n* feat: make both web apps installable PWAs\n\nAdd a Web App Manifest, a Module-Federation-aware service worker, and\nmaskable icons to the Admin Console (Vite) and S3 Browser (Rsbuild), so\nboth install to the home screen and run standalone with an app-shell\noffline fallback.\n\nThe service worker mirrors the BFFs'' Cache-Control discipline: hashed\n/assets and /static are cache-first; index.html, /api, /runtime-config.js\nand the MF entry files (remoteEntry.js, mf-manifest.json) are never\nprecached, so a stale SW can''t serve a version-skewed remote against the\nhost''s React singleton (\"Invalid hook call\"). It does not skipWaiting,\nand the S3 Browser registers it only from its standalone entry, so\nembedding the FileBrowser in the Admin host never double-registers.\n\n- icons: 192 / 512 / 512-maskable + a 180 apple-touch-icon per app,\n  rendered from each logo.svg on the brand background.\n- BFFs: serve sw.js + manifest.webmanifest no-store (so SW updates roll\n  out) with the correct application/manifest+json content type.\n- registration is prod-only so the dev servers'' HMR isn''t shadowed.\n\ntheme_color is the brand orange (#ff9429); background_color is #fffdfa.\n\n* docs: document PWA setup and token-TTL env vars\n\nAdd docs/pwa.md (manifests, the service-worker caching contract and its\nMF/\"Invalid hook call\" rationale, icon regeneration, install testing) and\nlist ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL / REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL in deployment.md.\n\n* fix(web-shared): recover from proactive token-refresh failures\n\nThe proactive refresh timer (and the no-recovery embedded FileBrowser\nthat relies on it) previously swallowed a failed /auth/refresh: tokens\nwere left in localStorage and subscribers weren''t notified, so a dead\nsession kept the user in the protected shell.\n\nClassify the failure. A rejected refresh token (4xx) is terminal — clear\nboth tokens and fire onUnauthorized so route guards flip to login. A\ntransient failure (offline, timeout, 5xx) keeps the tokens and\nreschedules a retry, so an installed PWA recovers on its own without a\nwrongful logout. The 401 interceptor passes the original request error to\nonUnauthorized so the Admin host''s proxy-skip policy still applies.\n\n* docs: add Chinese PWA doc and token TTLs in zh deployment\n\nAdd docs/pwa_zh.md (mirrors pwa.md), list ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL /\nREFRESH_TOKEN_TTL in deployment_zh.md, and cross-link the English/Chinese\nPWA docs.\n\n* chore(web): regenerate icons from 1024px sources, prune redundant assets\n\nAdd web/source/<app>-logo.svg (1024×1024 transparent masters) and render\nthe canonical icon set from them for both apps: the public *-logo.svg\n(UI logo + SVG favicon), favicon.ico (opaque 16/32/48), apple-touch-icon-180,\npwa-192/512 (any) and pwa-maskable-512 (maskable) — all rasters opaque on\n#fffdfa so the dark-element logos stay visible on dark surfaces.\n\nRemove unreferenced/redundant icons: the *-logo-{32,64,128}.png and\n*-logo.png raster sizes (admin + s3), plus the S3 Browser''s stale\napple-touch-icon.png and duplicate logo.svg. Verified none were referenced\nin src, html, configs, manifests, CSS, tests, or docs. Update the\nregeneration notes in docs/pwa.md + pwa_zh.md.","tree":{"sha":"862b48dcd3fea300533cd6523b8d647e05cc3a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/862b48dcd3fea300533cd6523b8d647e05cc3a4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/e23b279ef4b70e0402dbc2cd7e5cf01c3770a5b0","verification":{"payload":"tree 862b48dcd3fea300533cd6523b8d647e05cc3a4e\nparent 0a80fb45692412591534809f776ee87b3f7d0a13\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780792108 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780792108 +0800\n\nfeat: installable PWAs with transparent JWT token refresh (#32)\n\n* feat: add transparent JWT refresh-token flow\n\nReplace the single 1-day access token with a short-lived access token\n(15m) plus a long-lived refresh token (14d) — both stateless HS256 JWTs\ndistinguished by a `type` claim. The shared api-client refreshes\ntransparently on a 401 (single-flight + replay) and proactively before\nexpiry, so users (including an installed PWA) stay signed in without\nre-entering the password. Global sign-out = rotating JWT_SECRET.\n\n- server-config: createAuthRouter issues an access+refresh pair and adds\n  POST /auth/refresh; authenticateToken rejects non-access tokens.\n  ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL / REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL are optional env knobs.\n- web-shared api-client: refresh-on-401, proactive exp-based refresh,\n  and refresh-token storage helpers.\n- both apps: store/clear both tokens on login/logout; the embedded\n  FileBrowser hosts pass the access token reactively so a background\n  refresh propagates without a reload.\n\nPrereq for the PWA work (avoids the daily /login bounce on an installed\napp). Note: legacy typeless tokens are rejected, so deploying this forces\na one-time re-login.\n\n* feat: make both web apps installable PWAs\n\nAdd a Web App Manifest, a Module-Federation-aware service worker, and\nmaskable icons to the Admin Console (Vite) and S3 Browser (Rsbuild), so\nboth install to the home screen and run standalone with an app-shell\noffline fallback.\n\nThe service worker mirrors the BFFs'' Cache-Control discipline: hashed\n/assets and /static are cache-first; index.html, /api, /runtime-config.js\nand the MF entry files (remoteEntry.js, mf-manifest.json) are never\nprecached, so a stale SW can''t serve a version-skewed remote against the\nhost''s React singleton (\"Invalid hook call\"). It does not skipWaiting,\nand the S3 Browser registers it only from its standalone entry, so\nembedding the FileBrowser in the Admin host never double-registers.\n\n- icons: 192 / 512 / 512-maskable + a 180 apple-touch-icon per app,\n  rendered from each logo.svg on the brand background.\n- BFFs: serve sw.js + manifest.webmanifest no-store (so SW updates roll\n  out) with the correct application/manifest+json content type.\n- registration is prod-only so the dev servers'' HMR isn''t shadowed.\n\ntheme_color is the brand orange (#ff9429); background_color is #fffdfa.\n\n* docs: document PWA setup and token-TTL env vars\n\nAdd docs/pwa.md (manifests, the service-worker caching contract and its\nMF/\"Invalid hook call\" rationale, icon regeneration, install testing) and\nlist ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL / REFRESH_TOKEN_TTL in deployment.md.\n\n* fix(web-shared): recover from proactive token-refresh failures\n\nThe proactive refresh timer (and the no-recovery embedded FileBrowser\nthat relies on it) previously swallowed a failed /auth/refresh: tokens\nwere left in localStorage and subscribers weren''t notified, so a dead\nsession kept the user in the protected shell.\n\nClassify the failure. A rejected refresh token (4xx) is terminal — clear\nboth tokens and fire onUnauthorized so route guards flip to login. A\ntransient failure (offline, timeout, 5xx) keeps the tokens and\nreschedules a retry, so an installed PWA recovers on its own without a\nwrongful logout. The 401 interceptor passes the original request error to\nonUnauthorized so the Admin host''s proxy-skip policy still applies.\n\n* docs: add Chinese PWA doc and token TTLs in zh deployment\n\nAdd docs/pwa_zh.md (mirrors pwa.md), list ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL /\nREFRESH_TOKEN_TTL in deployment_zh.md, and cross-link the English/Chinese\nPWA docs.\n\n* chore(web): regenerate icons from 1024px sources, prune redundant assets\n\nAdd web/source/<app>-logo.svg (1024×1024 transparent masters) and render\nthe canonical icon set from them for both apps: the public *-logo.svg\n(UI logo + SVG favicon), favicon.ico (opaque 16/32/48), apple-touch-icon-180,\npwa-192/512 (any) and pwa-maskable-512 (maskable) — all rasters opaque on\n#fffdfa so the dark-element logos stay visible on dark surfaces.\n\nRemove unreferenced/redundant icons: the *-logo-{32,64,128}.png and\n*-logo.png raster sizes (admin + s3), plus the S3 Browser''s stale\napple-touch-icon.png and duplicate logo.svg. Verified none were referenced\nin src, html, configs, manifests, CSS, tests, or docs. Update the\nregeneration notes in docs/pwa.md + pwa_zh.md.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJLssCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASbwQADNCKwBToLnUi1E+7qhFf0Qd\n1SBQpg877fRP35TX2hJksUpDr+TEe3ZqwIP+DzIfLuutHHnFDuE7L0Avxbc3moVc\niiadjfdJrsqxQDTiXlwsnh