"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/0a80fb45692412591534809f776ee87b3f7d0a13","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKDBhODBmYjQ1NjkyNDEyNTkxNTM0ODA5Zjc3NmVlODdiM2Y3ZDBhMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/d3499a008217944763500748ee7fcce63c3ae82c","sha":"d3499a008217944763500748ee7fcce63c3ae82c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/d3499a008217944763500748ee7fcce63c3ae82c"}],"sha":"0a80fb45692412591534809f776ee87b3f7d0a13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/0a80fb45692412591534809f776ee87b3f7d0a13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/d3499a008217944763500748ee7fcce63c3ae82c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T05:33:32Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T05:33:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: support Garage v2.3.0 API fields with backward compatibility (#30)\n\n* feat: support Garage v2.3.0 API fields with backward compatibility\n\nAdd superset TypeScript types for all v2.3.0 additive nullable fields.\nNew fields render when present, gracefully absent for v2.2.0 clusters.\n\n- Node statistics: structured block manager + table stats panels\n  (falls back to freeform output for older nodes)\n- Layout manager: computation stats panel with zone/node breakdown,\n  shown in both overview and preview dialog\n- Bucket detail: read-only CORS rules, lifecycle rules, and routing\n  rules sections (hidden when null)\n- Replace single garage-admin-v2.json with versioned v2.2.0 + v2.3.0 specs\n\n* feat: cluster structured stats, bucket rule editors, dockerignore specs\n\n- ClusterOverview: surface structured stats (bucket count, object\n  count/size, data/metadata available) as a card grid when the v2.3.0\n  fields are present; incomplete-availability warning when nodes are\n  disconnected\n- BucketDetail: replace read-only CORS, lifecycle, and routing rule\n  displays with full CRUD editors (dialog forms with add/remove rules,\n  saved via UpdateBucket mutation)\n- Exclude OpenAPI spec JSON files from all three Docker images\n\n* fix: version-based rule visibility, collapsible CORS editor, collapsed freeform stats\n\n- Detect cluster version via node garageVersion instead of relying on\n  response field presence; CORS/lifecycle/routing sections appear for\n  all buckets on v2.3.0+ clusters\n- ClusterOverview: collapse freeform terminal output behind a <details>\n  when structured stats are present\n- CORS editor: rule cards are collapsible (<details> with origin/method\n  summary); optional fields (headers, expose headers, max age) nested\n  in a second collapsible; required fields marked with asterisk\n\n* fix: move routing rules into Website Access, lifecycle status toggle\n\nRouting rules are part of websiteConfig per the Garage API spec, not a\nstandalone bucket property. Move the editor into the Website Access\ndialog and remove the standalone section/dialog. Also replace the\nlifecycle rule Status dropdown with a Switch toggle for better\nvisibility, and add a Switch component to @garage/ui.\n\n* docs: clarify all-in-one s3 browser usage\n\n* fix: harden v2.3.0 version gating, routing rules editor, lifecycle filter\n\n- Parse pre-release suffixes (e.g. 2.3.0-rc1) in clusterMinVersion\n- Extract clusterMinVersion to its own module with 14 unit tests\n- Add missing ReplaceKeyWith field to website routing rules editor\n- Preserve lifecycle filter properties when clearing prefix\n- Remove no-op ternary in CORS/lifecycle save handlers\n- Fix capacityPct type inconsistency in LayoutManager","tree":{"sha":"4af98d5c50638aa38dc8cac814cc29dc12d22d95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/4af98d5c50638aa38dc8cac814cc29dc12d22d95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/d3499a008217944763500748ee7fcce63c3ae82c","verification":{"payload":"tree 4af98d5c50638aa38dc8cac814cc29dc12d22d95\nparent dbe63fb5cbf67ceff5dbd24c53e50dfd9b6bf863\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780724012 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780724012 +0800\n\nfeat: support Garage v2.3.0 API fields with backward compatibility (#30)\n\n* feat: support Garage v2.3.0 API fields with backward compatibility\n\nAdd superset TypeScript types for all v2.3.0 additive nullable fields.\nNew fields render when present, gracefully absent for v2.2.0 clusters.\n\n- Node statistics: structured block manager + table stats panels\n  (falls back to freeform output for older nodes)\n- Layout manager: computation stats panel with zone/node breakdown,\n  shown in both overview and preview dialog\n- Bucket detail: read-only CORS rules, lifecycle rules, and routing\n  rules sections (hidden when null)\n- Replace single garage-admin-v2.json with versioned v2.2.0 + v2.3.0 specs\n\n* feat: cluster structured stats, bucket rule editors, dockerignore specs\n\n- ClusterOverview: surface structured stats (bucket count, object\n  count/size, data/metadata available) as a card grid when the v2.3.0\n  fields are present; incomplete-availability warning when nodes are\n  disconnected\n- BucketDetail: replace read-only CORS, lifecycle, and routing rule\n  displays with full CRUD editors (dialog forms with add/remove rules,\n  saved via UpdateBucket mutation)\n- Exclude OpenAPI spec JSON files from all three Docker images\n\n* fix: version-based rule visibility, collapsible CORS editor, collapsed freeform stats\n\n- Detect cluster version via node garageVersion instead of relying on\n  response field presence; CORS/lifecycle/routing sections appear for\n  all buckets on v2.3.0+ clusters\n- ClusterOverview: collapse freeform terminal output behind a <details>\n  when structured stats are present\n- CORS editor: rule cards are collapsible (<details> with origin/method\n  summary); optional fields (headers, expose headers, max age) nested\n  in a second collapsible; required fields marked with asterisk\n\n* fix: move routing rules into Website Access, lifecycle status toggle\n\nRouting rules are part of websiteConfig per the Garage API spec, not a\nstandalone bucket property. Move the editor into the Website Access\ndialog and remove the standalone section/dialog. Also replace the\nlifecycle rule Status dropdown with a Switch toggle for better\nvisibility, and add a Switch component to @garage/ui.\n\n* docs: clarify all-in-one s3 browser usage\n\n* fix: harden v2.3.0 version gating, routing rules editor, lifecycle filter\n\n- Parse pre-release suffixes (e.g. 2.3.0-rc1) in clusterMinVersion\n- Extract clusterMinVersion to its own module with 14 unit tests\n- Add missing ReplaceKeyWith field to website routing rules editor\n- Preserve lifecycle filter properties when clearing prefix