,"sha":"c3de951bc75c46127c2d5632ce842fcb3d8c8fb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/c3de951bc75c46127c2d5632ce842fcb3d8c8fb5"}],"sha":"a2ca246aeadfbcdffee28ec94f4ea6c6c070e9a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/a2ca246aeadfbcdffee28ec94f4ea6c6c070e9a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/c3de951bc75c46127c2d5632ce842fcb3d8c8fb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T16:51:33Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T16:53:50Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"message":"fix(server-config): redact credentials from pino error logs\n\nAxiosError objects carry config.headers.Authorization (the decrypted\nadmin token) and AWS SDK errors can carry endpoint metadata. Pino''s\ndefault error serializer includes all enumerable properties, so any\n`logger.error({ err })` call leaked these secrets to log sinks.\n\nAdd a centralized safeErrorSerializer in createServiceLoggers that:\n- Redacts sensitive HTTP headers (Authorization, Cookie, etc.)\n- Redacts known secret property names (secretAccessKey, password, etc.)\n- Applies recursively (depth-capped at 8) to catch nested AxiosError\n  response.config.headers\n\nAlso hardens sanitizeForLog in garage-keys.ts to strip config.headers\nand response.config (defense-in-depth alongside the pino serializer).","tree":{"sha":"9b6ea553f5db86c5baba1801f86f7fda8c0290e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/9b6ea553f5db86c5baba1801f86f7fda8c0290e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/c3de951bc75c46127c2d5632ce842fcb3d8c8fb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/c3de951bc75c46127c2d5632ce842fcb3d8c8fb5","node_id":"C_kwDORZGCMtoAKGMzZGU5NTFiYzc1YzQ2MTI3YzJkNTYzMmNlODQyZmNiM2Q4YzhmYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commit/e5847859e6f80169518ebd4b77a5d3ca01ad07c7","sha":"e5847859e6f80169518ebd4b77a5d3ca01ad07c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/e5847859e6f80169518ebd4b77a5d3ca01ad07c7"}],"sha":"c3de951bc75c46127c2d5632ce842fcb3d8c8fb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/c3de951bc75c46127c2d5632ce842fcb3d8c8fb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48169104?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eyebrowkang","id":48169104,"login":"eyebrowkang","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MTY5MTA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eyebrowkang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/commits/e5847859e6f80169518ebd4b77a5d3ca01ad07c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T16:41:05Z","email":"me@eyebrowkang.com","name":"eyebrowkang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T16:41:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: UI/UX improve and init design docs\n\n* feat(web): cap desktop content at 80% width and default dashboards to grid\n\nThe app shells were max-w-full, which reads too wide on large desktops;\nconstrain the header/main/footer to max-w-[80%] in both products. Also flip\nthe shared useViewMode default to the card grid so both fleet dashboards open\nin grid view (a stored preference still wins).\n\n* fix(dashboard): size Min zone capacity per zone, drop duplicate nodes-online text\n\nMin zone capacity compared raw per-node capacities, understating a zone whose\ncapacity is spread over several nodes. Group nodes by zone, sum each zone''s\ncapacity, then take the smallest zone — Garage''s usable capacity is bounded by\nits smallest zone. Extracted buildZoneStats/zonesByCapacity so the pressure\nmeter reuses the same grouping. Also drop the \"N/N nodes online\" status line on\nthe dashboard card; the Nodes tile above already shows that exact ratio.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): drop redundant \"N buckets accessible\" copy from connection cards\n\nThe bucket count is already shown in the Buckets metric tile; the prose line\njust repeated it. Remove it and only render the status separator when a\npreceding status message (unreachable/checking) is present.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): keep the upload dialog from overflowing on long filenames\n\nA long filename widened the whole dialog and forced horizontal scrolling.\nDialogContent is a grid, so its content wrapper inherited min-width:auto and\nrefused to shrink below the filename''s intrinsic width — defeating the row''s\ntruncate. Add min-w-0 to the wrapper (and the filename span) so the name\nellipsizes and the dialog stays at its max width.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): shrink the file-list border to its content height\n\nThe bordered list card used flex-1, so its border stretched to the full\navailable height even with only a few rows, leaving a large empty boxed area.\nUse max-h-full instead: the card now hugs its content when short and still caps\n+ scrolls when the list is long.\n\n* feat(web): remove the Metrics page; keep /metrics as a raw pass-through proxy\n\nThere is no longer a frontend Metrics page or sidebar entry. Prometheus metrics\nremain available as a deliberate raw pass-through at\n`GET /api/proxy/:clusterId/metrics` (using the cluster''s optional metric token),\nintended for scrapers / curl rather than a rendered UI.\n\n- web: drop the Metrics nav item, its lazy route, and MetricsPage.tsx\n  (plus the now-unused Suspense/LazyFallback/PageLoadingState wiring).\n- api: document the /metrics pass-through intent in proxy.ts; metric-token\n  handling is unchanged.\n- docs: record the decision in architecture.md so it isn''t read as a gap.\n\n* feat(web): add a domain check action to the cluster Overview\n\nAdds a \"Check Domain\" button + dialog on the cluster Overview that calls\nGarage''s `/check` special endpoint (proxied) to answer whether a website-enabled\nbucket in this cluster serves a given domain — a previously-missing convenience.\nHTTP 200 = served, 400 = not served (both treated as valid answers via\nvalidateStatus); other statuses surface as an error. Verified against a live\nGarage v2 cluster (400 for an unconfigured domain, with and without a token).\n\n* fix(web): keep deep client routes containing dots from 404ing on refresh\n\nBoth BFFs'' SPA fallback gated index.html on `!path.extname(req.path)`, so any\nclient route whose last segment contained a dot — a bucket named\n\"my.bucket.com\", or an s3-browser object-key route like\n/connections/:id/b/:bucket/report.pdf — was treated as a static asset, skipped\nthe fallback, and 404''d to a white screen on refresh.\n\nServe index.html for browser navigations regardless of dots, excluding only\nreal asset locations so genuinely-missing files still 404 (not masked as HTML):\n- admin: exclude /api, /assets (Vite), and /s3-browser (the federated remote).\n- s3-browser: exclude /api, /static (Rsbuild), and the MF entry files.\n\nVerified against a production build: /clusters/x/buckets/my.bucket.com now\nreturns 200 + index.html, while /assets/missing.js and unknown /api paths 404.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): redirect to login when standalone credentials expire\n\nA 401 cleared the stored token (onUnauthorized) but ProtectedShell read it only\nonce at render, so an expired session left the user stranded on the dashboard\ninstead of returning to /login.\n\nMake the token reactive: createApiClient now exposes a `subscribe` that\nwriteStoredToken notifies, and the standalone app reads it through a\n`useAuthToken()` hook (useSyncExternalStore). When a 401 clears the token the\nguard re-renders and routes to /login — a render flag, not a hard reload, so\nembedded (federated) mode is unaffected (it never uses this shell or client).\n\nVerified in the dev server: no token → /login, valid token → dashboard, no\nerrors; unit tests cover subscribe/notify incl. the 401-clears-token path.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): make >10MB downloads work on mobile (same-tab, not a new tab)\n\nThe large-file path presigns then triggered the download via an anchor with\ntarget=\"_blank\". That new tab is opened *after* the awaited /presign call, so\nmobile Safari/Chrome popup-block it (no longer tied to the tap gesture) and the\ndownload silently did nothing. Drop target=\"_blank\": the presigned URL already\ncarries Content-Disposition: attachment, so a same-tab top-level navigation\ndownloads the file without navigating away and is never popup-blocked. (Small\nfiles already used a same-tab blob download.)\n\n* refactor(ui): extract FloatingActionBar from ResourceList\n\nPull the fixed/floating selection-action pill out of ResourceList into a\nstandalone, reusable @garage/ui component so the S3 Browser can share the exact\nsame bar. Pure refactor — ResourceList renders identical markup and behaviour.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): float the multi-select bar so it no longer shifts the layout\n\nThe BulkBar rendered in-flow above the list, so toggling multi-select pushed\nthe whole list down and back (visible jank). Render it through the shared\n@garage/ui FloatingActionBar instead — the same floating pill the admin\nResourceList uses — so it overlays the viewport and slides in/out without\nreflowing anything. Actions (select-all, download, copy keys, delete, exit) are\nunchanged. Verified in the playground: entering multi-select no longer moves the\nlist; the pill shows \"N of N selected\" with working actions.\n\n* fix(web): only cap content width on desktop, keep mobile full-width\n\nThe 80% width cap was applied unconditionally, so it also squeezed mobile\n(wasting phone screen space). Make it responsive — full width below md, 80% at\nmd+ (the app''s own desktop breakpoint). Verified: mobile 375px → full width,\ndesktop → ~80%.\n\n* fix(dashboard): show no status line for a healthy cluster\n\nThe previous change swapped the removed \"N/N nodes online\" for \"All checks\npassing\", but the ask was to remove the copy, not replace it. Healthy clusters\nnow render no status text at all; the card shows just \"Min zone capacity\", and\nthe separator only appears when a non-healthy status message precedes it.\n\n* feat(api): serve raw cluster metrics at /clusters/:id/metrics (public passthrough)\n\nRemoving the Metrics page also dropped its route, so navigating to a cluster''s\nmetrics URL hit the SPA fallback and returned a blank app instead of metrics.\nAdd a dedicated, browser-navigable passthrough that proxies the cluster''s Garage\n/metrics as raw text/plain, registered before the SPA fallback.\n\nIt is intentionally UNAUTHENTICATED: a browser / Prometheus scraper can''t carry\nthe console JWT, so the route uses the cluster''s stored read-only metric token\nserver-side (per the agreed \"完全透传\" design). Trade-off documented in\nroutes/metrics.ts + architecture.md. Verified against a live v2 cluster: returns\n200 text/plain Prometheus, while /clusters/:id/buckets/... still serves the SPA.\n\n* refactor(api): drop the cluster /metrics passthrough (no metrics UI planned)\n\nThere is no Metrics page and no plan to wire one up for now, so the dedicated\nraw-passthrough route added in 6e480c0 is unnecessary. Remove it along with the\nolder `/metrics` special-casing inside the generic proxy:\n\n- delete routes/metrics.ts and its registration/import in app.ts\n- proxy.ts now always uses the admin token (drop the metricToken branch)\n- update architecture.md and strip the related comments\n\nThe optional, encrypted `metricToken` credential (DB column + cluster form) is\nintentionally kept for a future integration; nothing reads it today.\n\n* feat(web): optimize cluster form — collapsible advanced, complete S3 fields\n\nRestructure the Connect/Edit Garage Cluster dialog form:\n\n- Add missing S3 Region and Force Path-style fields (were in the backend\n  schema and ClusterSummary type but absent from the form)\n- Fold optional fields (Metric Token, S3 configuration) into a collapsible\n  \"Advanced\" section so the primary form stays clean\n- Conditionally show the S3 Object Storage section only when Module\n  Federation is explicitly configured (isMfExplicitlyConfigured), since S3\n  credentials are only used by the embedded FileBrowser\n- Advanced auto-opens in edit mode when the cluster already has S3 values\n\n* docs: impeccable init and document\n\n* fix(tokens): align primaryForeground with CSS","tree":{"sha":"646006a32e4ad6414e6ddb12789e10f6795fae4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/trees/646006a32e4ad6414e6ddb12789e10f6795fae4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eyebrowkang/garage-admin-console/git/commits/e5847859e6f80169518ebd4b77a5d3ca01ad07c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 646006a32e4ad6414e6ddb12789e10f6795fae4c\nparent 49549d10de580f6d25bbbfe857bb78176ee6d7e1\nauthor eyebrowkang <me@eyebrowkang.com> 1780677665 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780677665 +0800\n\nfeat: UI/UX improve and init design docs\n\n* feat(web): cap desktop content at 80% width and default dashboards to grid\n\nThe app shells were max-w-full, which reads too wide on large desktops;\nconstrain the header/main/footer to max-w-[80%] in both products. Also flip\nthe shared useViewMode default to the card grid so both fleet dashboards open\nin grid view (a stored preference still wins).\n\n* fix(dashboard): size Min zone capacity per zone, drop duplicate nodes-online text\n\nMin zone capacity compared raw per-node capacities, understating a zone whose\ncapacity is spread over several nodes. Group nodes by zone, sum each zone''s\ncapacity, then take the smallest zone — Garage''s usable capacity is bounded by\nits smallest zone. Extracted buildZoneStats/zonesByCapacity so the pressure\nmeter reuses the same grouping. Also drop the \"N/N nodes online\" status line on\nthe dashboard card; the Nodes tile above already shows that exact ratio.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): drop redundant \"N buckets accessible\" copy from connection cards\n\nThe bucket count is already shown in the Buckets metric tile; the prose line\njust repeated it. Remove it and only render the status separator when a\npreceding status message (unreachable/checking) is present.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): keep the upload dialog from overflowing on long filenames\n\nA long filename widened the whole dialog and forced horizontal scrolling.\nDialogContent is a grid, so its content wrapper inherited min-width:auto and\nrefused to shrink below the filename''s intrinsic width — defeating the row''s\ntruncate. Add min-w-0 to the wrapper (and the filename span) so the name\nellipsizes and the dialog stays at its max width.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): shrink the file-list border to its content height\n\nThe bordered list card used flex-1, so its border stretched to the full\navailable height even with only a few rows, leaving a large empty boxed area.\nUse max-h-full instead: the card now hugs its content when short and still caps\n+ scrolls when the list is long.\n\n* feat(web): remove the Metrics page; keep /metrics as a raw pass-through proxy\n\nThere is no longer a frontend Metrics page or sidebar entry. Prometheus metrics\nremain available as a deliberate raw pass-through at\n`GET /api/proxy/:clusterId/metrics` (using the cluster''s optional metric token),\nintended for scrapers / curl rather than a rendered UI.\n\n- web: drop the Metrics nav item, its lazy route, and MetricsPage.tsx\n  (plus the now-unused Suspense/LazyFallback/PageLoadingState wiring).\n- api: document the /metrics pass-through intent in proxy.ts; metric-token\n  handling is unchanged.\n- docs: record the decision in architecture.md so it isn''t read as a gap.\n\n* feat(web): add a domain check action to the cluster Overview\n\nAdds a \"Check Domain\" button + dialog on the cluster Overview that calls\nGarage''s `/check` special endpoint (proxied) to answer whether a website-enabled\nbucket in this cluster serves a given domain — a previously-missing convenience.\nHTTP 200 = served, 400 = not served (both treated as valid answers via\nvalidateStatus); other statuses surface as an error. Verified against a live\nGarage v2 cluster (400 for an unconfigured domain, with and without a token).\n\n* fix(web): keep deep client routes containing dots from 404ing on refresh\n\nBoth BFFs'' SPA fallback gated index.html on `!path.extname(req.path)`, so any\nclient route whose last segment contained a dot — a bucket named\n\"my.bucket.com\", or an s3-browser object-key route like\n/connections/:id/b/:bucket/report.pdf — was treated as a static asset, skipped\nthe fallback, and 404''d to a white screen on refresh.\n\nServe index.html for browser navigations regardless of dots, excluding only\nreal asset locations so genuinely-missing files still 404 (not masked as HTML):\n- admin: exclude /api, /assets (Vite), and /s3-browser (the federated remote).\n- s3-browser: exclude /api, /static (Rsbuild), and the MF entry files.\n\nVerified against a production build: /clusters/x/buckets/my.bucket.com now\nreturns 200 + index.html, while /assets/missing.js and unknown /api paths 404.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): redirect to login when standalone credentials expire\n\nA 401 cleared the stored token (onUnauthorized) but ProtectedShell read it only\nonce at render, so an expired session left the user stranded on the dashboard\ninstead of returning to /login.\n\nMake the token reactive: createApiClient now exposes a `subscribe` that\nwriteStoredToken notifies, and the standalone app reads it through a\n`useAuthToken()` hook (useSyncExternalStore). When a 401 clears the token the\nguard re-renders and routes to /login — a render flag, not a hard reload, so\nembedded (federated) mode is unaffected (it never uses this shell or client).\n\nVerified in the dev server: no token → /login, valid token → dashboard, no\nerrors; unit tests cover subscribe/notify incl. the 401-clears-token path.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): make >10MB downloads work on mobile (same-tab, not a new tab)\n\nThe large-file path presigns then triggered the download via an anchor with\ntarget=\"_blank\". That new tab is opened *after* the awaited /presign call, so\nmobile Safari/Chrome popup-block it (no longer tied to the tap gesture) and the\ndownload silently did nothing. Drop target=\"_blank\": the presigned URL already\ncarries Content-Disposition: attachment, so a same-tab top-level navigation\ndownloads the file without navigating away and is never popup-blocked. (Small\nfiles already used a same-tab blob download.)\n\n* refactor(ui): extract FloatingActionBar from ResourceList\n\nPull the fixed/floating selection-action pill out of ResourceList into a\nstandalone, reusable @garage/ui component so the S3 Browser can share the exact\nsame bar. Pure refactor — ResourceList renders identical markup and behaviour.\n\n* fix(s3-browser): float the multi-select bar so it no longer shifts the layout\n\nThe BulkBar rendered in-flow above the list, so toggling multi-select pushed\nthe whole list down and back (visible jank). Render it through the shared\n@garage/ui FloatingActionBar instead — the same floating pill the admin\nResourceList uses — so it overlays the viewport and slides in/out without\nreflowing anything. Actions (select-all, download, copy keys, delete, exit) are\nunchanged. Verified in the playground: entering multi-select no longer moves the\nlist; the pill shows \"N of N selected\" with working actions.\n\n* fix(web): only cap content width on desktop, keep mobile full-width\n\nThe 80% width cap was applied unconditionally, so it also squeezed mobile\n(wasting phone screen space). Make it responsive — full width below md, 80% at\nmd+ (the app''s own desktop breakpoint). Verified: mobile 375px → full width,\ndesktop → ~80%.\n\n* fix(dashboard): show no status line for a healthy cluster\n\nThe previous change swapped the removed \"N/N nodes online\" for \"All checks\npassing\", but the ask was to remove the copy, not replace it. Healthy clusters\nnow render no status text at all; the card shows just \"Min zone capacity\", and\nthe separator only appears when a non-healthy status message precedes it.\n\n* feat(api): serve raw cluster metrics at /clusters/:id/metrics (public passthrough)\n\nRemoving the Metrics page also dropped its route, so navigating to a cluster''s\nmetrics URL hit the SPA fallback and returned a blank app instead of metrics.\nAdd a dedicated, browser-navigable passthrough that proxies the cluster''s Garage\n/metrics as raw text/plain, registered before the SPA fallback.\n\nIt is intentionally UNAUTHENTICATED: a browser / Prometheus scraper can''t carry\nthe console JWT, so the route uses the cluster''s stored read-only metric token\nserver-side (per the agreed \"完全透传\" design). Trade-off documented in\nroutes/metrics.ts + architecture.md. Verified against a live v2 cluster: returns\n200 text/plain Prometheus, while /clusters/:id/buckets/... still serves the SPA.\n\n* refactor(api): drop the cluster /metrics passthrough (no metrics UI planned)\n\nThere is no Metrics page and no plan to wire one up for now, so the dedicated\nraw-passthrough route added in 6e480c0 is unnecessary. Remove it along with the\nolder `/metrics` special-casing inside the generic proxy:\n\n- delete routes/metrics.ts and its registration/import in app.ts\n- proxy.ts now always uses the admin token (drop the metricToken branch)\n- update architecture.md and strip the related comments\n\nThe optional, encrypted `metricToken` credential (DB column + cluster form) is\nintentionally kept for a future integration; nothing reads it today.\n\n* feat(web): optimize cluster form — collapsible advanced, complete S3 fields\n\nRestructure the Connect/Edit Garage Cluster dialog form:\n\n- Add missing S3 Region and Force Path-style fields (were in the backend\n  schema and ClusterSummary type but absent from the form)\n- Fold optional fields (Metric Token, S3 configuration) into a collapsible\n  \"Advanced\" section so the primary form stays clean\n- Conditionally show the S3 Object Storage section only when Module\n  Federation is explicitly configured (isMfExplicitlyConfigured), since S3\n  credentials are only used by the embedded FileBrowser\n- Advanced auto-opens in edit mode when the cluster already has S3 values\n\n* docs: impeccable init and document\n\n* fix(tokens): align primaryForeground with CSS","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIvwhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5FEQAEm0XxG0HdeUYsl1Caq4Q0Ia\nRTc2MTrLLQFS3kLxnkLy2kML89ofDKWE4vnwWf0ZL9cq/m4xNoCx7hMceX32Gqr8\n8bMWdNUmGGP3qnjkO+sYJcnWmKzlF/PRu7BbgB+yoCBABreSrvaYkxOTef+iZqkj\nyUSWOZPBmbZ/w7KHjH8qStdIE5LznoaHCIBZY7PeYhMSmbUOmrfiYC+hxMOPKRPK\n3O419lVq6k/lT/wki8LBO1MjeeYevO/vRvwekYv/rA15VWykgwyBvZ8off6TF4BN\nsehsfw3BGrDMjHnGm/JaXeJVHk0bcLyEWdeNpQ3nPmK6xbMZRWRjV/0xxfNknKnv\nbqM8MEstef6Dqs2/EfpkCF6ioD6/LpqNY2CnPQ2yHgozjNRNndDfNE+WMH0hdF04\n2OJCECbx5VceUppKGv1Ci7wByjkNH5FCwztHaRF85vfOfHg3THYXBeSBgnTSFI+n\nhMXx0r0md96FSGoQaiGVgWWS+x6buPoBgN//HklNRpGbPkhFP4sitMS53YQ37uRI\nZhgax+naFABo3lne8CAVkkPS6Qp1yzwk8jDx3U9lzVC3KJkvS7h8W8k+WiUVVi0o\nWBicm+B/WRsE94s/ZOmZ4uKbKDdvYn9WQwcsp9